searchData={"items":[{"type":"module","title":"Operator","doc":"Operator - A pluggable AI planning and narrative orchestration library.\n\nOperator provides two main subsystems for building intelligent agents and\ndynamic narrative systems:\n\n* **HTN Planning** - Goal-based hierarchical task decomposition\n* **Director** - Event-driven narrative orchestration","ref":"Operator.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Quick Start - Operator","doc":"","ref":"Operator.html#module-quick-start"},{"type":"module","title":"1. Define Agent Behaviors - Operator","doc":"Use the DSL to define goals, tasks, and primitives:\n\n    defmodule MyGame.NPCBehavior do\n      use Operator.HTN.DSL\n\n      goal :patrol do\n        precond fn facts ->\n          Operator.HTN.Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :on_duty})\n        end\n\n        decompose do\n          task :walk_to_waypoint, :next\n          task :scan_area\n          task :patrol  # Recursive!\n        end\n\n        metadata priority: 3, domain: :security\n      end\n\n      primitive :scan_area do\n        run fn actor, _facts ->\n          # Your game logic here\n          {:ok, %{actor | scanning: true}}\n        end\n      end\n    end","ref":"Operator.html#module-1-define-agent-behaviors"},{"type":"module","title":"2. Generate Plans - Operator","doc":"facts = Operator.HTN.Facts.from_perception(%{\n      self: %{on_duty: true, location: :lobby},\n      world: %{threat_level: :low}\n    })\n\n    case Operator.HTN.Planner.run(:patrol, facts, agent_traits) do\n      {:ok, plan} ->\n        # plan.tasks contains executable primitives\n        execute_plan(plan)\n\n      {:error, reason} ->\n        handle_planning_failure(reason)\n    end","ref":"Operator.html#module-2-generate-plans"},{"type":"module","title":"3. Orchestrate Narrative Events - Operator","doc":"defmodule MyGame.DramaticStoryteller do\n      @behaviour Operator.Storyteller\n\n      @impl true\n      def init(_opts), do: %{tension: 0.0}\n\n      @impl true\n      def pick_event(tick, world_state, state) do\n        if world_state.tension > 0.8 do\n          event = %{type: :confrontation, severity: :high}\n          {event, %{state | tension: 0.0}}\n        else\n          {nil, state}\n        end\n      end\n    end\n\n    {:ok, _pid} = Operator.Director.start_link(\n      storyteller: MyGame.DramaticStoryteller,\n      on_event: &MyGame.EventHandler.process/1\n    )","ref":"Operator.html#module-3-orchestrate-narrative-events"},{"type":"module","title":"Architecture Overview - Operator","doc":"```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                      Operator Library                        │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  HTN Planning                   │  Director                  │\n│  ├─ Facts (world state)         │  ├─ Storyteller behaviour  │\n│  ├─ Goals (high-level)          │  ├─ Tick-based events      │\n│  ├─ Tasks (decomposable)        │  └─ World state queries    │\n│  ├─ Primitives (executable)     │                            │\n│  ├─ Effects (state changes)     │                            │\n│  └─ Axioms (reusable queries)   │                            │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  Integration Behaviours                                      │\n│  ├─ Telemetry  - Metrics and observability                  │\n│  ├─ Traits     - Agent personality/capabilities             │\n│  ├─ Storage    - Plan persistence                           │\n│  └─ Rationalization - Plan annotation/explanation           │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```","ref":"Operator.html#module-architecture-overview"},{"type":"module","title":"Module Index - Operator","doc":"","ref":"Operator.html#module-module-index"},{"type":"module","title":"HTN Planning - Operator","doc":"* `Operator.HTN.DSL` - Macro-based goal/task definition\n* `Operator.HTN.Facts` - World state representation\n* `Operator.HTN.Plan` - Generated plan structure\n* `Operator.HTN.Task` - Task definition struct\n* `Operator.HTN.Effect` - World state modifications\n* `Operator.HTN.Axiom` - Reusable query patterns\n* `Operator.HTN.Precondition` - Logical operators (AND/OR/NOT)\n* `Operator.HTN.Engine` - Plan generation algorithm\n* `Operator.HTN.Planner` - High-level planning API\n* `Operator.HTN.GoalSelector` - Automatic goal selection\n* `Operator.HTN.Registry` - Goal/task lookup\n* `Operator.HTN.Trace` - Debug tracing","ref":"Operator.html#module-htn-planning"},{"type":"module","title":"Director - Operator","doc":"* `Operator.Director` - Event orchestration GenServer\n* `Operator.Storyteller` - Event generation behaviour","ref":"Operator.html#module-director"},{"type":"module","title":"Integration Behaviours - Operator","doc":"* `Operator.Telemetry` - Metrics callbacks\n* `Operator.Traits` - Agent trait integration\n* `Operator.Storage` - Plan persistence\n* `Operator.Rationalization` - Plan annotation","ref":"Operator.html#module-integration-behaviours"},{"type":"module","title":"Configuration - Operator","doc":"All configuration is optional. Operator works out of the box with sensible\ndefaults:\n\n    # config/config.exs\n    config :operator,\n      # Emit telemetry events for monitoring\n      telemetry_module: MyApp.OperatorTelemetry,\n\n      # Custom agent trait system integration\n      traits_module: MyApp.OperatorTraits,\n\n      # Plan storage backend (default: ETS)\n      storage_module: Operator.HTN.Storage,\n\n      # Plan explanation/annotation\n      rationalization_module: MyApp.OperatorRationalization,\n\n      # Enable detailed planning traces\n      trace_handler: Operator.HTN.Trace.ConsoleHandler","ref":"Operator.html#module-configuration"},{"type":"module","title":"Use Cases - Operator","doc":"Operator is designed for:\n\n* **Game AI** - NPC behaviors, enemy tactics, companion AI\n* **Simulation** - Agent-based modeling, emergent behavior\n* **Robotics** - Task planning, goal-directed behavior\n* **Workflow Automation** - Complex multi-step processes\n* **Chatbots** - Conversation flow management","ref":"Operator.html#module-use-cases"},{"type":"module","title":"Resources - Operator","doc":"* [GameAIPro HTN Chapter](https://www.gameaipro.com/GameAIPro/GameAIPro_Chapter12_Exploring_HTN_Planners_through_Example.pdf) - Theory background\n* [Hex Documentation](https://hexdocs.pm/operator) - API reference\n* [Examples](https://github.com/yourorg/operator/tree/main/examples) - Sample applications","ref":"Operator.html#module-resources"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.version/0","doc":"Returns the Operator library version.","ref":"Operator.html#version/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.version/0","doc":"iex> Operator.version()\n    \"0.1.0\"","ref":"Operator.html#version/0-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.Director","doc":"Narrative orchestration system for dynamic event generation.\n\nThe Director is a GenServer that acts as your game's \"AI Director\" (inspired\nby Left 4 Dead's famous system). It monitors world state and decides when\ninteresting events should occur, controlling narrative pacing and dramatic\ntension.","ref":"Operator.Director.html"},{"type":"module","title":"The Director Pattern - Operator.Director","doc":"```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        Game Loop                                 │\n│   ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐       │\n│   │ Update NPCs │ --> │ Physics/AI  │ --> │ Render      │       │\n│   └─────────────┘     └─────────────┘     └─────────────┘       │\n│         │                                                        │\n│         │ world_state                                            │\n│         ▼                                                        │\n│   ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐                       │\n│   │           Director                  │                       │\n│   │  ┌─────────────────────────────┐    │                       │\n│   │  │      Storyteller            │    │     ┌──────────────┐  │\n│   │  │  - monitors tension         │----│---> │ Game Events  │  │\n│   │  │  - picks event timing       │    │     │ (spawn enemy,│  │\n│   │  │  - controls pacing          │    │     │  trigger     │  │\n│   │  └─────────────────────────────┘    │     │  dialogue)   │  │\n│   └─────────────────────────────────────┘     └──────────────┘  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```","ref":"Operator.Director.html#module-the-director-pattern"},{"type":"module","title":"Quick Start - Operator.Director","doc":"# 1. Define your storyteller\n    defmodule MyGame.TensionStoryteller do\n      @behaviour Operator.Storyteller\n\n      @impl true\n      def init(_opts), do: %{last_event_tick: 0}\n\n      @impl true\n      def pick_event(tick, world_state, state) do\n        tension = Map.get(world_state, :tension, 0.0)\n\n        if tension > 0.7 and tick - state.last_event_tick > 100 do\n          event = %{type: :ambush, location: pick_location(world_state)}\n          {event, %{state | last_event_tick: tick}}\n        else\n          {nil, state}\n        end\n      end\n    end\n\n    # 2. Start the Director\n    {:ok, _pid} = Operator.Director.start_link(\n      storyteller: MyGame.TensionStoryteller,\n      on_event: &MyGame.EventHandler.process/1\n    )\n\n    # 3. Feed it world state each tick\n    def game_tick(world_state) do\n      Operator.Director.tick(world_state)\n      # ... rest of game loop\n    end","ref":"Operator.Director.html#module-quick-start"},{"type":"module","title":"Startup Options - Operator.Director","doc":"* `:storyteller` - Module implementing `Operator.Storyteller`\n  (default: `NullStoryteller`)\n* `:name` - GenServer name (default: `Operator.Director`)\n* `:on_event` - Callback `fn event -> :ok end` for generated events","ref":"Operator.Director.html#module-startup-options"},{"type":"module","title":"Event Flow - Operator.Director","doc":"1. Your game calls `Director.tick(world_state)` each simulation tick\n2. Director invokes `storyteller.pick_event(tick, world_state, state)`\n3. If the storyteller returns an event, Director:\n   - Rationalizes it via `Operator.Rationalization`\n   - Emits telemetry via `Operator.Telemetry`\n   - Calls your `:on_event` callback\n4. Your game reacts to the event (spawn enemies, trigger dialogue, etc.)","ref":"Operator.Director.html#module-event-flow"},{"type":"module","title":"Runtime Control - Operator.Director","doc":"# Change storytellers based on game phase\n    Operator.Director.change_storyteller(MyGame.BossFightStoryteller)\n\n    # Get current tick for synchronization\n    current_tick = Operator.Director.current_tick()\n\n    # Debug storyteller state\n    state = Operator.Director.get_state()","ref":"Operator.Director.html#module-runtime-control"},{"type":"module","title":"Integration Philosophy - Operator.Director","doc":"The Director is intentionally lightweight. It does NOT:\n\n* Subscribe to PubSub topics\n* Persist events to timelines\n* Handle clustering\n\nThese concerns belong to your host application. The Director's job is\npurely to decide **when** and **what** events to generate.","ref":"Operator.Director.html#module-integration-philosophy"},{"type":"module","title":"Synchronous Testing - Operator.Director","doc":"For tests, use `tick_sync/2` to get immediate results:\n\n    event = Operator.Director.tick_sync(world_state)\n    assert event.type == :ambush","ref":"Operator.Director.html#module-synchronous-testing"},{"type":"module","title":"See Also - Operator.Director","doc":"* `Operator.Storyteller` - Behaviour for storyteller modules\n* `Operator.Director.NullStoryteller` - No-op storyteller for testing\n* `Operator.Rationalization` - Event annotation","ref":"Operator.Director.html#module-see-also"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.Director.storyteller_state/0","doc":"","ref":"Operator.Director.html#t:storyteller_state/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.Director.t/0","doc":"","ref":"Operator.Director.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Director.change_storyteller/2","doc":"Change the active storyteller at runtime.","ref":"Operator.Director.html#change_storyteller/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Director.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"Operator.Director.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Director.current_tick/1","doc":"Get the current tick.","ref":"Operator.Director.html#current_tick/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Director.get_state/1","doc":"Get the current state (for debugging).","ref":"Operator.Director.html#get_state/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Director.start_link/1","doc":"Start the Director.","ref":"Operator.Director.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - Operator.Director.start_link/1","doc":"- `:storyteller` - Storyteller module (default: NullStoryteller)\n- `:name` - GenServer name (default: Operator.Director)\n- `:on_event` - Callback for generated events","ref":"Operator.Director.html#start_link/1-options"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Director.tick/2","doc":"Trigger a tick with the given world state.\n\nCall this from your simulation's tick handler.","ref":"Operator.Director.html#tick/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Director.tick_sync/2","doc":"Synchronous tick that returns any generated event.\n\nUseful for testing.","ref":"Operator.Director.html#tick_sync/2"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.Director.NullStoryteller","doc":"A storyteller that never generates events.\n\nThe NullStoryteller is a no-op implementation of the `Operator.Storyteller`\nbehaviour. It's the narrative equivalent of `/dev/null` - events go in,\nnothing comes out.","ref":"Operator.Director.NullStoryteller.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Use Cases - Operator.Director.NullStoryteller","doc":"**Testing:** When you want to test Director integration without event noise:\n\n    {:ok, _pid} = Director.start_link(\n      storyteller: Operator.Director.NullStoryteller,\n      on_event: fn event -> flunk(\"Should not fire: #{inspect(event)}\") end\n    )\n\n**Baseline Performance:** Measure your game loop overhead without storyteller\nprocessing:\n\n    # Compare tick times with NullStoryteller vs your real storyteller\n    {:ok, _} = Director.start_link(storyteller: NullStoryteller)\n\n**Gradual Integration:** Start with NullStoryteller while building your game,\nthen swap in a real storyteller when you're ready for narrative events:\n\n    storyteller = if Mix.env() == :dev do\n      Operator.Director.NullStoryteller\n    else\n      MyGame.DramaticStoryteller\n    end\n\n    Director.start_link(storyteller: storyteller, on_event: &handle/1)\n\n**Disabling Events:** Temporarily disable event generation without stopping\nthe Director:\n\n    # In your config/runtime.exs\n    config :my_game, :storyteller,\n      if System.get_env(\"DISABLE_EVENTS\"),\n        do: Operator.Director.NullStoryteller,\n        else: MyGame.Storyteller","ref":"Operator.Director.NullStoryteller.html#module-use-cases"},{"type":"module","title":"Behaviour - Operator.Director.NullStoryteller","doc":"* `init/1` - Returns empty state `%{}`\n* `pick_event/3` - Always returns `{nil, state}` (no event)","ref":"Operator.Director.NullStoryteller.html#module-behaviour"},{"type":"module","title":"See Also - Operator.Director.NullStoryteller","doc":"* `Operator.Storyteller` - The behaviour this implements\n* `Operator.Director` - The GenServer that calls this","ref":"Operator.Director.NullStoryteller.html#module-see-also"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Director.NullStoryteller.init/1","doc":"Initialize with empty state.\n\nIgnores all options since NullStoryteller has no configuration.","ref":"Operator.Director.NullStoryteller.html#init/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.Director.NullStoryteller.init/1","doc":"* `_opts` - Ignored","ref":"Operator.Director.NullStoryteller.html#init/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.Director.NullStoryteller.init/1","doc":"Empty map `%{}`","ref":"Operator.Director.NullStoryteller.html#init/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Director.NullStoryteller.pick_event/3","doc":"Never generate an event.\n\nAlways returns `{nil, state}` regardless of tick or world state.","ref":"Operator.Director.NullStoryteller.html#pick_event/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.Director.NullStoryteller.pick_event/3","doc":"* `_tick` - Current game tick (ignored)\n* `_world_state` - Current world state (ignored)\n* `state` - Storyteller state (passed through unchanged)","ref":"Operator.Director.NullStoryteller.html#pick_event/3-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.Director.NullStoryteller.pick_event/3","doc":"`{nil, state}` - No event, state unchanged","ref":"Operator.Director.NullStoryteller.html#pick_event/3-returns"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.HTN.Axiom","doc":"Reusable query patterns for HTN preconditions.\n\nInspired by Decima's HTN implementation, axioms allow you to define\nnamed, parameterized query patterns that can be reused across multiple\ngoals and tasks.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Axiom.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Usage - Operator.HTN.Axiom","doc":"Define axioms in your HTN module:\n\n    defmodule MyGame.Behavior do\n      use Operator.HTN.DSL\n\n      # Define a reusable query pattern\n      axiom :nearby_enemy do\n        fn facts, args ->\n          max_distance = Keyword.get(args, :max_distance, 10.0)\n          enemies = Facts.get(facts, {:world, :visible_enemies}, [])\n\n          Enum.any?(enemies, fn enemy ->\n            Facts.get(facts, {:world, {:distance, enemy}}, 999) <= max_distance\n          end)\n        end\n      end\n\n      # Use the axiom in a precondition\n      goal :attack_nearby do\n        precond {:axiom, :nearby_enemy, max_distance: 5.0}\n\n        decompose do\n          task :engage_enemy\n        end\n      end\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.Axiom.html#module-usage"},{"type":"module","title":"Arguments - Operator.HTN.Axiom","doc":"Axioms receive two arguments:\n- `facts` - The current world state\n- `args` - Keyword list of arguments passed when the axiom is invoked","ref":"Operator.HTN.Axiom.html#module-arguments"},{"type":"module","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Axiom","doc":"# Axiom with no arguments\n    axiom :has_weapon do\n      fn facts, _args -> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :weapon}) end\n    end\n\n    # Axiom with arguments\n    axiom :health_above do\n      fn facts, args ->\n        threshold = Keyword.get(args, :threshold, 50)\n        Facts.get(facts, {:self, :health}, 0) > threshold\n      end\n    end\n\n    # Usage in preconditions\n    precond {:axiom, :has_weapon}\n    precond {:axiom, :health_above, threshold: 75}","ref":"Operator.HTN.Axiom.html#module-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Registration - Operator.HTN.Axiom","doc":"Axioms defined in DSL modules are automatically registered with the\n`Operator.HTN.Registry` alongside goals, tasks, and primitives.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Axiom.html#module-registration"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Axiom.t/0","doc":"","ref":"Operator.HTN.Axiom.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Axiom.evaluate/3","doc":"Evaluate an axiom against facts with the given arguments.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Axiom.html#evaluate/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Axiom.evaluate/3","doc":"iex> alias Operator.HTN.{Axiom, Facts}\n    iex> axiom = Axiom.new(:energized?, fn facts, _args -> Facts.get(facts, {:self, :energy}, 0) > 0 end)\n    iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{energy: 10}})\n    iex> Axiom.evaluate(axiom, facts, [])\n    true","ref":"Operator.HTN.Axiom.html#evaluate/3-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Axiom.new/3","doc":"Create a new axiom.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Axiom.html#new/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Arguments - Operator.HTN.Axiom.new/3","doc":"- `name` - The axiom identifier\n- `query_fn` - A function of arity 2: `fn facts, args -> boolean end`\n- `opts` - Options:\n  - `:metadata` - Arbitrary metadata map","ref":"Operator.HTN.Axiom.html#new/3-arguments"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Axiom.new/3","doc":"iex> alias Operator.HTN.Axiom\n    iex> axiom = Axiom.new(:has_energy, fn _facts, _args -> true end)\n    iex> axiom.name\n    :has_energy","ref":"Operator.HTN.Axiom.html#new/3-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.HTN.DSL","doc":"Domain-specific language for defining HTN goals, tasks, and primitives.\n\nThe DSL provides a declarative way to define agent behaviors that compile\ninto efficient runtime structures. This is the primary way to define HTN\ndomains in Operator.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Important: Alias Scope in Functions - Operator.HTN.DSL","doc":"**Functions inside `precond` and `decompose` are evaluated at runtime, not\ncompile time.** This means module aliases from your module's header are NOT\navailable inside these functions.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#module-important-alias-scope-in-functions"},{"type":"module","title":"This will FAIL at runtime: - Operator.HTN.DSL","doc":"defmodule MyBehavior do\n      use Operator.HTN.DSL\n\n      alias Operator.HTN.Facts  # This alias is NOT available in precond!\n\n      goal :my_goal do\n        precond fn facts ->\n          Facts.get(facts, {:self, :ready})  # FAILS - Facts not in scope\n        end\n      end\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#module-this-will-fail-at-runtime"},{"type":"module","title":"Use full module paths instead: - Operator.HTN.DSL","doc":"defmodule MyBehavior do\n      use Operator.HTN.DSL\n\n      goal :my_goal do\n        precond fn facts ->\n          Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:self, :ready})  # Works!\n        end\n      end\n    end\n\nThis limitation exists because the anonymous functions are stored as AST\nand compiled at runtime when the module is registered. The runtime\ncompilation context doesn't have access to your module's compile-time\naliases.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#module-use-full-module-paths-instead"},{"type":"module","title":"Quick Start - Operator.HTN.DSL","doc":"defmodule MyGame.NPCBehavior do\n      use Operator.HTN.DSL\n\n      # High-level objective\n      goal :find_food do\n        precond fn facts ->\n          Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:self, :hunger}, 0) > 50\n        end\n\n        decompose do\n          task :locate_food\n          task :move_to_food\n          task :eat_food\n        end\n\n        metadata priority: 5, domain: :survival\n      end\n\n      # Intermediate task with dynamic decomposition\n      task :locate_food do\n        precond fn facts ->\n          not Operator.HTN.Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :food_location})\n        end\n\n        decompose fn facts ->\n          nearby = Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:world, :food_sources}, [])\n          [{:search_for_food, [List.first(nearby)]}]\n        end\n\n        cost 2.0\n      end\n\n      # Directly executable action\n      primitive :eat_food do\n        run fn actor, _facts ->\n          # Your execution logic here\n          {:ok, %{actor | hunger: 0}}\n        end\n\n        metadata action_type: :consume, duration: 1000\n      end\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#module-quick-start"},{"type":"module","title":"DSL Elements - Operator.HTN.DSL","doc":"","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#module-dsl-elements"},{"type":"module","title":"Goals - Operator.HTN.DSL","doc":"Goals are high-level objectives that an agent can pursue:\n\n    goal :goal_name do\n      # Optional precondition (must be true to pursue goal)\n      precond fn facts -> boolean end\n\n      # Static task sequence\n      decompose do\n        task :first_task\n        task :second_task, \"arg1\", :arg2\n      end\n\n      # Optional metadata\n      metadata priority: 5, category: :combat\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#module-goals"},{"type":"module","title":"Tasks - Operator.HTN.DSL","doc":"Tasks are intermediate steps that can decompose into subtasks:\n\n    task :task_name, arg1, arg2 do\n      # Optional precondition\n      precond fn facts -> boolean end\n\n      # Dynamic decomposition based on world state\n      decompose fn facts ->\n        [{:subtask_a, []}, {:subtask_b, [some_value]}]\n      end\n\n      # Optional cost for planning heuristics\n      cost 1.5\n\n      # Optional metadata\n      metadata category: :movement\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#module-tasks"},{"type":"module","title":"Primitives - Operator.HTN.DSL","doc":"Primitives are directly executable actions:\n\n    primitive :action_name, target do\n      # Execution function\n      run fn actor, facts ->\n        # Perform the action\n        {:ok, updated_actor}\n      end\n\n      # Optional metadata\n      metadata action_type: :attack, animation: \"strike\"\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#module-primitives"},{"type":"module","title":"Axioms - Operator.HTN.DSL","doc":"Axioms are reusable query patterns (inspired by Decima's HTN):\n\n    axiom :enemy_nearby do\n      fn facts, args ->\n        max_dist = Keyword.get(args, :max_distance, 10)\n        enemy_dist = Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:world, :enemy_distance}, 999)\n        enemy_dist <= max_dist\n      end\n    end\n\n    # Use in preconditions:\n    precond {:axiom, :enemy_nearby, max_distance: 5}","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#module-axioms"},{"type":"module","title":"Precondition Operators - Operator.HTN.DSL","doc":"Preconditions support logical operators:\n\n    # AND (all must be true)\n    precond {:all, [fn1, fn2, fn3]}\n\n    # OR (any must be true)\n    precond {:any, [fn1, fn2]}\n\n    # ALT (first matching, with preference order)\n    precond {:first, [preferred_fn, fallback_fn]}\n\n    # NOT (negation)\n    precond {:not, fn facts -> ... end}\n\n    # Axiom reference\n    precond {:axiom, :axiom_name, args}","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#module-precondition-operators"},{"type":"module","title":"Auto-Registration - Operator.HTN.DSL","doc":"Modules using this DSL are automatically registered with `Operator.HTN.Registry`\nafter compilation. To disable:\n\n    use Operator.HTN.DSL, auto_register: false","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#module-auto-registration"},{"type":"module","title":"Compilation - Operator.HTN.DSL","doc":"The DSL uses Elixir macros to transform your definitions into optimized\nruntime structures at compile time. Anonymous functions in preconditions\nand decompose blocks are preserved for runtime evaluation.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#module-compilation"},{"type":"module","title":"See Also - Operator.HTN.DSL","doc":"* `Operator.HTN.Registry` - Where goals/tasks are stored\n* `Operator.HTN.Engine` - How goals are expanded into plans\n* `Operator.HTN.Precondition` - Logical operators\n* `Operator.HTN.Axiom` - Reusable queries","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#module-see-also"},{"type":"macro","title":"Operator.HTN.DSL.__using__/1","doc":"Sets up the module to use the HTN DSL.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#__using__/1"},{"type":"macro","title":"Options - Operator.HTN.DSL.__using__/1","doc":"* `:auto_register` - Whether to register with `Operator.HTN.Registry` after\n  compilation. Defaults to `true`.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#__using__/1-options"},{"type":"macro","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.DSL.__using__/1","doc":"defmodule MyDomain do\n      use Operator.HTN.DSL\n      # ...\n    end\n\n    # Disable auto-registration (useful for testing)\n    defmodule TestDomain do\n      use Operator.HTN.DSL, auto_register: false\n      # ...\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#__using__/1-examples"},{"type":"macro","title":"Operator.HTN.DSL.axiom/2","doc":"Define a reusable query axiom.\n\nAxioms are named query patterns that can be reused in preconditions.\nInspired by Decima's HTN implementation.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#axiom/2"},{"type":"macro","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.DSL.axiom/2","doc":"* `name` - Atom identifier for the axiom","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#axiom/2-parameters"},{"type":"macro","title":"Block Contents - Operator.HTN.DSL.axiom/2","doc":"The block should contain a function with signature:\n\n    fn facts, args -> boolean end\n\nWhere:\n* `facts` - Current world state (`Operator.HTN.Facts.t()`)\n* `args` - Keyword list of arguments passed when invoked","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#axiom/2-block-contents"},{"type":"macro","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.DSL.axiom/2","doc":"axiom :has_clear_shot do\n      fn facts, args ->\n        target = Keyword.get(args, :target)\n        distance = Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:world, {:distance, target}}, 999)\n        cover = Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:world, {:cover_between, target}}, false)\n\n        distance < 50 and not cover\n      end\n    end\n\n    # Use in preconditions:\n    goal :snipe do\n      precond {:axiom, :has_clear_shot, target: :enemy}\n      # ...\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#axiom/2-examples"},{"type":"macro","title":"Operator.HTN.DSL.goal/2","doc":"Define a goal.\n\nGoals are high-level objectives that decompose into sequences of tasks.\nThey are the entry points for HTN planning.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#goal/2"},{"type":"macro","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.DSL.goal/2","doc":"* `name` - Atom identifier for the goal","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#goal/2-parameters"},{"type":"macro","title":"Block Contents - Operator.HTN.DSL.goal/2","doc":"* `precond fn facts -> boolean end` - Optional precondition\n* `decompose do ... end` - Task sequence\n* `metadata key: value` - Optional metadata","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#goal/2-block-contents"},{"type":"macro","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.DSL.goal/2","doc":"goal :patrol do\n      precond fn facts ->\n        Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:self, :on_duty}, false)\n      end\n\n      decompose do\n        task :walk_to_waypoint, :next\n        task :scan_area\n      end\n\n      metadata priority: 3, domain: :security\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#goal/2-examples"},{"type":"macro","title":"Operator.HTN.DSL.primitive/2","doc":"Define a primitive action without arguments.\n\nSee `primitive/3` for full documentation.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#primitive/2"},{"type":"macro","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.DSL.primitive/2","doc":"primitive :wait do\n      run fn actor, _facts ->\n        {:ok, actor}\n      end\n\n      metadata action_type: :idle\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#primitive/2-examples"},{"type":"macro","title":"Operator.HTN.DSL.primitive/3","doc":"Define a primitive action with arguments.\n\nPrimitives are directly executable actions that don't decompose further.\nThey are the \"leaves\" of the HTN tree.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#primitive/3"},{"type":"macro","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.DSL.primitive/3","doc":"* `name` - Atom identifier for the primitive\n* `args` - Variable names for action arguments","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#primitive/3-parameters"},{"type":"macro","title":"Block Contents - Operator.HTN.DSL.primitive/3","doc":"* `run fn actor, facts -> {:ok, actor} | {:error, reason} end` - Execution function\n* `metadata key: value` - Optional metadata","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#primitive/3-block-contents"},{"type":"macro","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.DSL.primitive/3","doc":"primitive :fire_weapon, target do\n      run fn actor, facts ->\n        ammo = Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:self, :ammo}, 0)\n\n        if ammo > 0 do\n          # Your game logic here\n          {:ok, %{actor | ammo: ammo - 1}}\n        else\n          {:error, :no_ammo}\n        end\n      end\n\n      metadata action_type: :attack, sound: \"gunshot.wav\"\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#primitive/3-examples"},{"type":"macro","title":"Operator.HTN.DSL.task/2","doc":"Define a task without arguments.\n\nSee `task/3` for full documentation.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#task/2"},{"type":"macro","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.DSL.task/2","doc":"task :scan_area do\n      precond fn facts ->\n        Operator.HTN.Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :sensors})\n      end\n\n      decompose do\n        task :rotate_sensors\n        task :process_data\n      end\n\n      cost 1.0\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#task/2-examples"},{"type":"macro","title":"Operator.HTN.DSL.task/3","doc":"Define a task with arguments.\n\nTasks are intermediate steps that may decompose into subtasks or primitives.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#task/3"},{"type":"macro","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.DSL.task/3","doc":"* `name` - Atom identifier for the task\n* `args` - Variable names for task arguments (captured at definition time)","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#task/3-parameters"},{"type":"macro","title":"Block Contents - Operator.HTN.DSL.task/3","doc":"* `precond fn facts -> boolean end` - Optional precondition\n* `decompose fn facts -> [{task, args}] end` - Dynamic subtask list\n* `cost number` - Optional planning cost\n* `metadata key: value` - Optional metadata","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#task/3-block-contents"},{"type":"macro","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.DSL.task/3","doc":"task :move_to, destination do\n      precond fn facts ->\n        Operator.HTN.Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :can_move})\n      end\n\n      decompose fn facts ->\n        current = Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:self, :position})\n        [{:navigate, [current, destination]}]\n      end\n\n      cost 5.0\n      metadata category: :locomotion\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.html#task/3-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder","doc":"Builds runtime structures from DSL AST.\n\nThis module transforms the compile-time AST captured by `Operator.HTN.DSL`\nmacros into data structures that can be stored in the compiled module. It's\nthe bridge between Elixir's macro system and Operator's runtime planning.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Why This Module Exists - Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder","doc":"When you write DSL code like:\n\n    goal :attack do\n      precond fn facts -> Facts.get(facts, {:self, :armed}) end\n      decompose do\n        task :aim\n        task :fire\n      end\n    end\n\nThe `goal` macro captures this as AST (Abstract Syntax Tree). But we can't\njust store raw AST - we need structured data that the planner can work with\nefficiently at runtime.\n\nThis module handles that transformation:\n\n1. **Parses** the captured AST blocks\n2. **Extracts** preconditions, decompose functions, costs, metadata\n3. **Builds** `%Task{}` structs and goal maps\n4. **Preserves** function AST for runtime compilation","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#module-why-this-module-exists"},{"type":"module","title":"AST Preservation - Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder","doc":"Anonymous functions cannot be escaped with `Macro.escape/1` and stored\ndirectly in module attributes. Instead, we store them as quoted AST and\ncompile them at runtime when needed (see `Operator.HTN.Executor`).\n\nThis is why you'll see patterns like:\n\n    %Task{\n      preconditions: [{:fn, _, _clauses}],  # Stored as AST\n      decompose: {:fn, _, _clauses}          # Stored as AST\n    }","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#module-ast-preservation"},{"type":"module","title":"Internal Module - Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder","doc":"This module is considered internal to the DSL implementation. Users should\ninteract with `Operator.HTN.DSL` macros rather than calling these functions\ndirectly.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#module-internal-module"},{"type":"module","title":"See Also - Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder","doc":"* `Operator.HTN.DSL` - The public macro interface\n* `Operator.HTN.Task` - The runtime task structure\n* `Operator.HTN.Registry` - Where built structures are stored","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#module-see-also"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.build_axiom/1","doc":"Build an axiom map from captured DSL AST.\n\nTransforms the AST captured by the `axiom` macro into a map structure.\nAxioms are reusable query patterns that can be referenced in preconditions.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#build_axiom/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.build_axiom/1","doc":"* `{name, query_fn_ast}` - Tuple of axiom name and the query function AST","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#build_axiom/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.build_axiom/1","doc":"A map with:\n\n* `:name` - Axiom identifier atom\n* `:query_fn` - The query function AST","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#build_axiom/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Axiom Functions - Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.build_axiom/1","doc":"Axiom functions have the signature:\n\n    fn facts, args -> boolean end\n\nWhere `args` is a keyword list of arguments passed when the axiom is\ninvoked in a precondition.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#build_axiom/1-axiom-functions"},{"type":"function","title":"Example - Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.build_axiom/1","doc":"Given this DSL input:\n\n    axiom :enemy_in_range do\n      fn facts, args ->\n        max_range = Keyword.get(args, :range, 10)\n        enemy_dist = Facts.get(facts, {:world, :enemy_distance}, 999)\n        enemy_dist <= max_range\n      end\n    end\n\nUsed in preconditions as:\n\n    precond {:axiom, :enemy_in_range, range: 5}","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#build_axiom/1-example"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.build_goal/1","doc":"Build a goal map from captured DSL AST.\n\nTransforms the AST captured by the `goal` macro into a map structure\nsuitable for storage in the Registry.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#build_goal/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.build_goal/1","doc":"* `{name, block}` - Tuple of goal name atom and the captured block AST","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#build_goal/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.build_goal/1","doc":"A map with the following keys:\n\n* `:name` - Goal identifier atom\n* `:precond` - Precondition function AST, or `nil` if none specified\n* `:decompose` - List of `{task_name, args}` tuples from the decompose block\n* `:metadata` - Map of user-defined metadata","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#build_goal/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Example Transformation - Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.build_goal/1","doc":"Given this DSL input:\n\n    goal :infiltrate do\n      precond fn facts -> Facts.get(facts, {:self, :stealthy}) end\n      decompose do\n        task :sneak_to, :entrance\n        task :pick_lock\n      end\n      metadata domain: :stealth, priority: 5\n    end\n\nThis function produces:\n\n    %{\n      name: :infiltrate,\n      precond: {:fn, _, _},  # AST for the precondition\n      decompose: [{:sneak_to, [:entrance]}, {:pick_lock, []}],\n      metadata: %{domain: :stealth, priority: 5}\n    }","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#build_goal/1-example-transformation"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.build_primitive/1","doc":"Build a primitive Task struct from captured DSL AST.\n\nTransforms the AST captured by the `primitive` macro into a `%Task{}`\nstruct. Primitives are the executable leaf nodes of the HTN tree - they\ndon't decompose further but instead have a `run` function.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#build_primitive/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.build_primitive/1","doc":"* `{name, args, block}` - Tuple containing:\n  * `name` - Primitive identifier atom\n  * `args` - List of argument variable names\n  * `block` - The captured block AST","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#build_primitive/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.build_primitive/1","doc":"A `%Task{}` struct with:\n\n* `:name` - Primitive identifier\n* `:type` - Always `:primitive`\n* `:preconditions` - Empty list (primitives use runtime checks)\n* `:decompose` - `nil` (primitives don't decompose)\n* `:cost` - Fixed at 1.0\n* `:metadata` - Map containing:\n  * `:args` - Argument names from definition\n  * `:run` - The execution function AST\n  * Any user-defined metadata","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#build_primitive/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Run Function - Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.build_primitive/1","doc":"The `run` function AST is stored in metadata and compiled at execution\ntime by `Operator.HTN.Executor`. The function signature is:\n\n    fn actor, facts -> {:ok, updated_actor} | {:error, reason} end","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#build_primitive/1-run-function"},{"type":"function","title":"Example - Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.build_primitive/1","doc":"Given this DSL input:\n\n    primitive :fire_weapon, target do\n      run fn actor, facts ->\n        {:ok, %{actor | ammo: actor.ammo - 1}}\n      end\n      metadata animation: \"shoot\", sound: \"gunfire.wav\"\n    end\n\nThis function produces a Task with metadata containing both the run\nfunction AST and the user metadata.","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#build_primitive/1-example"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.build_task/1","doc":"Build a Task struct from captured DSL AST.\n\nTransforms the AST captured by the `task` macro into a `%Task{}` struct.\nTasks defined via DSL are always `:abstract` type (they decompose into\nother tasks or primitives).","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#build_task/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.build_task/1","doc":"* `{name, args, block}` - Tuple containing:\n  * `name` - Task identifier atom\n  * `args` - List of argument variable names from the task definition\n  * `block` - The captured block AST","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#build_task/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.build_task/1","doc":"A `%Task{}` struct with:\n\n* `:name` - Task identifier\n* `:type` - Always `:abstract` for DSL tasks\n* `:preconditions` - List of precondition function ASTs\n* `:decompose` - Either `{:static_tasks, list}` or function AST\n* `:cost` - Numeric cost value (default: 1.0)\n* `:metadata` - Map including `:args` and user metadata","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#build_task/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Decomposition Modes - Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.build_task/1","doc":"Tasks can decompose in two ways:\n\n**Static decomposition** (compile-time known sequence):\n\n    task :prepare_attack do\n      decompose do\n        task :draw_weapon\n        task :aim\n      end\n    end\n\nStored as: `{:static_tasks, [{:draw_weapon, []}, {:aim, []}]}`\n\n**Dynamic decomposition** (runtime decision):\n\n    task :move_to, destination do\n      decompose fn facts ->\n        current = Facts.get(facts, {:self, :position})\n        [{:pathfind, [current, destination]}]\n      end\n    end\n\nStored as: `{:fn, _, _}` (raw AST for runtime compilation)","ref":"Operator.HTN.DSL.Builder.html#build_task/1-decomposition-modes"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.HTN.Effect","doc":"Effects represent world state changes that result from task execution.\n\nEffects are the bridge between planning and reality. They let the planner\nreason about future states, enabling complex plans where early actions\ncreate conditions needed by later actions.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Why Effects Matter - Operator.HTN.Effect","doc":"Consider an NPC that needs to enter a locked room:\n\n1. Without effects, the planner checks `:enter_room`'s precondition\n   (`door_unlocked == true`), finds it false, and gives up.\n\n2. With effects, the planner:\n   - Plans `:unlock_door` first\n   - Applies its effect (`door_unlocked = true`) to a working copy of facts\n   - Now `:enter_room`'s precondition passes against the projected state\n   - Generates plan: `[{:unlock_door, []}, {:enter_room, []}]`\n\nThis is the essence of HTN planning - reasoning about sequences of actions\nand their cumulative effects on world state.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#module-why-effects-matter"},{"type":"module","title":"Effect Types - Operator.HTN.Effect","doc":"Based on GameAIPro HTN patterns, there are three effect types:\n\n| Type               | Planning | Execution | Use Case                           |\n|--------------------|----------|-----------|-----------------------------------|\n| `:plan_only`       | ✓        | ✗         | Temporary planning assumptions     |\n| `:plan_and_execute`| ✓        | ✓         | Standard effects (most common)     |\n| `:permanent`       | ✓        | ✓*        | Effects that persist on failure    |\n\n*Permanent effects are applied even if subsequent tasks fail.\n\n### `:plan_only`\n\nApplied during planning but NOT during execution. Use when:\n- The execution system handles the effect differently\n- You need to \"pretend\" something is true for planning purposes\n- Simulating optimistic assumptions\n\n    # Assume we'll find ammo during the mission (planning only)\n    Effect.new(:plan_only, {:self, :has_ammo}, true)\n\n### `:plan_and_execute`\n\nApplied during both planning AND execution. This is the standard type for\nmost game actions.\n\n    # Door is unlocked after picking the lock\n    Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:world, :door_unlocked}, true)\n\n    # Health consumed after healing\n    Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:self, :health_potion_count}, 0)\n\n### `:permanent`\n\nApplied during planning and persists regardless of task success/failure.\nUse sparingly - these represent irreversible actions.\n\n    # Alert triggered - can't un-ring that bell\n    Effect.new(:permanent, {:world, :alarm_triggered}, true)\n\n    # Resource consumed even if subsequent actions fail\n    Effect.new(:permanent, {:self, :grenade_count}, :decrement)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#module-effect-types"},{"type":"module","title":"Working with Effects - Operator.HTN.Effect","doc":"","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#module-working-with-effects"},{"type":"module","title":"Creating Effects - Operator.HTN.Effect","doc":"effect = Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:self, :armed}, true)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#module-creating-effects"},{"type":"module","title":"Applying Effects - Operator.HTN.Effect","doc":"# Single effect\n    updated_facts = Effect.apply_effect(effect, facts)\n\n    # Multiple effects\n    updated_facts = Effect.apply_all(effects, facts)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#module-applying-effects"},{"type":"module","title":"Filtering Effects - Operator.HTN.Effect","doc":"# Get effects for execution (excludes :plan_only)\n    execution_effects = Effect.execution_effects(task.effects)\n\n    # Get effects by specific type\n    permanent_only = Effect.filter_by_type(effects, :permanent)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#module-filtering-effects"},{"type":"module","title":"Integration with Tasks - Operator.HTN.Effect","doc":"Effects are typically defined on primitives in the DSL:\n\n    primitive :unlock_door do\n      run fn actor, _facts ->\n        {:ok, %{actor | picked_lock: true}}\n      end\n\n      effect Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:world, :door_unlocked}, true)\n    end\n\nThe `Executor` automatically applies execution effects after successful\nprimitive completion.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#module-integration-with-tasks"},{"type":"module","title":"See Also - Operator.HTN.Effect","doc":"* `Operator.HTN.Task` - Where effects are attached\n* `Operator.HTN.Engine` - Applies effects during planning\n* `Operator.HTN.Executor` - Applies effects during execution\n* `Operator.HTN.Facts` - The world state effects modify","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#module-see-also"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Effect.effect_type/0","doc":"The effect type determining when the effect is applied.\n\n* `:plan_only` - Planning phase only\n* `:plan_and_execute` - Both planning and execution\n* `:permanent` - Persists even on task failure","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#t:effect_type/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Effect.t/0","doc":"The Effect struct.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Fields - Operator.HTN.Effect.t/0","doc":"* `:type` - When the effect is applied\n* `:key` - The fact key to modify (e.g., `{:self, :armed}`)\n* `:value` - The new value to set","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#t:t/0-fields"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Effect.apply_all/2","doc":"Apply multiple effects to facts in sequence.\n\nEffects are applied in list order, so later effects can override earlier ones\nif they modify the same key.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#apply_all/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Effect.apply_all/2","doc":"* `effects` - List of Effect structs\n* `facts` - The current Facts struct","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#apply_all/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Effect.apply_all/2","doc":"A new Facts struct with all effects applied.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#apply_all/2-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Effect.apply_all/2","doc":"iex> alias Operator.HTN.{Effect, Facts}\n    iex> effects = [\n    ...>   Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:self, :armed}, true),\n    ...>   Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:self, :in_combat}, true)\n    ...> ]\n    iex> updated_facts = Effect.apply_all(effects, Facts.new())\n    iex> Facts.get(updated_facts, {:self, :armed})\n    true","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#apply_all/2-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Effect.apply_effect/2","doc":"Apply an effect to facts, updating the world state.\n\nThis function modifies the facts by setting the effect's key to its value.\nNamed `apply_effect` to avoid conflict with `Kernel.apply/2`.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#apply_effect/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Effect.apply_effect/2","doc":"* `effect` - The Effect struct to apply\n* `facts` - The current Facts struct","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#apply_effect/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Effect.apply_effect/2","doc":"A new Facts struct with the effect applied.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#apply_effect/2-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Effect.apply_effect/2","doc":"iex> alias Operator.HTN.{Effect, Facts}\n    iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{armed: false}})\n    iex> effect = Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:self, :armed}, true)\n    iex> updated_facts = Effect.apply_effect(effect, facts)\n    iex> Facts.get(updated_facts, {:self, :armed})\n    true","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#apply_effect/2-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Effect.execution_effects/1","doc":"Get only effects that should be applied during execution.\n\nExcludes `:plan_only` effects, which are only used during planning.\nReturns both `:plan_and_execute` and `:permanent` effects.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#execution_effects/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Effect.execution_effects/1","doc":"* `effects` - List of Effect structs","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#execution_effects/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Effect.execution_effects/1","doc":"List of effects suitable for execution (excludes `:plan_only`).","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#execution_effects/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Effect.execution_effects/1","doc":"iex> alias Operator.HTN.Effect\n    iex> effects = [\n    ...>   Effect.new(:plan_only, {:self, :optimistic_assumption}, true),\n    ...>   Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:self, :armed}, true)\n    ...> ]\n    iex> Enum.map(Effect.execution_effects(effects), & &1.type)\n    [:plan_and_execute]","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#execution_effects/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Effect.filter_by_type/2","doc":"Filter effects by type.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#filter_by_type/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Effect.filter_by_type/2","doc":"* `effects` - List of Effect structs\n* `type` - The effect type to filter for","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#filter_by_type/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Effect.filter_by_type/2","doc":"List of effects matching the specified type.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#filter_by_type/2-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Effect.filter_by_type/2","doc":"iex> alias Operator.HTN.Effect\n    iex> effects = [\n    ...>   Effect.new(:plan_only, {:self, :assumed_safe}, true),\n    ...>   Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:self, :armed}, true),\n    ...>   Effect.new(:permanent, {:world, :alerted}, true)\n    ...> ]\n    iex> length(Effect.filter_by_type(effects, :plan_only))\n    1","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#filter_by_type/2-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Effect.new/3","doc":"Create a new effect.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#new/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Effect.new/3","doc":"* `type` - When the effect is applied:\n  * `:plan_only` - Planning phase only\n  * `:plan_and_execute` - Both planning and execution (most common)\n  * `:permanent` - Persists even on task failure\n* `key` - The fact key to modify (e.g., `{:self, :has_weapon}`)\n* `value` - The new value to set","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#new/3-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Effect.new/3","doc":"iex> alias Operator.HTN.Effect\n    iex> # Standard effect - door unlocked after picking lock\n    iex> Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:world, :door_locked}, false)\n\n    iex> # Planning assumption - assume we'll find resources\n    iex> Effect.new(:plan_only, {:self, :has_keycard}, true)\n\n    iex> # Permanent - alert can't be un-triggered\n    iex> Effect.new(:permanent, {:world, :security_alerted}, true)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#new/3-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Effect.planning_effects/1","doc":"Get only effects applied during planning.\n\nAll effect types are applied during planning, so this returns the full list.\nThis function exists for API symmetry with `execution_effects/1`.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#planning_effects/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Effect.planning_effects/1","doc":"* `effects` - List of Effect structs","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#planning_effects/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Effect.planning_effects/1","doc":"The input list unchanged (all effects apply during planning).","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#planning_effects/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Effect.planning_effects/1","doc":"iex> alias Operator.HTN.Effect\n    iex> effects = [\n    ...>   Effect.new(:plan_only, {:self, :assumed}, true),\n    ...>   Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:self, :real}, true)\n    ...> ]\n    iex> Effect.planning_effects(effects) == effects\n    true","ref":"Operator.HTN.Effect.html#planning_effects/1-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.HTN.Engine","doc":"HTN engine for goal expansion, precondition evaluation, and plan generation.\n\nThe engine implements **total-order forward decomposition**, the HTN planning\napproach described in GameAIPro. This means:\n\n1. Tasks are expanded in order (total-order)\n2. Planning proceeds forward from the current state\n3. Effects are applied during planning to simulate future states","ref":"Operator.HTN.Engine.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Planning Algorithm - Operator.HTN.Engine","doc":"1. Look up the goal in the registry\n2. Check goal preconditions against current facts\n3. Decompose goal into tasks via its decompose function\n4. For each task:\n   - If abstract: check preconditions, decompose recursively\n   - If primitive: check preconditions, collect into plan, apply effects\n5. Return the plan (list of primitive tasks)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Engine.html#module-planning-algorithm"},{"type":"module","title":"Effects During Planning - Operator.HTN.Engine","doc":"A key feature of HTN planning is that effects are applied to a working copy\nof world state during planning. This allows downstream tasks to have their\npreconditions validated against the expected future state.\n\nFor example, if task A has effect \"has_key=true\" and task B has precondition\n\"has_key\", then B's precondition will be satisfied when planning A before B.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Engine.html#module-effects-during-planning"},{"type":"module","title":"Usage - Operator.HTN.Engine","doc":"facts = Operator.HTN.Facts.from_perception(%{\n      self: %{location: :lobby},\n      world: %{target: :server_room}\n    })\n\n    case Engine.expand(:infiltrate, facts, %{}) do\n      {:ok, plan} ->\n        # plan.tasks contains the sequence of primitives\n        IO.inspect(plan.tasks)\n\n      {:error, :preconditions_not_met} ->\n        # Goal preconditions failed\n        :retry_later\n\n      {:error, :goal_not_found} ->\n        # Goal not registered\n        :unknown_goal\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.Engine.html#module-usage"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Engine.expand/5","doc":"Expand a goal into a plan.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Engine.html#expand/5"},{"type":"function","title":"Arguments - Operator.HTN.Engine.expand/5","doc":"- `goal_name` - The goal atom to expand\n- `facts` - Current world state\n- `traits` - Agent traits/genome for cost calculations\n- `htn_registry` - Optional registry (defaults to `Registry.all()`)\n- `opts` - Options:\n  - `:budget` - Budget limits (e.g., `[max_tasks: 100, max_expansions: 200, max_depth: 20, timeout_ms: 5]`)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Engine.html#expand/5-arguments"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Engine.expand/5","doc":"- `{:ok, plan}` - Successfully expanded plan\n- `{:error, :goal_not_found}` - Goal not in registry\n- `{:error, :preconditions_not_met}` - Goal preconditions failed","ref":"Operator.HTN.Engine.html#expand/5-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Engine.goal_preconditions_met?/3","doc":"Check if a goal's preconditions are met.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Engine.html#goal_preconditions_met?/3"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.HTN.Executor","doc":"Executes HTN plans and primitive tasks.\n\nThe Executor bridges the gap between plan generation and actual execution.\nWhile the HTN planner generates plans (sequences of primitive tasks), the\nExecutor handles running those tasks against your game/simulation state.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Quick Start - Operator.HTN.Executor","doc":"# Generate a plan\n    {:ok, plan} = Operator.HTN.Planner.run(:my_goal, facts, traits)\n\n    # Execute step by step\n    case Executor.step(plan, actor, facts) do\n      {:ok, :completed, updated_actor, updated_facts} ->\n        # Plan finished successfully\n        handle_completion(updated_actor)\n\n      {:ok, :continue, updated_actor, updated_facts, remaining_plan} ->\n        # More tasks to execute\n        loop_execution(remaining_plan, updated_actor, updated_facts)\n\n      {:error, reason, actor, facts, plan} ->\n        # Task failed - decide whether to replan or abort\n        handle_failure(reason, actor, facts, plan)\n    end\n\n    # Or execute entire plan at once\n    case Executor.run_plan(plan, actor, facts) do\n      {:ok, final_actor, final_facts} ->\n        # All tasks completed\n        :done\n\n      {:error, reason, actor, facts, remaining_plan} ->\n        # Failed mid-execution\n        :failed\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#module-quick-start"},{"type":"module","title":"Primitive Execution - Operator.HTN.Executor","doc":"Primitives defined via the DSL store their `run` function as quoted AST.\nThe Executor handles compiling and invoking these functions:\n\n    # Direct primitive execution\n    primitive = Registry.get_primitive(:attack)\n    {:ok, updated_actor} = Executor.execute_primitive(primitive, actor, facts)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#module-primitive-execution"},{"type":"module","title":"Task Tuples - Operator.HTN.Executor","doc":"Plans contain task tuples of the form `{task_name, args}`:\n\n    plan.tasks\n    #=> [{:move_to, [:lobby]}, {:hack_terminal, [\"server_1\"]}, {:extract, []}]\n\nExecute individual task tuples:\n\n    {:ok, actor} = Executor.execute_task({:attack, [:enemy]}, actor, facts)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#module-task-tuples"},{"type":"module","title":"Error Handling - Operator.HTN.Executor","doc":"Execution functions return tagged tuples:\n\n* `{:ok, actor}` - Task succeeded, returns updated actor\n* `{:error, reason}` - Task failed with reason\n\nCommon failure reasons:\n* `:primitive_not_found` - No primitive registered with that name\n* `:no_run_function` - Primitive missing `run` in metadata\n* `:execution_failed` - The run function raised or returned error","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#module-error-handling"},{"type":"module","title":"Effects - Operator.HTN.Executor","doc":"When tasks complete successfully, their `:plan_and_execute` and `:permanent`\neffects should be applied to world state. The Executor provides helpers:\n\n    # Get effects to apply after successful execution\n    effects = Executor.execution_effects(primitive)\n    updated_facts = Operator.HTN.Effect.apply_all(effects, facts)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#module-effects"},{"type":"module","title":"Integration with Game Loop - Operator.HTN.Executor","doc":"Typical integration pattern:\n\n    defmodule MyGame.AISystem do\n      alias Operator.HTN.{Executor, Planner, Facts}\n\n      def tick(entity, world_state) do\n        facts = build_facts(entity, world_state)\n        traits = entity.genome\n\n        case entity.current_plan do\n          nil ->\n            # No plan - try to create one\n            case Planner.run(pick_goal(entity), facts, traits) do\n              {:ok, plan} -> %{entity | current_plan: plan}\n              {:error, _} -> entity\n            end\n\n          plan ->\n            # Have a plan - execute next step\n            case Executor.step(plan, entity, facts) do\n              {:ok, :completed, updated_entity, _facts, _plan} ->\n                %{updated_entity | current_plan: nil}\n\n              {:ok, :continue, updated_entity, _facts, remaining_plan} ->\n                %{updated_entity | current_plan: remaining_plan}\n\n              {:error, _reason, entity, _facts, _plan} ->\n                %{entity | current_plan: nil}  # Replan next tick\n            end\n        end\n      end\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#module-integration-with-game-loop"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Executor.plan_result/0","doc":"Result of running a complete plan.\n\n* `{:ok, actor, facts}` - All tasks completed successfully\n* `{:error, reason, actor, facts, remaining_plan}` - Failed mid-execution","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#t:plan_result/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Executor.step_result/0","doc":"Result of a plan execution step.\n\n* `{:ok, :completed, actor, facts, plan}` - Plan finished\n* `{:ok, :continue, actor, facts, plan}` - More tasks remain\n* `{:error, reason, actor, facts, plan}` - Task failed","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#t:step_result/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Executor.task_result/0","doc":"Result of executing a single task.\n\n* `{:ok, actor}` - Success with updated actor state\n* `{:error, reason}` - Failure with reason atom or tuple","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#t:task_result/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Executor.execute_primitive/4","doc":"Execute a primitive's run function.\n\nHandles the complexity of extracting and compiling the run function from\nthe primitive's metadata.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#execute_primitive/4"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Executor.execute_primitive/4","doc":"* `primitive` - The primitive Task struct from the registry\n* `actor` - Current actor state\n* `facts` - Current world state\n* `args` - Arguments from the task tuple (default: [])","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#execute_primitive/4-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Executor.execute_primitive/4","doc":"* `{:ok, updated_actor}` - Execution succeeded\n* `{:error, reason}` - Execution failed","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#execute_primitive/4-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Executor.execute_primitive/4","doc":"primitive = Registry.get_primitive(:fire_weapon)\n    {:ok, updated_soldier} = Executor.execute_primitive(primitive, soldier, facts)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#execute_primitive/4-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Notes - Operator.HTN.Executor.execute_primitive/4","doc":"The run function in primitives is stored as quoted AST in `primitive.metadata.run`.\nThis function handles compiling and invoking it. If the run function is already\ncompiled (a function reference), it's called directly.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#execute_primitive/4-notes"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Executor.execute_task/4","doc":"Execute a single task tuple.\n\nLooks up the primitive in the registry and executes its run function.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#execute_task/4"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Executor.execute_task/4","doc":"* `task_tuple` - Tuple of `{task_name, args}`\n* `actor` - Current actor state\n* `facts` - Current world state\n* `opts` - Options (reserved for future use)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#execute_task/4-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Executor.execute_task/4","doc":"* `{:ok, updated_actor, updated_facts}` - Task succeeded\n* `{:error, reason}` - Task failed","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#execute_task/4-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Executor.execute_task/4","doc":"case Executor.execute_task({:attack, [:enemy_1]}, warrior, facts) do\n      {:ok, warrior, facts} ->\n        IO.puts(\"Attack successful!\")\n\n      {:error, :primitive_not_found} ->\n        IO.puts(\"No :attack primitive defined\")\n\n      {:error, {:execution_failed, :no_ammo}} ->\n        IO.puts(\"Out of ammo!\")\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#execute_task/4-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Executor.execution_effects/1","doc":"Get the effects that should be applied after successful task execution.\n\nReturns only `:plan_and_execute` and `:permanent` effects (excludes `:plan_only`).","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#execution_effects/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Executor.execution_effects/1","doc":"* `task` - The Task struct","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#execution_effects/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Executor.execution_effects/1","doc":"List of Effect structs to apply.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#execution_effects/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Executor.execution_effects/1","doc":"primitive = Registry.get_primitive(:unlock_door)\n    effects = Executor.execution_effects(primitive)\n    # => [%Effect{type: :plan_and_execute, key: {:world, :door_locked}, value: false}]\n\n    updated_facts = Effect.apply_all(effects, facts)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#execution_effects/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Executor.run_plan/4","doc":"Execute an entire plan to completion.\n\nRuns all tasks in sequence until either the plan completes or a task fails.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#run_plan/4"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Executor.run_plan/4","doc":"* `plan` - The plan to execute\n* `actor` - Initial actor state\n* `facts` - Initial world state\n* `opts` - Options:\n  * `:on_task_complete` - Callback `fn task_tuple, actor, facts -> :ok end`\n  * `:max_steps` - Maximum tasks to execute (default: 1000)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#run_plan/4-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Executor.run_plan/4","doc":"* `{:ok, final_actor, final_facts}` - All tasks completed\n* `{:error, reason, actor, facts, remaining_plan}` - Failed mid-execution","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#run_plan/4-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Executor.run_plan/4","doc":"{:ok, plan} = Planner.run(:build_house, facts, traits)\n\n    case Executor.run_plan(plan, builder, facts) do\n      {:ok, builder, facts} ->\n        IO.puts(\"House built!\")\n\n      {:error, :no_materials, builder, facts, remaining} ->\n        IO.puts(\"Ran out of materials with #{Plan.task_count(remaining)} tasks left\")\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#run_plan/4-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Executor.step/4","doc":"Execute a single step of a plan.\n\nPops the next task from the plan, executes it, and returns the result\nalong with the remaining plan.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#step/4"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Executor.step/4","doc":"* `plan` - The plan to execute\n* `actor` - Current actor state (passed to primitive run functions)\n* `facts` - Current world state\n* `opts` - Options (currently unused, reserved for future use)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#step/4-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Executor.step/4","doc":"* `{:ok, :completed, actor, facts, plan}` - No more tasks, plan complete\n* `{:ok, :continue, actor, facts, remaining_plan}` - Task succeeded, more remain\n* `{:error, reason, actor, facts, plan}` - Task failed","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#step/4-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Executor.step/4","doc":"{:ok, plan} = Planner.run(:patrol, facts, traits)\n\n    case Executor.step(plan, npc, facts) do\n      {:ok, :completed, npc, facts, _plan} ->\n        IO.puts(\"Patrol complete!\")\n        {npc, facts}\n\n      {:ok, :continue, npc, facts, remaining} ->\n        # Store remaining plan for next tick\n        {%{npc | plan: remaining}, facts}\n\n      {:error, :primitive_not_found, npc, facts, plan} ->\n        IO.puts(\"Missing primitive - aborting plan\")\n        {%{npc | plan: nil}, facts}\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.Executor.html#step/4-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.HTN.Facts","doc":"World state representation for HTN planning.\n\nFacts represent an agent's knowledge about the world, organized into three\ncategories:\n\n* **self** - Agent's internal state (health, inventory, abilities)\n* **world** - Environmental knowledge (locations, objects, conditions)\n* **social** - Relationships and knowledge about other agents","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Creating Facts - Operator.HTN.Facts","doc":"The primary way to create facts is from a perception map:\n\n    facts = Facts.from_perception(%{\n      self: %{\n        health: 100,\n        position: {10, 20},\n        inventory: [:keycard, :pistol]\n      },\n      world: %{\n        time_of_day: :night,\n        alarm_active: false,\n        guards_nearby: 2\n      },\n      social: %{\n        faction_standing: %{corp: -50, runners: 80}\n      }\n    })","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#module-creating-facts"},{"type":"module","title":"Querying Facts - Operator.HTN.Facts","doc":"Use `has?/2` to check for existence and `get/3` to retrieve values:\n\n    Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :keycard})\n    #=> true (checks if key exists in self map)\n\n    Facts.get(facts, {:self, :health}, 0)\n    #=> 100\n\n    Facts.get(facts, {:world, :alarm_active}, true)\n    #=> false","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#module-querying-facts"},{"type":"module","title":"Modifying Facts (During Planning) - Operator.HTN.Facts","doc":"Facts are immutable. Modifications return new fact structs:\n\n    updated = Facts.put(facts, {:self, :health}, 80)\n    updated = Facts.merge(facts, %{self: %{ammo: 30}})\n\nThis immutability is crucial for HTN planning - the planner can explore\ndifferent branches without corrupting shared state.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#module-modifying-facts-during-planning"},{"type":"module","title":"Fact Keys - Operator.HTN.Facts","doc":"Keys are always tuples of `{category, path}` where:\n\n* `category` is `:self`, `:world`, or `:social`\n* `path` is an atom or nested key path","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#module-fact-keys"},{"type":"module","title":"Integration with Preconditions - Operator.HTN.Facts","doc":"Facts are passed to precondition functions during planning:\n\n    goal :attack do\n      precond fn facts ->\n        Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :weapon}) and\n        Facts.get(facts, {:self, :ammo}, 0) > 0\n      end\n      # ...\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#module-integration-with-preconditions"},{"type":"module","title":"See Also - Operator.HTN.Facts","doc":"* `Operator.HTN.Effect` - Modifying facts during planning\n* `Operator.HTN.Plan` - Plans generated from facts\n* `Operator.HTN.Precondition` - Logical operators on facts","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#module-see-also"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Facts.category/0","doc":"The category of a fact.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#t:category/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Facts.fact_key/0","doc":"A fact key specifying category and path.\n\nCategories:\n* `:self` - Agent's internal state\n* `:world` - Environmental knowledge\n* `:social` - Relationship data","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#t:fact_key/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Facts.fact_key/0","doc":"{:self, :health}\n    {:world, :door_locked}\n    {:social, :faction_standing}","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#t:fact_key/0-examples"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Facts.t/0","doc":"The Facts struct containing agent world knowledge.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Fields - Operator.HTN.Facts.t/0","doc":"* `:self` - Map of agent's internal state\n* `:world` - Map of environmental knowledge\n* `:social` - Map of relationship/social knowledge","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#t:t/0-fields"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Facts.delete/2","doc":"Delete a fact key, returning a new Facts struct.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#delete/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Facts.delete/2","doc":"* `facts` - The Facts struct\n* `key` - Tuple of `{category, path}` to delete","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#delete/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Facts.delete/2","doc":"iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{health: 100, mana: 50}})\n    iex> updated = Facts.delete(facts, {:self, :mana})\n    iex> Facts.has?(updated, {:self, :mana})\n    false\n    iex> Facts.get(updated, {:self, :health})\n    100","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#delete/2-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Facts.from_perception/1","doc":"Create facts from a perception map.\n\nThis is the primary constructor for Facts. The perception map should contain\nkeys for `:self`, `:world`, and/or `:social`.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#from_perception/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Facts.from_perception/1","doc":"* `perception` - Map with optional `:self`, `:world`, `:social` keys","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#from_perception/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Facts.from_perception/1","doc":"iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{ready: true}})\n    iex> Facts.get(facts, {:self, :ready})\n    true\n\n    iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{\n    ...>   self: %{hp: 100, mp: 50},\n    ...>   world: %{location: :town}\n    ...> })\n    iex> Facts.get(facts, {:world, :location})\n    :town","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#from_perception/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Empty Facts - Operator.HTN.Facts.from_perception/1","doc":"iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{})\n    iex> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :anything})\n    false","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#from_perception/1-empty-facts"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Facts.get/3","doc":"Get a fact value with an optional default.\n\nReturns the value at the given key, or the default if the key doesn't exist.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#get/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Facts.get/3","doc":"* `facts` - The Facts struct\n* `key` - Tuple of `{category, path}`\n* `default` - Value to return if key doesn't exist (default: `nil`)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#get/3-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Facts.get/3","doc":"iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{health: 100}})\n    iex> Facts.get(facts, {:self, :health})\n    100\n\n    iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{}})\n    iex> Facts.get(facts, {:self, :health}, 0)\n    0\n\n    iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{world: %{enemies: [:goblin, :orc]}})\n    iex> Facts.get(facts, {:world, :enemies}, [])\n    [:goblin, :orc]","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#get/3-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Facts.has?/2","doc":"Check if a fact key exists (has a value, even if nil).\n\nReturns `true` if the key exists in the appropriate category map,\nregardless of the value.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#has?/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Facts.has?/2","doc":"* `facts` - The Facts struct\n* `key` - Tuple of `{category, path}`","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#has?/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Facts.has?/2","doc":"iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{weapon: :sword}})\n    iex> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :weapon})\n    true\n\n    # Key exists, even though value is nil\n    iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{weapon: nil}})\n    iex> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :weapon})\n    true\n\n    iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{}})\n    iex> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :weapon})\n    false","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#has?/2-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Facts.merge/2","doc":"Merge additional facts into the existing struct.\n\nPerforms a shallow merge of each category.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#merge/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Facts.merge/2","doc":"* `facts` - The Facts struct\n* `additional` - Map with `:self`, `:world`, and/or `:social` keys","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#merge/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Facts.merge/2","doc":"iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{health: 100}})\n    iex> updated = Facts.merge(facts, %{self: %{mana: 50}, world: %{zone: :forest}})\n    iex> Facts.get(updated, {:self, :mana})\n    50\n    iex> Facts.get(updated, {:world, :zone})\n    :forest","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#merge/2-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Facts.missing_keys/2","doc":"Return the list of missing fact keys from a required set.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#missing_keys/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Facts.missing_keys/2","doc":"iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{ready: true}})\n    iex> Facts.missing_keys(facts, [{:self, :ready}, {:world, :time}])\n    [{:world, :time}]","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#missing_keys/2-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Facts.new/0","doc":"Create an empty Facts struct.\n\nThis is a convenience alias for `from_perception(%{})`.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#new/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Facts.new/0","doc":"iex> facts = Facts.new()\n    iex> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :anything})\n    false","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#new/0-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Facts.put/3","doc":"Set a fact value, returning a new Facts struct.\n\nThis is used during planning to simulate effects of actions.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#put/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Facts.put/3","doc":"* `facts` - The Facts struct\n* `key` - Tuple of `{category, path}`\n* `value` - The new value to set","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#put/3-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Facts.put/3","doc":"iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{health: 100}})\n    iex> updated = Facts.put(facts, {:self, :health}, 80)\n    iex> Facts.get(updated, {:self, :health})\n    80\n    iex> Facts.get(facts, {:self, :health})\n    100","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#put/3-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Facts.to_map/1","doc":"Convert facts to a flat map representation.\n\nUseful for debugging and logging.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#to_map/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Facts.to_map/1","doc":"iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{hp: 100}, world: %{zone: :a}})\n    iex> Facts.to_map(facts)\n    %{self: %{hp: 100}, world: %{zone: :a}, social: %{}}","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#to_map/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Facts.validate_required/2","doc":"Validate that all required fact keys exist.\n\nReturns `:ok` when all keys exist, otherwise returns `{:error, missing_keys}`.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#validate_required/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Facts.validate_required/2","doc":"iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{ready: true}})\n    iex> Facts.validate_required(facts, [{:self, :ready}])\n    :ok\n\n    iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{ready: true}})\n    iex> Facts.validate_required(facts, [{:self, :ready}, {:world, :time}])\n    {:error, [{:world, :time}]}","ref":"Operator.HTN.Facts.html#validate_required/2-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector","doc":"Automatic goal selection for agents based on world state and personality.\n\nThe GoalSelector answers the question \"What should this NPC do right now?\"\nby evaluating all registered goals and picking the best match based on:\n\n1. **Preconditions** - Goals whose preconditions fail are filtered out\n2. **Base priority** - From goal metadata (`:priority` key)\n3. **Trait affinity** - How well agent traits match the goal\n4. **Archetype affinity** - Class/role bonuses (warrior prefers combat, etc.)\n5. **World context** - Environmental modifiers (tension, location type)","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Scoring Formula - Operator.HTN.GoalSelector","doc":"```\nscore = base_priority\n      + config_trait_bonus      # From :htn_trait_weights config\n      + metadata_trait_score    # From goal metadata trait_weights\n      + archetype_score         # From goal metadata archetype_weights\n      + world_context_bonus     # Based on tension and land_use\n      + priority_bonus          # From options\n```","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#module-scoring-formula"},{"type":"module","title":"Basic Usage - Operator.HTN.GoalSelector","doc":"facts = Facts.from_perception(%{\n      self: %{health: 80, armed: true},\n      world: %{tension: 0.7, land_use: :corporate}\n    })\n\n    traits = %{\n      archetype: :street_sam,\n      traits: [:aggressive, :territorial]\n    }\n\n    case GoalSelector.pick_goal(facts, traits) do\n      {:ok, goal_name} ->\n        Planner.run(goal_name, facts, traits)\n\n      :none ->\n        # No eligible goals - agent idles\n        :idle\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#module-basic-usage"},{"type":"module","title":"Goal Metadata for Selection - Operator.HTN.GoalSelector","doc":"Goals can include metadata that influences selection:\n\n    goal :attack_enemy do\n      precond fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:world, :enemy_visible}) end\n\n      decompose do\n        task :engage\n      end\n\n      metadata(\n        priority: 8,                           # Base priority\n        domain: :combat,                       # World context domain\n        required_traits: [:aggressive],        # Must have one of these\n        trait_weights: %{aggressive: 2},       # Bonus for traits\n        archetype_weights: %{warrior: 3}       # Bonus for archetypes\n      )\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#module-goal-metadata-for-selection"},{"type":"module","title":"Configuration - Operator.HTN.GoalSelector","doc":"Global trait-goal weights can be configured:\n\n    config :operator,\n      htn_trait_weights: %{\n        {:aggressive, :attack} => 5,\n        {:cautious, :scout} => 3,\n        {:greedy, :loot} => 4\n      }","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#module-configuration"},{"type":"module","title":"Tie-Breaking - Operator.HTN.GoalSelector","doc":"When goals have equal scores, you can provide a deterministic order:\n\n    GoalSelector.pick_goal(facts, traits,\n      goal_order: [:defend, :patrol, :idle]\n    )\n\nGoals in the list are preferred over goals not in the list.","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#module-tie-breaking"},{"type":"module","title":"Debugging Selection - Operator.HTN.GoalSelector","doc":"Use `score_goal/4` to understand why a goal was or wasn't selected:\n\n    GoalSelector.score_goal(:attack, facts, traits)\n    #=> 12.5\n\n    GoalSelector.score_goal(:flee, facts, traits)\n    #=> 8.0","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#module-debugging-selection"},{"type":"module","title":"World Context Bonuses - Operator.HTN.GoalSelector","doc":"The selector applies environmental modifiers based on domain and location:\n\n| Domain     | Location    | Tension Multiplier |\n|------------|-------------|-------------------|\n| :security  | :corporate  | 0.5               |\n| :security  | :industrial | 0.4               |\n| :street    | :barrens    | 0.6               |\n| :street    | :mixed      | 0.3               |\n| (other)    | (other)     | 0.1               |","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#module-world-context-bonuses"},{"type":"module","title":"See Also - Operator.HTN.GoalSelector","doc":"* `Operator.HTN.Planner` - Generates plans for selected goals\n* `Operator.Traits` - Trait/archetype system\n* `Operator.Telemetry` - Goal selection events","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#module-see-also"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.explain/3","doc":"Explain goal selection with scores and eligibility.\n\nReturns a map with the selected goal, eligible/ineligible goals, and\nscoring details. This is intended for debugging and UI tooling.","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#explain/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Example - Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.explain/3","doc":"result = GoalSelector.explain(facts, traits)\n    result.selected\n    #=> :patrol\n\n    Enum.map(result.eligible, & &1.goal)\n    #=> [:patrol, :idle]","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#explain/3-example"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.pick_goal/3","doc":"Selects the highest-priority eligible goal for an agent.\n\nEvaluates all registered goals, filters by preconditions and trait\nrequirements, scores the remainder, and returns the best match.","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#pick_goal/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.pick_goal/3","doc":"* `facts` - Current world state (`Facts.t()`)\n* `traits` - Agent traits/genome map\n* `opts` - Options (see below)","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#pick_goal/3-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.pick_goal/3","doc":"* `:trait_weights` - Map of `{trait, goal}` to integer bonuses.\n  Overrides the global `:htn_trait_weights` config.\n* `:goal_order` - List of goal atoms for deterministic tie-breaking.\n  Goals earlier in the list win ties.\n* `:priority_bonus` - Scalar added to every goal's score.","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#pick_goal/3-options"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.pick_goal/3","doc":"* `{:ok, goal_name}` - The highest-scoring eligible goal\n* `:none` - No goals passed preconditions","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#pick_goal/3-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.pick_goal/3","doc":"# Basic usage\n    case GoalSelector.pick_goal(facts, traits) do\n      {:ok, :patrol} -> Planner.run(:patrol, facts, traits)\n      :none -> :idle\n    end\n\n    # With options\n    GoalSelector.pick_goal(facts, traits,\n      trait_weights: %{{:aggressive, :attack} => 10},\n      goal_order: [:defend, :attack, :patrol],\n      priority_bonus: 2\n    )","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#pick_goal/3-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Telemetry - Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.pick_goal/3","doc":"Emits `Telemetry.emit_goal_selected/3` with the selected goal and score.","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#pick_goal/3-telemetry"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.score_goal/4","doc":"Score a specific goal for an agent without selecting it.\n\nUseful for debugging goal selection or building custom selection logic.","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#score_goal/4"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.score_goal/4","doc":"* `goal_name` - The goal atom to score\n* `facts` - Current world state\n* `traits` - Agent traits/genome\n* `opts` - Same options as `pick_goal/3`","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#score_goal/4-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.score_goal/4","doc":"* `number()` - The computed score\n* `nil` - Goal not found in registry","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#score_goal/4-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.score_goal/4","doc":"# Debug why one goal beats another\n    attack_score = GoalSelector.score_goal(:attack, facts, traits)\n    #=> 12.5\n\n    flee_score = GoalSelector.score_goal(:flee, facts, traits)\n    #=> 8.0\n\n    # Attack wins because aggressive trait gives +5 bonus","ref":"Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.html#score_goal/4-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.HTN.Loop","doc":"Convenience helpers for integrating HTN planning into tick-based loops.\n\nThe goal is to reduce boilerplate: plan if needed, execute one step, and\nreturn a structured result.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Loop.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Example - Operator.HTN.Loop","doc":"alias Operator.HTN.{Facts, Loop}\n\n    facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{energy: 50}})\n    traits = %{archetype: :guard}\n\n    result = Loop.tick(nil, actor, facts, traits,\n      goal: :patrol\n    )\n\n    case result.status do\n      :idle -> :no_plan\n      :continue -> result.plan\n      :completed -> :done\n      :failed -> result.reason\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.Loop.html#module-example"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Loop.result/0","doc":"","ref":"Operator.HTN.Loop.html#t:result/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Loop.status/0","doc":"","ref":"Operator.HTN.Loop.html#t:status/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Loop.tick/5","doc":"Tick the AI loop once.\n\n- If there is no plan (or it needs replan), a new plan is created.\n- If no goal is available, returns `:idle`.\n- Otherwise, executes one step of the plan.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Loop.html#tick/5"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - Operator.HTN.Loop.tick/5","doc":"- `:goal` - specific goal atom to plan for (skips goal selection)\n- `:select_goal` - custom goal selector (default: `GoalSelector.pick_goal/2`)\n- `:planner_opts` - options passed to `Planner.run/4` (budgets, etc.)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Loop.html#tick/5-options"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.HTN.Plan","doc":"Represents a generated plan from HTN expansion.\n\nA Plan is the output of the HTN planning process - a sequence of primitive\ntasks that, when executed in order, should achieve the original goal.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Plan Structure - Operator.HTN.Plan","doc":"%Plan{\n      goal: :acquire_data,\n      tasks: [\n        {:move_to, [:server_room]},\n        {:hack_terminal, [\"mainframe\"]},\n        {:download, [:target_file]}\n      ],\n      validity: :active,\n      created_at: 1699999999,\n      metadata: %{estimated_cost: 15.0}\n    }","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#module-plan-structure"},{"type":"module","title":"Plan Lifecycle - Operator.HTN.Plan","doc":"Plans have a validity state that tracks their lifecycle:\n\n* `:active` - Plan is valid and can be executed\n* `:invalid` - Plan is no longer valid (world changed)\n* `:completed` - All tasks have been executed","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#module-plan-lifecycle"},{"type":"module","title":"Usage - Operator.HTN.Plan","doc":"","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#module-usage"},{"type":"module","title":"Creating Plans - Operator.HTN.Plan","doc":"Plans are typically created by the Engine or Planner:\n\n    {:ok, plan} = Operator.HTN.Planner.run(:my_goal, facts, traits)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#module-creating-plans"},{"type":"module","title":"Executing Plans - Operator.HTN.Plan","doc":"case Plan.next_task(plan) do\n      {{:move_to, [location]}, remaining_plan} ->\n        execute_move(location)\n        # Continue with remaining_plan\n\n      :empty ->\n        Plan.complete(plan)\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#module-executing-plans"},{"type":"module","title":"Invalidation - Operator.HTN.Plan","doc":"Plans should be invalidated when the world changes in ways that affect\npreconditions:\n\n    plan = Plan.invalidate(plan)\n    # plan.validity is now :invalid","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#module-invalidation"},{"type":"module","title":"Metadata - Operator.HTN.Plan","doc":"Plans can carry arbitrary metadata for debugging, cost tracking, or\nintegration with external systems:\n\n    plan = Plan.add_metadata(plan, :source, \"GoalSelector\")\n    plan = Plan.add_metadata(plan, :planning_time_ms, 5)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#module-metadata"},{"type":"module","title":"See Also - Operator.HTN.Plan","doc":"* `Operator.HTN.Engine` - Generates plans\n* `Operator.HTN.Planner` - High-level planning API\n* `Operator.HTN.Task` - Individual task definitions","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#module-see-also"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Plan.t/0","doc":"The Plan struct.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Fields - Operator.HTN.Plan.t/0","doc":"* `:goal` - The goal this plan achieves\n* `:tasks` - List of primitive task tuples\n* `:validity` - Current plan validity\n* `:created_at` - Unix timestamp of creation\n* `:metadata` - Arbitrary metadata map","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#t:t/0-fields"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Plan.task_tuple/0","doc":"A task tuple with name and arguments.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#t:task_tuple/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Plan.task_tuple/0","doc":"{:move_to, [:lobby]}\n    {:attack, [:enemy_1, :melee]}\n    {:wait, [5000]}","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#t:task_tuple/0-examples"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Plan.validity/0","doc":"Plan validity states.\n\n* `:active` - Plan is valid and executable\n* `:invalid` - Plan preconditions no longer hold\n* `:completed` - All tasks have been executed","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#t:validity/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Plan.add_metadata/3","doc":"Add metadata to a plan.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#add_metadata/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Plan.add_metadata/3","doc":"iex> plan = Plan.new(:test, [])\n    iex> plan = Plan.add_metadata(plan, :source, \"manual\")\n    iex> plan.metadata.source\n    \"manual\"","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#add_metadata/3-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Plan.complete/1","doc":"Mark a plan as completed.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#complete/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Plan.complete/1","doc":"iex> plan = Plan.new(:test, [])\n    iex> completed = Plan.complete(plan)\n    iex> completed.validity\n    :completed","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#complete/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Plan.get_metadata/3","doc":"Get metadata value from a plan.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#get_metadata/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Plan.get_metadata/3","doc":"iex> plan = Plan.new(:test, [], metadata: %{priority: 5})\n    iex> Plan.get_metadata(plan, :priority)\n    5\n\n    iex> plan = Plan.new(:test, [], metadata: %{priority: 5})\n    iex> Plan.get_metadata(plan, :missing, :default)\n    :default","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#get_metadata/3-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Plan.has_tasks?/1","doc":"Check if the plan has remaining tasks.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#has_tasks?/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Plan.has_tasks?/1","doc":"iex> plan = Plan.new(:test, [{:task, []}])\n    iex> Plan.has_tasks?(plan)\n    true\n\n    iex> empty = Plan.new(:test, [])\n    iex> Plan.has_tasks?(empty)\n    false","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#has_tasks?/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Plan.invalidate/1","doc":"Mark a plan as invalid.\n\nUse this when world state changes in a way that invalidates plan\npreconditions.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#invalidate/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Plan.invalidate/1","doc":"iex> plan = Plan.new(:test, [{:task, []}])\n    iex> invalid = Plan.invalidate(plan)\n    iex> invalid.validity\n    :invalid","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#invalidate/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Plan.new/3","doc":"Create a new plan.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#new/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Plan.new/3","doc":"* `goal` - The goal atom this plan achieves\n* `tasks` - List of `{task_name, args}` tuples\n* `opts` - Optional keyword list:\n  * `:metadata` - Initial metadata map\n  * `:validity` - Initial validity (default: `:active`)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#new/3-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Plan.new/3","doc":"iex> plan = Plan.new(:patrol, [{:walk_to, [:waypoint_1]}, {:scan, []}])\n    iex> plan.goal\n    :patrol\n    iex> plan.validity\n    :active\n\n    iex> plan = Plan.new(:attack, [{:strike, []}], metadata: %{priority: :high})\n    iex> plan.metadata.priority\n    :high","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#new/3-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Plan.next_task/1","doc":"Get the next task to execute.\n\nReturns `{task_tuple, remaining_plan}` or `:empty` if no tasks remain.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#next_task/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Plan.next_task/1","doc":"iex> plan = Plan.new(:test, [{:a, []}, {:b, [1]}])\n    iex> {{:a, []}, remaining} = Plan.next_task(plan)\n    iex> remaining.tasks\n    [{:b, [1]}]\n\n    iex> empty_plan = Plan.new(:test, [])\n    iex> Plan.next_task(empty_plan)\n    :empty","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#next_task/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Plan.task_count/1","doc":"Get the number of remaining tasks.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#task_count/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Plan.task_count/1","doc":"iex> plan = Plan.new(:test, [{:a, []}, {:b, []}, {:c, []}])\n    iex> Plan.task_count(plan)\n    3","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#task_count/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Plan.valid?/1","doc":"Check if plan is still valid for execution.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#valid?/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Plan.valid?/1","doc":"iex> plan = Plan.new(:test, [])\n    iex> Plan.valid?(plan)\n    true\n\n    iex> plan = Plan.new(:test, [])\n    iex> invalid = Plan.invalidate(plan)\n    iex> Plan.valid?(invalid)\n    false","ref":"Operator.HTN.Plan.html#valid?/1-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.HTN.Planner","doc":"High-level API for HTN plan generation.\n\nThe Planner is your primary interface for generating plans. It wraps the\nEngine with telemetry, rationalization, and convenience functions for\ntick-based game loops.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Basic Usage - Operator.HTN.Planner","doc":"alias Operator.HTN.{Facts, Planner}\n\n    facts = Facts.from_perception(%{\n      self: %{location: :lobby, has_keycard: true},\n      world: %{target: :server_room, threat_level: :low}\n    })\n\n    traits = %{archetype: :infiltrator, traits: [:stealthy, :tech_savvy]}\n\n    case Planner.run(:infiltrate_building, facts, traits) do\n      {:ok, plan} ->\n        IO.inspect(plan.tasks)\n        # => [{:move_to, [:server_room]}, {:hack_terminal, []}, {:download_data, []}]\n\n      {:error, :preconditions_not_met} ->\n        # Goal preconditions not satisfied - wait or choose different goal\n        :retry_later\n\n      {:error, :goal_not_found} ->\n        # Goal not registered - check your DSL module\n        :unknown_goal\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#module-basic-usage"},{"type":"module","title":"Integration with Game Loops - Operator.HTN.Planner","doc":"For continuous simulations, the Planner provides tick-based helpers:\n\n    defmodule MyGame.AISystem do\n      alias Operator.HTN.{Executor, Facts, Planner}\n\n      def update(entity, world) do\n        facts = build_facts(entity, world)\n        traits = entity.genome\n\n        case entity.plan do\n          nil ->\n            # No plan - generate one\n            plan = Planner.tick(nil, facts, traits, :default_goal)\n            %{entity | plan: plan}\n\n          plan ->\n            # Have plan - check if still valid, execute or replan\n            if Planner.needs_replan?(plan, facts) do\n              new_plan = Planner.tick(plan, facts, traits, :default_goal)\n              %{entity | plan: new_plan}\n            else\n              # Execute current plan\n              case Executor.step(plan, entity, facts) do\n                {:ok, :completed, entity, _facts, _plan} ->\n                  %{entity | plan: nil}\n\n                {:ok, :continue, entity, _facts, remaining} ->\n                  %{entity | plan: remaining}\n\n                {:error, _reason, entity, _facts, _plan} ->\n                  %{entity | plan: nil}  # Will replan next tick\n              end\n            end\n        end\n      end\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#module-integration-with-game-loops"},{"type":"module","title":"What Happens During Planning - Operator.HTN.Planner","doc":"1. **Goal lookup** - Find the goal in the Registry\n2. **Precondition check** - Verify goal preconditions pass\n3. **Decomposition** - Expand goal into task sequence\n4. **Recursive expansion** - Expand abstract tasks into primitives\n5. **Effect simulation** - Apply effects to working facts copy\n6. **Annotation** - Add narrative metadata via Rationalization\n7. **Telemetry** - Emit planning metrics","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#module-what-happens-during-planning"},{"type":"module","title":"Telemetry Events - Operator.HTN.Planner","doc":"Each successful `run/3` emits `Telemetry.emit_htn_plan_generated/3` with:\n- Goal name\n- Task count\n- Planning duration (ms)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#module-telemetry-events"},{"type":"module","title":"See Also - Operator.HTN.Planner","doc":"* `Operator.HTN.Engine` - Low-level expansion logic\n* `Operator.HTN.Executor` - Running generated plans\n* `Operator.HTN.GoalSelector` - Automatic goal selection\n* `Operator.HTN.Plan` - The plan data structure","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#module-see-also"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Planner.explain/3","doc":"Explain plan generation for a specific goal.\n\nReturns a structured map for debugging or UI tooling. Unlike tracing,\nthis gives you a deterministic, inspectable payload.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#explain/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Example - Operator.HTN.Planner.explain/3","doc":"result = Planner.explain(:patrol, facts, traits)\n    result.result\n    #=> :ok\n\n    result.plan.tasks\n    #=> [{:move_to, [:waypoint_1]}, {:look_around, []}]","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#explain/3-example"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Planner.needs_replan?/2","doc":"Check if a plan needs replanning.\n\nReturns `true` if the plan is missing, invalid, or completed.\nUse this to decide whether to call `run/3` or continue with\nthe current plan.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#needs_replan?/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Planner.needs_replan?/2","doc":"* `plan` - Current plan (or `nil`)\n* `facts` - Current world state (reserved for future validation)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#needs_replan?/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Planner.needs_replan?/2","doc":"* `true` - Plan is `nil`, `:invalid`, or `:completed`\n* `false` - Plan is `:active` and ready for execution","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#needs_replan?/2-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Planner.needs_replan?/2","doc":"Planner.needs_replan?(nil, facts)\n    #=> true\n\n    active_plan = Plan.new(:goal, [{:task, []}])\n    Planner.needs_replan?(active_plan, facts)\n    #=> false\n\n    completed = Plan.complete(active_plan)\n    Planner.needs_replan?(completed, facts)\n    #=> true","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#needs_replan?/2-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Planner.run/4","doc":"Generate a plan for a goal.\n\nThis is the primary planning function. It expands the goal into a sequence\nof primitive tasks, annotates the plan with narrative metadata, and emits\ntelemetry.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#run/4"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Planner.run/4","doc":"* `goal_name` - The goal atom to plan for (must be registered)\n* `facts` - Current world state (`Facts.t()`)\n* `traits` - Agent traits/genome map for cost heuristics","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#run/4-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Planner.run/4","doc":"* `{:ok, plan}` - Successfully generated plan with tasks\n* `{:error, :goal_not_found}` - Goal not in Registry\n* `{:error, :preconditions_not_met}` - Goal preconditions failed\n* `{:error, {:budget_exceeded, reason}}` - Planning exceeded configured budget","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#run/4-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Planner.run/4","doc":"# Successful planning\n    {:ok, plan} = Planner.run(:patrol, facts, traits)\n    plan.tasks\n    #=> [{:walk_to, [:waypoint_1]}, {:scan, []}, {:walk_to, [:waypoint_2]}]\n\n    # Goal doesn't exist\n    {:error, :goal_not_found} = Planner.run(:nonexistent, facts, traits)\n\n    # Preconditions failed (e.g., attack requires weapon)\n    facts_unarmed = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{armed: false}})\n    {:error, :preconditions_not_met} = Planner.run(:attack, facts_unarmed, traits)\n\n    # Budgeted planning\n    Planner.run(:patrol, facts, traits, budget: [max_tasks: 50, timeout_ms: 5])","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#run/4-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Planner.run_with_registry/5","doc":"Generate a plan using a specific registry.\n\nPrimarily useful for testing with isolated registries or when you need\nto plan against a subset of behaviors.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#run_with_registry/5"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Planner.run_with_registry/5","doc":"* `goal_name` - The goal atom to plan for\n* `facts` - Current world state\n* `traits` - Agent traits/genome\n* `htn_registry` - Registry map (from `Registry.all()` or custom)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#run_with_registry/5-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Planner.run_with_registry/5","doc":"Same as `run/3`.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#run_with_registry/5-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Planner.run_with_registry/5","doc":"# Testing with isolated registry\n    test \"my goal generates correct plan\" do\n      registry = %{\n        goals: %{test_goal: %{name: :test_goal, decompose: ...}},\n        tasks: %{},\n        primitives: %{test_action: %Task{...}},\n        axioms: %{}\n      }\n\n      {:ok, plan} = Planner.run_with_registry(:test_goal, facts, %{}, registry)\n      assert [{:test_action, []}] = plan.tasks\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#run_with_registry/5-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Planner.tick/4","doc":"Update or create a plan on each game tick.\n\nConvenience function for tick-based game loops. Handles the common pattern\nof \"create plan if none exists, replan if invalid, keep if valid\".","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#tick/4"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Planner.tick/4","doc":"* `plan` - Current plan (or `nil` if none)\n* `facts` - Current world state\n* `traits` - Agent traits/genome\n* `goal_name` - Goal to plan for if replanning needed","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#tick/4-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Planner.tick/4","doc":"* `%Plan{}` - The current or newly generated plan\n* `nil` - Planning failed and no valid plan exists","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#tick/4-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Behavior - Operator.HTN.Planner.tick/4","doc":"| Current Plan | Plan Valid? | Result                    |\n|--------------|-------------|---------------------------|\n| `nil`        | N/A         | Generate new plan         |\n| `%Plan{}`    | Yes         | Return existing plan      |\n| `%Plan{}`    | No          | Generate new plan         |","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#tick/4-behavior"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Planner.tick/4","doc":"# In your game loop\n    def update_ai(entity, world) do\n      facts = build_facts(entity, world)\n      plan = Planner.tick(entity.plan, facts, entity.traits, :default_goal)\n      %{entity | plan: plan}\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.Planner.html#tick/4-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.HTN.Precondition","doc":"Logical operators for HTN preconditions.\n\nInspired by the Decima engine's HTN implementation, this module provides\nlogical combinators for preconditions beyond simple conjunction (AND).","ref":"Operator.HTN.Precondition.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Supported Operators - Operator.HTN.Precondition","doc":"- `:all` (AND) - All conditions must be true (default behavior)\n- `:any` (OR) - At least one condition must be true\n- `:first` (ALT) - Use first matching condition with preference order\n- `:not` - Negate a condition\n- `:none` - No conditions match (equivalent to not-any)\n- `:axiom` - Reference a registered axiom","ref":"Operator.HTN.Precondition.html#module-supported-operators"},{"type":"module","title":"Usage - Operator.HTN.Precondition","doc":"Preconditions can be:\n- A simple function: `fn facts -> boolean end`\n- A tuple with operator: `{:any, [fn1, fn2, fn3]}`\n- Nested operators: `{:all, [fn1, {:any, [fn2, fn3]}]}`\n- An axiom reference: `{:axiom, :axiom_name}` or `{:axiom, :axiom_name, args}`","ref":"Operator.HTN.Precondition.html#module-usage"},{"type":"module","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Precondition","doc":"iex> alias Operator.HTN.{Facts, Precondition}\n    iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{has_weapon: true}})\n    iex> cond = {:any, [\n    ...>   fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :has_weapon}) end,\n    ...>   fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:world, :weapon_nearby}) end\n    ...> ]}\n    iex> Precondition.satisfied?(cond, facts, %{})\n    true\n\n    iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{has_melee_weapon: true}})\n    iex> cond = {:first, [\n    ...>   fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :has_ranged_weapon}) end,\n    ...>   fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :has_melee_weapon}) end\n    ...> ]}\n    iex> Precondition.satisfied?(cond, facts, %{})\n    true\n\n    iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{in_combat: false}})\n    iex> cond = {:not, fn facts -> Facts.get(facts, {:self, :in_combat}, false) end}\n    iex> Precondition.satisfied?(cond, facts, %{})\n    true\n\n    iex> facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{has_cover: true, has_grenade: true}})\n    iex> cond = {:all, [\n    ...>   fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :has_cover}) end,\n    ...>   {:any, [\n    ...>     fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :has_weapon}) end,\n    ...>     fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :has_grenade}) end\n    ...>   ]}\n    ...> ]}\n    iex> Precondition.satisfied?(cond, facts, %{})\n    true","ref":"Operator.HTN.Precondition.html#module-examples"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Precondition.condition/0","doc":"","ref":"Operator.HTN.Precondition.html#t:condition/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Precondition.operator/0","doc":"","ref":"Operator.HTN.Precondition.html#t:operator/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Precondition.all_satisfied?/3","doc":"Evaluate a list of preconditions with AND semantics.\n\nThis is the default behavior matching Task.preconditions_satisfied?/3.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Precondition.html#all_satisfied?/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Precondition.evaluate/3","doc":"Evaluate a precondition against facts and traits.\n\nReturns `{true, bindings}` on success or `{false, nil}` on failure.\nBindings are currently unused but reserved for future unification support.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Precondition.html#evaluate/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Precondition.find_all_matches/3","doc":"Find all matching alternatives.\n\nReturns a list of indices for all conditions that match.\nUseful for OR semantics where you want to know all valid options.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Precondition.html#find_all_matches/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Precondition.find_first_match/3","doc":"Find the first matching alternative in an ALT list.\n\nUnlike `:first` which just returns true/false, this returns\n`{:ok, index}` with the index of the first matching condition,\nor `:none` if nothing matches.\n\nUseful for branch selection in decomposition.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Precondition.html#find_first_match/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Precondition.satisfied?/3","doc":"Simple boolean evaluation of a precondition.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Precondition.html#satisfied?/3"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.HTN.Registry","doc":"Central storage for HTN goals, tasks, primitives, and axioms.\n\nThe Registry aggregates all HTN behavior modules into a single lookup table,\nenabling the planner and executor to find definitions by name. It uses\n`persistent_term` for essentially free read access after initialization.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html"},{"type":"module","title":"How It Works - Operator.HTN.Registry","doc":"1. **Compile time**: Modules using `Operator.HTN.DSL` define goals/tasks/primitives\n2. **After compile**: The `@after_compile` hook calls `register/1`\n3. **Runtime**: The planner calls `get_goal/2`, `get_primitive/2`, etc.\n\n```\n┌──────────────────┐     ┌──────────────────┐     ┌──────────────────┐\n│  MyBehavior.ex   │     │  EnemyAI.ex      │     │  PatrolBehavior  │\n│  use HTN.DSL     │     │  use HTN.DSL     │     │  use HTN.DSL     │\n└────────┬─────────┘     └────────┬─────────┘     └────────┬─────────┘\n         │                        │                        │\n         └────────────────────────┼────────────────────────┘\n                                  ▼\n                       ┌──────────────────────┐\n                       │      Registry        │\n                       │  (persistent_term)   │\n                       │                      │\n                       │  goals: %{...}       │\n                       │  tasks: %{...}       │\n                       │  primitives: %{...}  │\n                       │  axioms: %{...}      │\n                       └──────────────────────┘\n```","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#module-how-it-works"},{"type":"module","title":"Auto-Registration - Operator.HTN.Registry","doc":"Modules using `Operator.HTN.DSL` are automatically registered after compilation.\nTo disable this (useful for testing):\n\n    use Operator.HTN.DSL, auto_register: false","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#module-auto-registration"},{"type":"module","title":"Manual Registration - Operator.HTN.Registry","doc":"# Register a single module\n    Operator.HTN.Registry.register(MyHTNModule)\n\n    # Force refresh from all registered modules\n    Operator.HTN.Registry.refresh()","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#module-manual-registration"},{"type":"module","title":"Lookup Functions - Operator.HTN.Registry","doc":"# Get the full registry map\n    registry = Registry.all()\n    #=> %{goals: %{...}, tasks: %{...}, primitives: %{...}, axioms: %{...}}\n\n    # Get specific items by name\n    goal = Registry.get_goal(:acquire_data)\n    task = Registry.get_task(:move_to)\n    primitive = Registry.get_primitive(:attack)\n    axiom = Registry.get_axiom(:enemy_nearby)\n\n    # List all registered names\n    Registry.list_goal_names()\n    #=> [:patrol, :attack, :flee, :idle]\n\n    # Get statistics\n    Registry.stats()\n    #=> %{goals: 5, tasks: 12, primitives: 8, axioms: 3}","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#module-lookup-functions"},{"type":"module","title":"Testing Considerations - Operator.HTN.Registry","doc":"The Registry uses `persistent_term`, which is global state. For test isolation:\n\n1. Use `async: false` on test modules that touch the Registry\n2. Call `Registry.reset()` in setup to ensure clean state\n3. Use `Operator.HTN.TestHelpers` for convenient setup functions\n\n    defmodule MyTest do\n      use ExUnit.Case, async: false\n      import Operator.HTN.TestHelpers\n\n      setup :reset_registry\n\n      setup do\n        register_modules([MyBehavior])\n        :ok\n      end\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#module-testing-considerations"},{"type":"module","title":"Performance - Operator.HTN.Registry","doc":"* **Reads**: O(1) via `persistent_term` - essentially free\n* **Writes**: Relatively expensive (copies data), but only happens at registration\n* **Memory**: All registered modules share a single persistent_term entry","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#module-performance"},{"type":"module","title":"See Also - Operator.HTN.Registry","doc":"* `Operator.HTN.DSL` - How modules define HTN structures\n* `Operator.HTN.TestHelpers` - Test utilities including `reset_registry/1`\n* `Operator.HTN.Planner` - Uses Registry to look up goals","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#module-see-also"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Registry.registry/0","doc":"The registry map containing all HTN definitions.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#t:registry/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Fields - Operator.HTN.Registry.registry/0","doc":"* `:goals` - Map of goal name atoms to goal definitions\n* `:tasks` - Map of task name atoms to `%Task{}` structs\n* `:primitives` - Map of primitive name atoms to `%Task{}` structs\n* `:axioms` - Map of axiom name atoms to `%Axiom{}` structs","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#t:registry/0-fields"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Registry.all/0","doc":"Returns the merged registry containing all registered definitions.\n\nThis is the primary read function - it returns everything in one map\nfor efficient batch access by the planner.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#all/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Registry.all/0","doc":"A map with `:goals`, `:tasks`, `:primitives`, and `:axioms` keys.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#all/0-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Registry.all/0","doc":"registry = Registry.all()\n    goal = registry.goals[:patrol]\n    primitive = registry.primitives[:fire_weapon]","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#all/0-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Registry.get_axiom/2","doc":"Get an axiom by name.\n\nAxioms are reusable query patterns for preconditions.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#get_axiom/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Registry.get_axiom/2","doc":"* `name` - The axiom atom (e.g., `:enemy_nearby`, `:has_weapon`)\n* `registry` - Optional registry map (defaults to `all()`)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#get_axiom/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Registry.get_axiom/2","doc":"The `%Axiom{}` struct if found, `nil` otherwise.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#get_axiom/2-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Registry.get_axiom/2","doc":"axiom = Registry.get_axiom(:enemy_in_range)\n    #=> %Axiom{name: :enemy_in_range, query_fn: #Function<...>}\n\n    # Evaluate axiom\n    Axiom.evaluate(axiom, facts, max_range: 10)\n    #=> true","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#get_axiom/2-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Registry.get_goal/2","doc":"Get a goal definition by name.\n\nGoals are high-level objectives that decompose into task sequences.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#get_goal/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Registry.get_goal/2","doc":"* `name` - The goal atom (e.g., `:patrol`, `:attack`)\n* `registry` - Optional registry map (defaults to `all()`)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#get_goal/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Registry.get_goal/2","doc":"The goal map if found, `nil` otherwise.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#get_goal/2-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Registry.get_goal/2","doc":"goal = Registry.get_goal(:infiltrate)\n    #=> %{name: :infiltrate, precond: #Function<...>, decompose: [...]}\n\n    Registry.get_goal(:nonexistent)\n    #=> nil","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#get_goal/2-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Registry.get_primitive/2","doc":"Get a primitive by name.\n\nPrimitives are directly executable actions - the leaf nodes of the HTN tree.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#get_primitive/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Registry.get_primitive/2","doc":"* `name` - The primitive atom (e.g., `:attack`, `:wait`, `:move`)\n* `registry` - Optional registry map (defaults to `all()`)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#get_primitive/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Registry.get_primitive/2","doc":"The `%Task{}` struct (with `type: :primitive`) if found, `nil` otherwise.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#get_primitive/2-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Registry.get_primitive/2","doc":"primitive = Registry.get_primitive(:fire_weapon)\n    #=> %Task{name: :fire_weapon, type: :primitive, metadata: %{run: ...}}\n\n    # Use with Executor\n    {:ok, actor} = Executor.execute_primitive(primitive, actor, facts)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#get_primitive/2-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Registry.get_task/2","doc":"Get an abstract task by name.\n\nTasks are intermediate steps that decompose into subtasks or primitives.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#get_task/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Registry.get_task/2","doc":"* `name` - The task atom (e.g., `:move_to`, `:prepare_weapon`)\n* `registry` - Optional registry map (defaults to `all()`)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#get_task/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Registry.get_task/2","doc":"The `%Task{}` struct if found, `nil` otherwise.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#get_task/2-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Registry.get_task/2","doc":"task = Registry.get_task(:travel_to)\n    #=> %Task{name: :travel_to, type: :abstract, ...}","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#get_task/2-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Registry.list_axiom_names/0","doc":"List all registered axiom names.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#list_axiom_names/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Registry.list_axiom_names/0","doc":"List of axiom atom names.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#list_axiom_names/0-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Registry.list_axiom_names/0","doc":"Registry.list_axiom_names()\n    #=> [:enemy_nearby, :has_ammo, :in_cover]","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#list_axiom_names/0-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Registry.list_goal_names/0","doc":"List all registered goal names.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#list_goal_names/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Registry.list_goal_names/0","doc":"List of goal atom names.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#list_goal_names/0-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Registry.list_goal_names/0","doc":"Registry.list_goal_names()\n    #=> [:patrol, :attack, :flee, :idle]","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#list_goal_names/0-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Registry.list_primitive_names/0","doc":"List all registered primitive names.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#list_primitive_names/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Registry.list_primitive_names/0","doc":"List of primitive atom names.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#list_primitive_names/0-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Registry.list_primitive_names/0","doc":"Registry.list_primitive_names()\n    #=> [:walk, :fire, :reload, :wait]","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#list_primitive_names/0-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Registry.list_task_names/0","doc":"List all registered abstract task names.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#list_task_names/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Registry.list_task_names/0","doc":"List of task atom names.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#list_task_names/0-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Registry.list_task_names/0","doc":"Registry.list_task_names()\n    #=> [:move_to, :prepare_weapon, :find_cover]","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#list_task_names/0-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Registry.merge/1","doc":"Merge multiple registry fragments into one.\n\nUsed internally to combine definitions from multiple modules. Later entries\noverride earlier ones if names conflict.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#merge/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Registry.merge/1","doc":"* `registries` - List of registry maps","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#merge/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Registry.merge/1","doc":"A single merged registry map.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#merge/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Registry.modules/0","doc":"Returns the list of currently registered modules.\n\nUseful for debugging or saving/restoring registry state in tests.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#modules/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Registry.modules/0","doc":"List of module atoms.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#modules/0-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Registry.modules/0","doc":"Registry.modules()\n    #=> [MyGame.CombatBehavior, MyGame.PatrolBehavior]","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#modules/0-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Registry.refresh/1","doc":"Forces a refresh of the registry from registered modules.\n\nReloads all module definitions and rebuilds the merged registry. This is\ncalled automatically by `register/1` but can be called manually if you\nsuspect the registry is stale.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#refresh/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Registry.refresh/1","doc":"* `modules` - Optional module list (defaults to all registered modules)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#refresh/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Registry.refresh/1","doc":"`:ok` after rebuilding the registry.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#refresh/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Registry.register/1","doc":"Registers an HTN module and refreshes the merged registry.\n\nThe module must export `__htn__/0`, which is automatically generated by\n`use Operator.HTN.DSL`. This function is typically called automatically\nvia `@after_compile`, but can be called manually for dynamic registration.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#register/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Registry.register/1","doc":"* `module` - The module atom to register","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#register/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Registry.register/1","doc":"`:ok` on success. Silently succeeds if module doesn't export `__htn__/0`.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#register/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Registry.register/1","doc":"# Manual registration (usually not needed)\n    Operator.HTN.Registry.register(MyGame.CombatBehavior)\n\n    # Verify registration\n    Registry.list_goal_names()\n    #=> [:attack, :defend, :flee]","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#register/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Registry.reset/0","doc":"Resets the registry to empty state.\n\nClears all registered modules and definitions. Essential for test isolation\nsince the registry uses global `persistent_term` storage.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#reset/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Registry.reset/0","doc":"`:ok` after clearing.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#reset/0-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Registry.reset/0","doc":"# In test setup\n    setup do\n      Operator.HTN.Registry.reset()\n      :ok\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#reset/0-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"See Also - Operator.HTN.Registry.reset/0","doc":"* `Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.reset_registry/1` - ExUnit-friendly wrapper","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#reset/0-see-also"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Registry.stats/0","doc":"Return counts for each category.\n\nUseful for debugging and monitoring registry state.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#stats/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Registry.stats/0","doc":"Map with counts for goals, tasks, primitives, and axioms.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#stats/0-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Registry.stats/0","doc":"Registry.stats()\n    #=> %{goals: 5, tasks: 12, primitives: 8, axioms: 3}","ref":"Operator.HTN.Registry.html#stats/0-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.HTN.Storage","doc":"Default ETS-based plan storage implementation.\n\nThis module provides the default storage backend for HTN plans.\nPlans are stored in an ETS table and persist for the lifetime of\nthe application.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Storage.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Usage - Operator.HTN.Storage","doc":"This module is used automatically when no custom storage module\nis configured:\n\n    # Automatic via Planner\n    {:ok, plan} = Operator.HTN.Planner.run(:goal, facts, traits)\n\n    # Direct access\n    Operator.HTN.Storage.persist_plan(entity_id, plan)\n    plan = Operator.HTN.Storage.fetch_plan(entity_id)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Storage.html#module-usage"},{"type":"module","title":"Configuration - Operator.HTN.Storage","doc":"To use a different storage backend:\n\n    config :operator,\n      storage_module: MyApp.CustomStorage","ref":"Operator.HTN.Storage.html#module-configuration"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Storage.clear_all/0","doc":"Clear all stored plans.\n\nUseful for testing.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Storage.html#clear_all/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Storage.init/0","doc":"Initialize the storage table.\n\nCalled automatically by the Operator application, but can also be\ncalled manually in tests.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Storage.html#init/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Storage.stats/0","doc":"Get storage statistics.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Storage.html#stats/0"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.HTN.Task","doc":"A task in the HTN hierarchy.\n\nTasks are the building blocks of HTN planning. They form a hierarchy where\nhigh-level objectives decompose into lower-level actions, ultimately reaching\nexecutable primitives.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Task Types - Operator.HTN.Task","doc":"* **Abstract** - High-level tasks that decompose into subtasks. They represent\n  \"what to do\" without specifying exactly how. Abstract tasks have a `decompose`\n  function that breaks them down further.\n\n* **Primitive** - Leaf-level tasks that are directly executable. They represent\n  concrete actions your game can perform (move, attack, interact, etc.).","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#module-task-types"},{"type":"module","title":"Task Anatomy - Operator.HTN.Task","doc":"Every task has these components:\n\n| Component       | Required | Description                                      |\n|-----------------|----------|--------------------------------------------------|\n| `name`          | Yes      | Atom identifier (`:attack`, `:move_to`)          |\n| `type`          | Yes      | `:abstract` or `:primitive`                      |\n| `preconditions` | No       | List of conditions that must be true             |\n| `decompose`     | No*      | Function returning subtask list (abstract only)  |\n| `effects`       | No       | World state changes when task completes          |\n| `cost`          | No       | Planning heuristic (number or function)          |\n| `metadata`      | No       | Arbitrary data (animations, sounds, tags)        |\n\n*Abstract tasks without decomposition are treated as primitives during planning.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#module-task-anatomy"},{"type":"module","title":"Preconditions - Operator.HTN.Task","doc":"Preconditions gate whether a task can be planned. They're evaluated against\nthe current (or projected) world state during planning.\n\n    preconditions: [\n      fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :weapon}) end,\n      fn facts -> Facts.get(facts, {:self, :ammo}, 0) > 0 end\n    ]\n\nSee `Operator.HTN.Precondition` for logical operators (`:any`, `:all`, etc.).","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#module-preconditions"},{"type":"module","title":"Effects - Operator.HTN.Task","doc":"Effects represent world state changes that result from task execution. During\nplanning, effects are applied to a working copy of world state so the planner\ncan reason about future states and validate downstream preconditions.\n\nFor example, if `:unlock_door` has effect `door_unlocked: true`, then a\nsubsequent `:enter_room` task with precondition `door_unlocked == true` will\npass during planning.\n\nSee `Operator.HTN.Effect` for effect types and usage.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#module-effects"},{"type":"module","title":"Cost Functions - Operator.HTN.Task","doc":"Costs influence which plan the planner prefers when multiple valid plans exist.\nThey can be:\n\n* **Static** - A simple number: `cost: 5.0`\n* **Dynamic** - Based on world state: `cost: fn facts -> distance_factor(facts) end`\n* **Trait-aware** - Influenced by agent personality:\n  `cost: fn facts, traits -> base_cost(facts) * aggression_modifier(traits) end`","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#module-cost-functions"},{"type":"module","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Task","doc":"","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#module-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Abstract Task with Decomposition - Operator.HTN.Task","doc":"task = Task.new(:travel_to, :abstract,\n      preconditions: [fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :can_move}) end],\n      decompose: fn facts ->\n        destination = Facts.get(facts, {:self, :destination})\n        [{:pathfind, [destination]}, {:walk_path, []}]\n      end,\n      cost: 5.0\n    )","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#module-abstract-task-with-decomposition"},{"type":"module","title":"Primitive Task with Effects - Operator.HTN.Task","doc":"task = Task.new(:attack, :primitive,\n      preconditions: [fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :has_weapon}) end],\n      effects: [\n        Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:self, :in_combat}, true),\n        Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:self, :ammo}, :decrement)\n      ],\n      cost: fn facts, traits ->\n        base = Facts.get(facts, {:world, :enemy_threat_level}, 1.0)\n        aggression = Map.get(traits, :aggression, 1.0)\n        base / aggression  # Aggressive agents find attacking \"cheaper\"\n      end,\n      metadata: %{animation: \"attack_01\", sound: \"sword_swing.wav\"}\n    )","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#module-primitive-task-with-effects"},{"type":"module","title":"See Also - Operator.HTN.Task","doc":"* `Operator.HTN.DSL` - Declarative task definition\n* `Operator.HTN.Effect` - World state modifications\n* `Operator.HTN.Precondition` - Logical operators\n* `Operator.HTN.Executor` - Task execution at runtime","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#module-see-also"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Task.t/0","doc":"The Task struct representing a node in the HTN hierarchy.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Fields - Operator.HTN.Task.t/0","doc":"* `:name` - Atom identifier for the task\n* `:type` - Either `:abstract` or `:primitive`\n* `:preconditions` - List of conditions that must be satisfied\n* `:decompose` - Function returning subtask list (abstract tasks only)\n* `:effects` - List of `Effect` structs applied on completion\n* `:cost` - Static number or function for planning heuristics\n* `:metadata` - Arbitrary map for game-specific data","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#t:t/0-fields"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.HTN.Task.task_type/0","doc":"The type of task in the HTN hierarchy.\n\n* `:abstract` - Decomposes into subtasks\n* `:primitive` - Directly executable leaf node","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#t:task_type/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Task.abstract?/1","doc":"Check if this task is abstract (decomposes into subtasks).\n\nAbstract tasks represent high-level objectives that break down into\nlower-level tasks during planning.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#abstract?/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Task.abstract?/1","doc":"iex> task = Task.new(:patrol, :abstract)\n    iex> Task.abstract?(task)\n    true\n\n    iex> task = Task.new(:fire, :primitive)\n    iex> Task.abstract?(task)\n    false","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#abstract?/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Task.calculate_cost/3","doc":"Calculate task cost for planning heuristics.\n\nCost influences plan selection when multiple valid plans exist. Lower cost\nplans are generally preferred.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#calculate_cost/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Cost Types - Operator.HTN.Task.calculate_cost/3","doc":"* **Static number** - Fixed cost regardless of world state\n* **Arity-1 function** - `fn facts -> number end`\n* **Arity-2 function** - `fn facts, traits -> number end`","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#calculate_cost/3-cost-types"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Task.calculate_cost/3","doc":"* `task` - The Task struct\n* `facts` - Current world state\n* `traits` - Agent traits/genome for personality-influenced costs","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#calculate_cost/3-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.Task.calculate_cost/3","doc":"A number representing the task's cost. Defaults to `1.0` if no cost specified.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#calculate_cost/3-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Task.calculate_cost/3","doc":"# Static cost\n    task = Task.new(:walk, :primitive, cost: 5.0)\n    Task.calculate_cost(task, facts, traits)\n    #=> 5.0\n\n    # Dynamic cost based on distance\n    task = Task.new(:travel, :abstract,\n      cost: fn facts ->\n        Facts.get(facts, {:world, :distance_to_target}, 10) * 0.5\n      end\n    )\n\n    # Trait-influenced cost (aggressive NPCs find combat \"cheaper\")\n    task = Task.new(:attack, :primitive,\n      cost: fn _facts, traits ->\n        10.0 / Map.get(traits, :aggression, 1.0)\n      end\n    )","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#calculate_cost/3-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Task.new/3","doc":"Create a new task.\n\nWhile the DSL is the recommended way to define tasks, this function provides\nprogrammatic task creation for dynamic scenarios or testing.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#new/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.Task.new/3","doc":"* `name` - Atom identifier for the task\n* `type` - Either `:abstract` or `:primitive`\n* `opts` - Keyword list of options","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#new/3-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - Operator.HTN.Task.new/3","doc":"* `:preconditions` - List of predicate functions (default: `[]`)\n* `:decompose` - Function returning subtask list (default: `nil`)\n* `:effects` - List of Effect structs (default: `[]`)\n* `:cost` - Static cost or cost function (default: `1.0`)\n* `:metadata` - Arbitrary metadata (default: `%{}`)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#new/3-options"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Task.new/3","doc":"# Simple primitive\n    Task.new(:wait, :primitive)\n\n    # Abstract with decomposition\n    Task.new(:patrol, :abstract,\n      decompose: fn _facts -> [{:walk_to, [:waypoint_1]}, {:look_around, []}] end\n    )\n\n    # Full-featured primitive\n    Task.new(:fire_weapon, :primitive,\n      preconditions: [\n        fn facts -> Facts.get(facts, {:self, :ammo}, 0) > 0 end\n      ],\n      effects: [\n        Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:self, :fired_weapon}, true)\n      ],\n      cost: 2.0,\n      metadata: %{animation: \"shoot\", cooldown_ms: 500}\n    )","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#new/3-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Task.preconditions_satisfied?/3","doc":"Check if all preconditions are satisfied.\n\nPreconditions can be:\n- Simple functions: `fn facts -> boolean end` or `fn facts, traits -> boolean end`\n- Logical operators: `{:any, [fns]}`, `{:all, [fns]}`, `{:first, [fns]}`, `{:not, fn}`\n\nAll preconditions in the list are combined with AND semantics.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#preconditions_satisfied?/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Task.preconditions_satisfied?/3","doc":"# Simple function\n    preconditions: [fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :ready}) end]\n\n    # OR operator: has weapon OR near pickup\n    preconditions: [\n      {:any, [\n        fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :has_weapon}) end,\n        fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:world, :weapon_nearby}) end\n      ]}\n    ]\n\n    # Combined: ready AND (armed OR near weapon)\n    preconditions: [\n      fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :ready}) end,\n      {:any, [\n        fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :armed}) end,\n        fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:world, :weapon_nearby}) end\n      ]}\n    ]","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#preconditions_satisfied?/3-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Task.primitive?/1","doc":"Check if this task is primitive (directly executable).\n\nPrimitive tasks are the leaf nodes of the HTN tree - they don't decompose\nfurther and are executed directly by the `Executor`.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#primitive?/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.Task.primitive?/1","doc":"iex> task = Task.new(:attack, :primitive)\n    iex> Task.primitive?(task)\n    true\n\n    iex> task = Task.new(:combat_sequence, :abstract)\n    iex> Task.primitive?(task)\n    false","ref":"Operator.HTN.Task.html#primitive?/1-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers","doc":"Test utilities for working with Operator's HTN system.\n\nThis module provides helper functions for setting up and tearing down\nHTN test fixtures, particularly around Registry isolation.","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Why Test Helpers? - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers","doc":"Operator's Registry uses `persistent_term` for fast lookups, which means:\n\n1. **Global state** - Registered modules persist across tests\n2. **No automatic cleanup** - You must explicitly reset between tests\n3. **Async conflicts** - Tests using Registry should use `async: false`","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#module-why-test-helpers"},{"type":"module","title":"Quick Start - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers","doc":"defmodule MyApp.BehaviorTest do\n      use ExUnit.Case, async: false\n\n      # Import the helpers\n      import Operator.HTN.TestHelpers\n\n      # Use the setup helper\n      setup :reset_registry\n\n      # Or use the full setup with module registration\n      setup do\n        setup_htn([MyApp.NPCBehavior, MyApp.EnemyBehavior])\n      end\n\n      test \"my behavior works\" do\n        facts = Operator.HTN.Facts.new()\n        {:ok, plan} = Operator.HTN.Planner.run(:my_goal, facts, %{})\n        assert Plan.has_tasks?(plan)\n      end\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#module-quick-start"},{"type":"module","title":"Setup Functions - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers","doc":"The module provides several setup patterns:","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#module-setup-functions"},{"type":"module","title":"reset_registry/1 - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers","doc":"ExUnit setup callback that resets the registry before each test:\n\n    setup :reset_registry","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#module-reset_registry-1"},{"type":"module","title":"setup_htn/1 - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers","doc":"Full setup that resets registry and registers modules:\n\n    setup do\n      setup_htn([MyBehavior])\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#module-setup_htn-1"},{"type":"module","title":"with_registry/2 - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers","doc":"Runs a function with specific modules registered, then cleans up:\n\n    test \"isolated test\" do\n      with_registry [TestBehavior], fn ->\n        # Test code here - registry only contains TestBehavior\n      end\n      # Registry is reset after block\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#module-with_registry-2"},{"type":"module","title":"Module Registration - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers","doc":"When testing HTN modules, you need to ensure they're registered:\n\n    setup do\n      # Reset first to ensure clean state\n      Operator.HTN.Registry.reset()\n\n      # Ensure module is compiled\n      Code.ensure_loaded!(MyBehavior)\n\n      # Register it\n      Operator.HTN.Registry.register(MyBehavior)\n\n      :ok\n    end\n\nOr use the helper:\n\n    setup do\n      setup_htn([MyBehavior])\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#module-module-registration"},{"type":"module","title":"Async Tests - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers","doc":"Because the Registry is global, tests that use it cannot run in parallel:\n\n    # WRONG - will cause flaky tests\n    use ExUnit.Case, async: true\n\n    # CORRECT\n    use ExUnit.Case, async: false\n\nTests that don't touch the Registry (e.g., pure Facts manipulation) can\nsafely use `async: true`.","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#module-async-tests"},{"type":"module","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers","doc":"","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#module-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Basic Test Setup - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers","doc":"defmodule MyApp.CombatBehaviorTest do\n      use ExUnit.Case, async: false\n      import Operator.HTN.TestHelpers\n\n      alias Operator.HTN.{Facts, Plan, Planner}\n\n      setup :reset_registry\n\n      setup do\n        # Register our behavior module\n        register_modules([MyApp.CombatBehavior])\n        :ok\n      end\n\n      test \"attack goal generates plan when armed\" do\n        facts = Facts.from_perception(%{\n          self: %{armed: true, ammo: 10},\n          world: %{enemy_visible: true}\n        })\n\n        assert {:ok, plan} = Planner.run(:attack_enemy, facts, %{})\n        assert Plan.has_tasks?(plan)\n      end\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#module-basic-test-setup"},{"type":"module","title":"Testing Multiple Behaviors - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers","doc":"defmodule MyApp.IntegrationTest do\n      use ExUnit.Case, async: false\n      import Operator.HTN.TestHelpers\n\n      setup do\n        setup_htn([\n          MyApp.CombatBehavior,\n          MyApp.MovementBehavior,\n          MyApp.SocialBehavior\n        ])\n      end\n\n      test \"behaviors can reference each other\" do\n        # Test cross-behavior task references\n      end\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#module-testing-multiple-behaviors"},{"type":"module","title":"Isolated Test with with_registry - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers","doc":"defmodule MyApp.IsolatedTest do\n      use ExUnit.Case, async: false\n      import Operator.HTN.TestHelpers\n\n      test \"test A uses BehaviorA\" do\n        with_registry [BehaviorA], fn ->\n          # Only BehaviorA is registered\n          assert Registry.get_goal(:goal_a) != nil\n          assert Registry.get_goal(:goal_b) == nil\n        end\n      end\n\n      test \"test B uses BehaviorB\" do\n        with_registry [BehaviorB], fn ->\n          # Only BehaviorB is registered\n          assert Registry.get_goal(:goal_a) == nil\n          assert Registry.get_goal(:goal_b) != nil\n        end\n      end\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#module-isolated-test-with-with_registry"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.assert_has_task/3","doc":"Assert that a plan contains a specific task.","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#assert_has_task/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.assert_has_task/3","doc":"* `plan` - The Plan struct\n* `task_name` - Expected task name atom\n* `args` - Optional expected arguments (if nil, only checks task name)","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#assert_has_task/3-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.assert_has_task/3","doc":"plan = Planner.run!(:attack, facts, traits)\n    assert_has_task(plan, :fire_weapon)\n    assert_has_task(plan, :move_to, [:enemy_position])","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#assert_has_task/3-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.register_modules/1","doc":"Register one or more HTN modules with the Registry.\n\nEnsures each module is loaded and then registers it.","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#register_modules/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.register_modules/1","doc":"* `modules` - Single module or list of modules to register","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#register_modules/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.register_modules/1","doc":"setup do\n      reset_registry(%{})\n      register_modules([MyApp.Behavior])\n      :ok\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#register_modules/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.reset_registry/1","doc":"ExUnit setup callback that resets the Registry.\n\nUse in your test module's setup:\n\n    setup :reset_registry\n\nThis ensures each test starts with a clean, empty registry.","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#reset_registry/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.reset_registry/1","doc":"Always returns `:ok`.","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#reset_registry/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.setup_htn/1","doc":"Full setup that resets registry and registers modules.\n\nConvenience function combining `reset_registry/1` and `register_modules/1`.","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#setup_htn/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.setup_htn/1","doc":"* `modules` - List of modules to register","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#setup_htn/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.setup_htn/1","doc":"Returns `:ok` for use in ExUnit setup blocks.","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#setup_htn/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.setup_htn/1","doc":"setup do\n      setup_htn([MyApp.NPCBehavior])\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#setup_htn/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.test_facts/1","doc":"Create a test Facts struct from a simple map.\n\nShorthand for `Facts.from_perception/1` with a cleaner test syntax.","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#test_facts/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.test_facts/1","doc":"* `data` - Map with `:self`, `:world`, and/or `:social` keys","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#test_facts/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.test_facts/1","doc":"facts = test_facts(%{\n      self: %{health: 100, armed: true},\n      world: %{enemies: [:goblin]}\n    })","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#test_facts/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.with_registry/2","doc":"Run a function with specific modules registered, then reset.\n\nUseful for tests that need complete isolation from other tests.","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#with_registry/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.with_registry/2","doc":"* `modules` - Modules to register for the duration\n* `fun` - Zero-arity function to execute","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#with_registry/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.with_registry/2","doc":"The return value of `fun`.","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#with_registry/2-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.with_registry/2","doc":"test \"isolated behavior test\" do\n      result = with_registry [TestBehavior], fn ->\n        {:ok, plan} = Planner.run(:test_goal, facts, traits)\n        plan\n      end\n\n      assert Plan.has_tasks?(result)\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.html#with_registry/2-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace","doc":"Detailed tracing for HTN planning operations.\n\nThe Trace system lets you observe every step of the planning process -\nwhich goals are being expanded, which preconditions pass or fail, how\ntasks decompose, and what effects are applied. Essential for debugging\ncomplex HTN behaviors.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Inspiration - Operator.HTN.Trace","doc":"Inspired by Decima's HTN translator (Horizon Zero Dawn, Death Stranding)\nwhich inserts logging at key points: ON_START_PRED, ON_RETRY_PRED,\nON_BIND, ON_END_PRED. This module provides similar hooks for Elixir.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html#module-inspiration"},{"type":"module","title":"Quick Start - Operator.HTN.Trace","doc":"# 1. Implement a trace handler\n    defmodule MyApp.HTNTraceHandler do\n      @behaviour Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler\n\n      @impl true\n      def on_goal_start(goal_name, _facts, _opts) do\n        IO.puts(\"[HTN] Goal start: #{goal_name}\")\n      end\n\n      @impl true\n      def on_goal_end(goal_name, result, _opts) do\n        IO.puts(\"[HTN] Goal end: #{goal_name} -> #{result}\")\n      end\n\n      @impl true\n      def on_precondition_eval(context, result, _opts) do\n        name = context[:goal] || context[:task]\n        IO.puts(\"[HTN] Precondition #{name}: #{result}\")\n      end\n\n      @impl true\n      def on_task_expand(task_name, args, _facts, _opts) do\n        IO.puts(\"[HTN] Expand: #{task_name} #{inspect(args)}\")\n      end\n\n      @impl true\n      def on_task_complete(task_name, result_tasks, status, _opts) do\n        IO.puts(\"[HTN] Complete: #{task_name} -> #{status} (#{length(result_tasks)} tasks)\")\n      end\n\n      @impl true\n      def on_effect_apply(effect, _facts, _opts) do\n        IO.puts(\"[HTN] Effect: #{inspect(effect.key)} = #{inspect(effect.value)}\")\n      end\n\n      @impl true\n      def on_branch_select(task_name, branch_id, _opts) do\n        IO.puts(\"[HTN] Branch: #{task_name} selected #{branch_id}\")\n      end\n    end\n\n    # 2. Enable tracing\n    Operator.HTN.Trace.set_handler(MyApp.HTNTraceHandler)\n\n    # 3. Run planner - trace events fire\n    Planner.run(:my_goal, facts, traits)\n    # [HTN] Goal start: my_goal\n    # [HTN] Precondition my_goal: true\n    # [HTN] Expand: subtask_a []\n    # [HTN] Effect: {:self, :armed} = true\n    # [HTN] Complete: subtask_a -> success (1 tasks)\n    # [HTN] Goal end: my_goal -> success","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html#module-quick-start"},{"type":"module","title":"Configuration - Operator.HTN.Trace","doc":"# In config/config.exs\n    config :operator, trace_handler: MyApp.HTNTraceHandler\n\n    # Or at runtime (takes precedence)\n    Operator.HTN.Trace.set_handler(MyApp.HTNTraceHandler)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html#module-configuration"},{"type":"module","title":"Trace Events - Operator.HTN.Trace","doc":"| Event              | When                                  | Key Data                    |\n|--------------------|---------------------------------------|-----------------------------|\n| `goal_start`       | Beginning goal expansion              | goal_name, facts            |\n| `goal_end`         | Goal expansion complete               | goal_name, :success/:failure|\n| `precondition_eval`| Precondition checked                  | context map, result boolean |\n| `task_expand`      | Starting task decomposition           | task_name, args, facts      |\n| `task_complete`    | Task decomposition done               | task_name, result_tasks     |\n| `effect_apply`     | Effect applied to working facts       | effect struct, facts        |\n| `branch_select`    | Decomposition branch chosen           | task_name, branch_id        |","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html#module-trace-events"},{"type":"module","title":"Production Performance - Operator.HTN.Trace","doc":"When no trace handler is configured (`nil`), all trace operations are\nno-ops with minimal overhead (one `persistent_term` lookup that returns\n`nil`, then immediate return). Safe to leave trace calls in production\ncode.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html#module-production-performance"},{"type":"module","title":"Built-in Console Handler - Operator.HTN.Trace","doc":"For quick debugging, use the provided console handler:\n\n    Operator.HTN.Trace.set_handler(Operator.HTN.Trace.ConsoleHandler)","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html#module-built-in-console-handler"},{"type":"module","title":"See Also - Operator.HTN.Trace","doc":"* `Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler` - Behaviour for trace handlers\n* `Operator.HTN.Trace.ConsoleHandler` - Built-in console output handler\n* `Operator.HTN.Engine` - Where trace events are emitted","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html#module-see-also"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.branch_select/3","doc":"Trace branch selection in decomposition.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html#branch_select/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.effect_apply/3","doc":"Trace effect application.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html#effect_apply/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.enabled?/0","doc":"Check if tracing is enabled.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html#enabled?/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.get_handler/0","doc":"Get the current trace handler, if any.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html#get_handler/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.goal_end/3","doc":"Trace the end of goal expansion.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html#goal_end/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.goal_start/3","doc":"Trace the start of goal expansion.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html#goal_start/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.precondition_eval/3","doc":"Trace precondition evaluation.\n\nContext is a map with:\n- `:goal` or `:task` - The current goal/task name\n- `:precondition_index` - Index in preconditions list\n- `:precondition_type` - `:function`, `:axiom`, `:operator`, etc.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html#precondition_eval/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.reset/0","doc":"Reset trace handler (useful for tests).","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html#reset/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.set_handler/1","doc":"Set the trace handler module.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html#set_handler/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.task_complete/4","doc":"Trace task expansion completion.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html#task_complete/4"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.task_expand/4","doc":"Trace task expansion start.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.html#task_expand/4"},{"type":"module","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.ConsoleHandler","doc":"Console-based trace handler for debugging HTN planning.\n\nPrints colored, formatted trace output to the console.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.ConsoleHandler.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Usage - Operator.HTN.Trace.ConsoleHandler","doc":"# Enable console tracing\n    Operator.HTN.Trace.set_handler(Operator.HTN.Trace.ConsoleHandler)\n\n    # Run your planner\n    Operator.HTN.Planner.run(:some_goal, facts, traits)\n\n    # Disable tracing\n    Operator.HTN.Trace.reset()","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.ConsoleHandler.html#module-usage"},{"type":"module","title":"Output Format - Operator.HTN.Trace.ConsoleHandler","doc":"[HTN] ▶ GOAL acquire_data\n    [HTN]   ✓ Precondition passed (goal: acquire_data)\n    [HTN]   → TASK ensure_access []\n    [HTN]     ✓ Precondition passed (task: ensure_access)\n    [HTN]     ⚡ Effect applied: {:self, :has_access} = true\n    [HTN]   ← TASK ensure_access → 2 subtasks\n    [HTN] ◀ GOAL acquire_data SUCCESS","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.ConsoleHandler.html#module-output-format"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler","doc":"Behaviour for HTN trace handlers.\n\nImplement this behaviour to receive detailed tracing events during\nHTN planning. All callbacks are optional - implement only the events\nyou care about.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler.html"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Example Implementation - Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler","doc":"defmodule MyApp.DetailedTracer do\n      @behaviour Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler\n\n      @impl true\n      def on_goal_start(goal_name, facts, _opts) do\n        Logger.debug(\"Planning goal: #{goal_name}\")\n        Logger.debug(\"Facts: #{inspect(facts, pretty: true)}\")\n      end\n\n      @impl true\n      def on_precondition_eval(%{goal: goal}, false, _opts) do\n        Logger.warning(\"Goal #{goal} precondition FAILED\")\n      end\n\n      def on_precondition_eval(_context, _result, _opts), do: :ok\n\n      # ... implement other callbacks as needed\n    end","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler.html#module-example-implementation"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Callback Summary - Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler","doc":"| Callback               | When Called                      |\n|------------------------|----------------------------------|\n| `on_goal_start/3`      | Goal expansion begins            |\n| `on_goal_end/3`        | Goal expansion ends              |\n| `on_precondition_eval/3`| Precondition evaluated          |\n| `on_task_expand/4`     | Task decomposition starts        |\n| `on_task_complete/4`   | Task decomposition ends          |\n| `on_effect_apply/3`    | Effect applied to facts          |\n| `on_branch_select/3`   | Decomposition branch chosen      |\n\nAll callbacks are optional via `@optional_callbacks`.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler.html#module-callback-summary"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler.on_branch_select/3","doc":"Called when a decomposition branch is selected.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler.html#c:on_branch_select/3"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler.on_effect_apply/3","doc":"Called when an effect is applied.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler.html#c:on_effect_apply/3"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler.on_goal_end/3","doc":"Called when goal expansion ends.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler.html#c:on_goal_end/3"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler.on_goal_start/3","doc":"Called when goal expansion starts.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler.html#c:on_goal_start/3"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler.on_precondition_eval/3","doc":"Called when a precondition is evaluated.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler.html#c:on_precondition_eval/3"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler.on_task_complete/4","doc":"Called when task expansion completes.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler.html#c:on_task_complete/4"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler.on_task_expand/4","doc":"Called when task expansion begins.","ref":"Operator.HTN.Trace.Handler.html#c:on_task_expand/4"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Operator.Rationalization","doc":"Behaviour for narrative annotation of plans and events.\n\nThe Rationalization system transforms cold, mechanical HTN outputs into\nrich narrative content. Instead of \"NPC executed :attack\", you get\n\"The guard spotted the intruder and drew his weapon.\"","ref":"Operator.Rationalization.html"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Two Responsibilities - Operator.Rationalization","doc":"1. **Plan Annotation** - Add narrative context to generated plans\n2. **Event Rationalization** - Transform raw Director events into full narratives","ref":"Operator.Rationalization.html#module-two-responsibilities"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Configuration - Operator.Rationalization","doc":"config :operator,\n      rationalization_module: MyApp.OperatorRationalization","ref":"Operator.Rationalization.html#module-configuration"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Example Implementation - Operator.Rationalization","doc":"defmodule MyApp.OperatorRationalization do\n      @behaviour Operator.Rationalization\n\n      @impl true\n      def annotate_plan(plan) do\n        %{\n          plan_id: plan.goal,\n          explanation: explain_goal(plan.goal),\n          narrative_tags: infer_tags(plan),\n          mood: infer_mood(plan)\n        }\n      end\n\n      @impl true\n      def apply(event) do\n        Map.merge(event, %{\n          explanation: generate_explanation(event),\n          effects: generate_effects(event),\n          dialogue: generate_dialogue(event)\n        })\n      end\n\n      defp explain_goal(:patrol), do: \"The guard begins their routine patrol.\"\n      defp explain_goal(:attack), do: \"Aggression surges as combat instincts take over.\"\n      defp explain_goal(:flee), do: \"Self-preservation kicks in. Time to run.\"\n      defp explain_goal(goal), do: \"Pursuing objective: #{goal}\"\n\n      defp infer_tags(%{goal: :attack}), do: [:combat, :action]\n      defp infer_tags(%{goal: :patrol}), do: [:routine, :ambient]\n      defp infer_tags(_), do: [:general]\n\n      defp infer_mood(%{goal: :flee}), do: :fearful\n      defp infer_mood(%{goal: :attack}), do: :aggressive\n      defp infer_mood(_), do: :neutral\n\n      defp generate_explanation(%{type: :ambush, severity: s}) when s >= 4 do\n        \"A devastating ambush springs from the shadows!\"\n      end\n      defp generate_explanation(%{type: :ambush}) do\n        \"Enemies emerge from hiding.\"\n      end\n      defp generate_explanation(%{type: type}) do\n        \"An event of type #{type} occurs.\"\n      end\n    end","ref":"Operator.Rationalization.html#module-example-implementation"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Use Cases - Operator.Rationalization","doc":"","ref":"Operator.Rationalization.html#module-use-cases"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Debug Logging - Operator.Rationalization","doc":"Add explanations for development debugging:\n\n    Logger.debug(\"Plan: #{plan.metadata.explanation}\")\n    # => \"Plan: The guard spotted movement and is investigating.\"","ref":"Operator.Rationalization.html#module-debug-logging"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"UI/UX Integration - Operator.Rationalization","doc":"Feed rationalized events to your UI:\n\n    def handle_event(event) do\n      Toast.show(event.explanation)\n      play_sound(event.mood)\n    end","ref":"Operator.Rationalization.html#module-ui-ux-integration"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Narrative Generation - Operator.Rationalization","doc":"Build emergent storytelling from plan sequences:\n\n    def chronicle_day(entity, plans) do\n      plans\n      |> Enum.map(& &1.metadata.explanation)\n      |> Enum.join(\" \")\n    end\n    # => \"The merchant opened shop. A customer arrived. They haggled fiercely.\"","ref":"Operator.Rationalization.html#module-narrative-generation"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Default Implementation - Operator.Rationalization","doc":"If no rationalization module is configured, Operator provides minimal\ndefaults that pass through data with basic annotations like\n\"Agent pursuing goal: :patrol\".","ref":"Operator.Rationalization.html#module-default-implementation"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"See Also - Operator.Rationalization","doc":"* `Operator.HTN.Plan` - Plans that get annotated\n* `Operator.Director` - Generates events that get rationalized","ref":"Operator.Rationalization.html#module-see-also"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.Rationalization.annotate_plan/1","doc":"Annotate an HTN plan with narrative justification.\n\nCalled after plan generation to add context about why the plan\nwas chosen and what it represents narratively.\n\nReturns a map of annotations to merge into plan metadata.","ref":"Operator.Rationalization.html#c:annotate_plan/1"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.Rationalization.apply/1","doc":"Rationalize a raw event into a full event with explanation.\n\nTakes a raw event map and returns a fully rationalized event\nwith explanation text, effects, and other narrative context.","ref":"Operator.Rationalization.html#c:apply/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Rationalization.annotate_plan/1","doc":"Annotate a plan using the configured module or defaults.","ref":"Operator.Rationalization.html#annotate_plan/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Rationalization.apply/1","doc":"Rationalize an event using the configured module or defaults.","ref":"Operator.Rationalization.html#apply/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Rationalization.get_module/0","doc":"Get the configured rationalization module, if any.","ref":"Operator.Rationalization.html#get_module/0"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Operator.Storage","doc":"Behaviour for plan persistence across ticks.\n\nThe Storage behaviour lets you customize how HTN plans are cached between\ngame ticks. This is essential for games where plan execution spans multiple\nframes - you need somewhere to store the \"current plan\" for each NPC.","ref":"Operator.Storage.html"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Why Plan Storage? - Operator.Storage","doc":"HTN plans often take multiple ticks to execute:\n\n1. Tick 1: Generate plan `[{:move_to, [:door]}, {:open_door, []}, {:enter, []}]`\n2. Tick 1: Execute `:move_to` - NPC starts walking\n3. Tick 2-10: NPC still walking (plan stored, waiting)\n4. Tick 11: NPC arrives, execute `:open_door`\n5. Tick 12: Execute `:enter`\n6. Tick 12: Plan complete, clear storage\n\nWithout storage, you'd need to track plans yourself or regenerate them\nevery tick (expensive and inconsistent).","ref":"Operator.Storage.html#module-why-plan-storage"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Configuration - Operator.Storage","doc":"config :operator,\n      storage_module: MyApp.PlanStorage","ref":"Operator.Storage.html#module-configuration"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Example Implementations - Operator.Storage","doc":"","ref":"Operator.Storage.html#module-example-implementations"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Redis (for distributed games) - Operator.Storage","doc":"defmodule MyApp.RedisPlanStorage do\n      @behaviour Operator.Storage\n\n      @impl true\n      def persist_plan(entity_id, plan) do\n        Redix.command!(:redix, [\"SET\", \"plan:#{entity_id}\", :erlang.term_to_binary(plan)])\n        :ok\n      end\n\n      @impl true\n      def fetch_plan(entity_id) do\n        case Redix.command!(:redix, [\"GET\", \"plan:#{entity_id}\"]) do\n          nil -> nil\n          binary -> :erlang.binary_to_term(binary)\n        end\n      end\n\n      @impl true\n      def clear_plan(entity_id) do\n        Redix.command!(:redix, [\"DEL\", \"plan:#{entity_id}\"])\n        :ok\n      end\n\n      @impl true\n      def list_plans do\n        keys = Redix.command!(:redix, [\"KEYS\", \"plan:*\"])\n        Enum.map(keys, fn key ->\n          entity_id = String.replace_prefix(key, \"plan:\", \"\")\n          plan = fetch_plan(entity_id)\n          {entity_id, plan}\n        end)\n      end\n    end","ref":"Operator.Storage.html#module-redis-for-distributed-games"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"In-Memory with TTL (for single-node games) - Operator.Storage","doc":"defmodule MyApp.CachexPlanStorage do\n      @behaviour Operator.Storage\n\n      @impl true\n      def persist_plan(entity_id, plan) do\n        Cachex.put(:plans, entity_id, plan, ttl: :timer.minutes(5))\n        :ok\n      end\n\n      @impl true\n      def fetch_plan(entity_id) do\n        case Cachex.get(:plans, entity_id) do\n          {:ok, plan} -> plan\n          _ -> nil\n        end\n      end\n\n      # ... etc\n    end","ref":"Operator.Storage.html#module-in-memory-with-ttl-for-single-node-games"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Default Implementation - Operator.Storage","doc":"If no storage module is configured, Operator uses `Operator.HTN.Storage`,\nwhich provides simple ETS-based storage suitable for single-node games.","ref":"Operator.Storage.html#module-default-implementation"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"See Also - Operator.Storage","doc":"* `Operator.HTN.Storage` - Default ETS implementation\n* `Operator.HTN.Plan` - The plan structure being stored\n* `Operator.HTN.Executor` - Uses storage during plan execution","ref":"Operator.Storage.html#module-see-also"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.Storage.clear_plan/1","doc":"Clear a plan for an entity.\n\nCalled when a plan is completed, invalidated, or needs to be replaced.","ref":"Operator.Storage.html#c:clear_plan/1"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.Storage.fetch_plan/1","doc":"Fetch a plan for an entity.\n\nReturns the cached plan or `nil` if no plan exists.","ref":"Operator.Storage.html#c:fetch_plan/1"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.Storage.list_plans/0","doc":"List all stored plans.\n\nReturns a list of `{entity_id, plan}` tuples.","ref":"Operator.Storage.html#c:list_plans/0"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.Storage.persist_plan/2","doc":"Persist a plan for an entity.\n\nCalled after successful plan generation to cache the plan for later\nretrieval during execution.","ref":"Operator.Storage.html#c:persist_plan/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Storage.clear_plan/1","doc":"Clear a plan using the configured storage module.","ref":"Operator.Storage.html#clear_plan/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Storage.fetch_plan/1","doc":"Fetch a plan using the configured storage module.","ref":"Operator.Storage.html#fetch_plan/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Storage.get_module/0","doc":"Get the configured storage module or the default ETS storage.","ref":"Operator.Storage.html#get_module/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Storage.list_plans/0","doc":"List all plans using the configured storage module.","ref":"Operator.Storage.html#list_plans/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Storage.persist_plan/2","doc":"Persist a plan using the configured storage module.","ref":"Operator.Storage.html#persist_plan/2"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Operator.Storyteller","doc":"Behaviour for narrative event generators.\n\nStorytellers are the brains behind the Director's event generation. Each\nstoryteller encapsulates a different dramatic philosophy - one might favor\nconstant action, another might build tension slowly before explosive releases.","ref":"Operator.Storyteller.html"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"The Storyteller's Job - Operator.Storyteller","doc":"A storyteller answers one question each tick: \"Should something interesting\nhappen right now?\" Based on world state (tension, player health, time since\nlast event, etc.), it either returns `nil` (nothing happens) or an event\nmap that the Director will process.","ref":"Operator.Storyteller.html#module-the-storyteller-s-job"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Implementing a Storyteller - Operator.Storyteller","doc":"defmodule MyGame.DramaticStoryteller do\n      @behaviour Operator.Storyteller\n\n      @impl true\n      def init(opts) do\n        %{\n          last_event_tick: 0,\n          min_interval: Map.get(opts, :min_interval, 100),\n          tension_threshold: Map.get(opts, :tension_threshold, 0.6),\n          escalation_factor: 1.0\n        }\n      end\n\n      @impl true\n      def pick_event(tick, world_state, state) do\n        tension = Map.get(world_state, :tension, 0.0)\n        ticks_since = tick - state.last_event_tick\n\n        cond do\n          # Cooldown period - no events too close together\n          ticks_since  \n            {nil, state}\n\n          # High tension - trigger dramatic event\n          tension > state.tension_threshold ->\n            event = %{\n              type: :dramatic_encounter,\n              severity: min(5, round(tension * 5)),\n              location: pick_hotspot(world_state)\n            }\n            {event, %{state | last_event_tick: tick, escalation_factor: 1.0}}\n\n          # Low tension for too long - inject ambient event\n          ticks_since > 500 and :rand.uniform() < 0.1 ->\n            event = %{\n              type: :ambient_event,\n              severity: 1,\n              location: pick_quiet_area(world_state)\n            }\n            {event, %{state | last_event_tick: tick}}\n\n          # Nothing this tick\n          true ->\n            {nil, state}\n        end\n      end\n\n      defp pick_hotspot(world_state), do: # ...\n      defp pick_quiet_area(world_state), do: # ...\n    end","ref":"Operator.Storyteller.html#module-implementing-a-storyteller"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Storyteller Philosophies - Operator.Storyteller","doc":"Different games need different pacing. Here are some patterns:","ref":"Operator.Storyteller.html#module-storyteller-philosophies"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Tension-Release (Left 4 Dead style) - Operator.Storyteller","doc":"Build tension through enemy density and environmental cues, then release\nwith a dramatic event (horde attack, special infected spawn).","ref":"Operator.Storyteller.html#module-tension-release-left-4-dead-style"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Reactive (Nemesis system style) - Operator.Storyteller","doc":"Track player actions and generate events that respond to them. Kill a\ncaptain? His blood brother shows up for revenge.","ref":"Operator.Storyteller.html#module-reactive-nemesis-system-style"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Procedural Drama (Dwarf Fortress style) - Operator.Storyteller","doc":"Generate events based on faction relationships, resource scarcity, and\nhistorical grudges. Let chaos emerge from simulation.","ref":"Operator.Storyteller.html#module-procedural-drama-dwarf-fortress-style"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Cinematic (Scripted game style) - Operator.Storyteller","doc":"Use storyteller state to track narrative beats. First act builds world,\nsecond act introduces conflict, third act resolves it.","ref":"Operator.Storyteller.html#module-cinematic-scripted-game-style"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Event Structure - Operator.Storyteller","doc":"Events should be maps with at least a `:type` key:\n\n    %{\n      type: :event_type,           # Required: atom identifier\n      location: %{...},            # Where the event occurs\n      actors: [entity_id, ...],    # Entities involved\n      severity: 1..5,              # Event intensity\n      raw_data: %{...}             # Game-specific data\n    }\n\nThe Director passes events through `Operator.Rationalization` before\ndelivering them to your game.","ref":"Operator.Storyteller.html#module-event-structure"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"World State - Operator.Storyteller","doc":"The Director passes a `world_state` map to `pick_event/3`. Structure this\nto give storytellers the information they need:\n\n    %{\n      tick: 12345,\n      tension: 0.7,                    # 0.0 - 1.0\n      player_health_percent: 0.4,\n      summary: %{\n        total_entities: 150,\n        enemies_alive: 23,\n        by_district: %{\"downtown\" => 45, \"suburbs\" => 30}\n      },\n      recent_events: [...],            # What's happened lately\n      # ... your game's specific data\n    }","ref":"Operator.Storyteller.html#module-world-state"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Built-in Storytellers - Operator.Storyteller","doc":"* `Operator.Director.NullStoryteller` - Never generates events (for testing)","ref":"Operator.Storyteller.html#module-built-in-storytellers"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"See Also - Operator.Storyteller","doc":"* `Operator.Director` - The GenServer that calls storytellers\n* `Operator.Rationalization` - Event annotation","ref":"Operator.Storyteller.html#module-see-also"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.Storyteller.init/1","doc":"Initialize storyteller state.\n\nCalled once when the Director starts or when switching storytellers.\nReturns the initial state map that will be passed to `pick_event/3`.","ref":"Operator.Storyteller.html#c:init/1"},{"type":"callback","title":"Arguments - Operator.Storyteller.init/1","doc":"- `opts` - Configuration options passed from Director startup","ref":"Operator.Storyteller.html#c:init/1-arguments"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.Storyteller.pick_event/3","doc":"Decide whether to generate an event this tick.\n\nCalled every tick by the Director. Should return:\n- `{nil, new_state}` - No event this tick\n- `{event_map, new_state}` - Generate an event","ref":"Operator.Storyteller.html#c:pick_event/3"},{"type":"callback","title":"Arguments - Operator.Storyteller.pick_event/3","doc":"- `tick` - Current simulation tick\n- `world_state` - Map containing world information\n- `storyteller_state` - Current storyteller state from init/previous tick","ref":"Operator.Storyteller.html#c:pick_event/3-arguments"},{"type":"callback","title":"World State - Operator.Storyteller.pick_event/3","doc":"The `world_state` map typically includes:\n\n    %{\n      tick: non_neg_integer(),\n      summary: %{\n        total_entities: non_neg_integer(),\n        by_type: %{atom() => non_neg_integer()},\n        by_district: %{String.t() => non_neg_integer()}\n      },\n      reports: [...],\n      # Additional fields depend on host application\n    }","ref":"Operator.Storyteller.html#c:pick_event/3-world-state"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Operator.Telemetry","doc":"Behaviour for telemetry and metrics integration.\n\nThe Telemetry behaviour allows you to instrument Operator with your\nobservability stack. Track goal selections, plan generation times,\nand Director events for debugging and performance analysis.","ref":"Operator.Telemetry.html"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Configuration - Operator.Telemetry","doc":"config :operator,\n      telemetry_module: MyApp.OperatorTelemetry","ref":"Operator.Telemetry.html#module-configuration"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Events - Operator.Telemetry","doc":"Operator emits three types of events:\n\n| Event                | When                          | Key Measurements        |\n|----------------------|-------------------------------|-------------------------|\n| `goal_selected`      | GoalSelector picks a goal     | `:score`                |\n| `htn_plan_generated` | Planner creates a plan        | `:task_count`, duration |\n| `director_event`     | Director fires an event       | `:count`                |","ref":"Operator.Telemetry.html#module-events"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Example Implementation - Operator.Telemetry","doc":"Using the standard `:telemetry` library:\n\n    defmodule MyApp.OperatorTelemetry do\n      @behaviour Operator.Telemetry\n\n      @impl true\n      def emit_goal_selected(goal_name, measurements, metadata) do\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:my_app, :operator, :goal_selected],\n          measurements,\n          Map.put(metadata, :goal, goal_name)\n        )\n      end\n\n      @impl true\n      def emit_htn_plan_generated(goal, task_count, duration_ms) do\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:my_app, :operator, :plan_generated],\n          %{task_count: task_count, duration_ms: duration_ms},\n          %{goal: goal}\n        )\n      end\n\n      @impl true\n      def emit_director_event(event_type, tick) do\n        :telemetry.execute(\n          [:my_app, :operator, :director_event],\n          %{count: 1},\n          %{event_type: event_type, tick: tick}\n        )\n      end\n    end","ref":"Operator.Telemetry.html#module-example-implementation"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Attaching Handlers - Operator.Telemetry","doc":"With `:telemetry`, attach handlers in your application startup:\n\n    def start(_type, _args) do\n      :telemetry.attach_many(\n        \"operator-metrics\",\n        [\n          [:my_app, :operator, :goal_selected],\n          [:my_app, :operator, :plan_generated],\n          [:my_app, :operator, :director_event]\n        ],\n        &MyApp.TelemetryHandler.handle_event/4,\n        nil\n      )\n\n      # ... rest of supervision tree\n    end","ref":"Operator.Telemetry.html#module-attaching-handlers"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Prometheus Example - Operator.Telemetry","doc":"If using `telemetry_metrics` with Prometheus:\n\n    def metrics do\n      [\n        counter(\"my_app.operator.goal_selected.count\",\n          tags: [:goal, :domain]\n        ),\n        distribution(\"my_app.operator.plan_generated.duration_ms\",\n          tags: [:goal],\n          buckets: [1, 5, 10, 25, 50, 100]\n        ),\n        counter(\"my_app.operator.director_event.count\",\n          tags: [:event_type]\n        )\n      ]\n    end","ref":"Operator.Telemetry.html#module-prometheus-example"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"No-Op Default - Operator.Telemetry","doc":"If no telemetry module is configured, Operator silently skips emission.\nThis has zero overhead in production when telemetry isn't needed.","ref":"Operator.Telemetry.html#module-no-op-default"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"See Also - Operator.Telemetry","doc":"* `Operator.HTN.GoalSelector` - Emits `goal_selected`\n* `Operator.HTN.Planner` - Emits `htn_plan_generated`\n* `Operator.Director` - Emits `director_event`","ref":"Operator.Telemetry.html#module-see-also"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.Telemetry.emit_director_event/2","doc":"Emit telemetry when the Director generates an event.\n\nCalled by `Director` when a storyteller produces an event.","ref":"Operator.Telemetry.html#c:emit_director_event/2"},{"type":"callback","title":"Arguments - Operator.Telemetry.emit_director_event/2","doc":"- `event_type` - The type of event generated\n- `tick` - The simulation tick when the event occurred","ref":"Operator.Telemetry.html#c:emit_director_event/2-arguments"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.Telemetry.emit_goal_selected/3","doc":"Emit telemetry when a goal is selected.\n\nCalled by `GoalSelector.pick_goal/3` when a goal is chosen.","ref":"Operator.Telemetry.html#c:emit_goal_selected/3"},{"type":"callback","title":"Arguments - Operator.Telemetry.emit_goal_selected/3","doc":"- `goal_name` - The selected goal atom (or `:none` if no goal selected)\n- `measurements` - Map containing at least `:score`\n- `metadata` - Additional context (goal_metadata, domain, etc.)","ref":"Operator.Telemetry.html#c:emit_goal_selected/3-arguments"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.Telemetry.emit_htn_plan_generated/3","doc":"Emit telemetry when an HTN plan is generated.\n\nCalled by `Planner.run/3` after successful plan generation.","ref":"Operator.Telemetry.html#c:emit_htn_plan_generated/3"},{"type":"callback","title":"Arguments - Operator.Telemetry.emit_htn_plan_generated/3","doc":"- `goal` - The goal that was planned\n- `task_count` - Number of tasks in the generated plan\n- `duration_ms` - Time taken to generate the plan","ref":"Operator.Telemetry.html#c:emit_htn_plan_generated/3-arguments"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Telemetry.emit_director_event/2","doc":"Emit director event if telemetry is configured.","ref":"Operator.Telemetry.html#emit_director_event/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Telemetry.emit_goal_selected/3","doc":"Emit goal selected event if telemetry is configured.","ref":"Operator.Telemetry.html#emit_goal_selected/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Telemetry.emit_htn_plan_generated/3","doc":"Emit plan generated event if telemetry is configured.","ref":"Operator.Telemetry.html#emit_htn_plan_generated/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Telemetry.get_module/0","doc":"Get the configured telemetry module, if any.","ref":"Operator.Telemetry.html#get_module/0"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Operator.Traits","doc":"Behaviour for agent personality and genome integration.\n\nThe Traits system allows you to influence HTN goal selection based on\nagent-specific attributes like personality traits, genetic makeup, or\ncharacter class. This creates emergent behavior where aggressive NPCs\nprefer combat goals while cautious ones prefer stealth.","ref":"Operator.Traits.html"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"How It Works - Operator.Traits","doc":"During goal selection, the `GoalSelector` calls trait functions to compute\nbonus scores for each goal. Goals with higher affinity for an agent's\ntraits score higher and are more likely to be selected.\n\n```\nGoal Score = base_priority + trait_bonus + archetype_bonus + ...\n```","ref":"Operator.Traits.html#module-how-it-works"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Configuration - Operator.Traits","doc":"config :operator,\n      traits_module: MyApp.OperatorTraits","ref":"Operator.Traits.html#module-configuration"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Implementing the Behaviour - Operator.Traits","doc":"defmodule MyApp.OperatorTraits do\n      @behaviour Operator.Traits\n\n      @impl true\n      def traits(genome) do\n        # Extract trait atoms from your genome/personality data\n        # Genome can be any data structure your game uses\n        Map.get(genome, :traits, [])\n      end\n\n      @impl true\n      def trait_affinity_score(genome, goal_metadata) do\n        # Return a numeric bonus based on trait-goal compatibility\n        # Higher scores make the goal more attractive\n        weights = Map.get(goal_metadata, :trait_weights, %{})\n        my_traits = traits(genome)\n\n        Enum.reduce(my_traits, 0, fn trait, acc ->\n          acc + Map.get(weights, trait, 0)\n        end)\n      end\n\n      @impl true\n      def archetype_affinity_score(genome, goal_metadata) do\n        # Archetype is a higher-level categorization (warrior, mage, etc.)\n        archetype = Map.get(genome, :archetype)\n        weights = Map.get(goal_metadata, :archetype_weights, %{})\n        Map.get(weights, archetype, 0)\n      end\n    end","ref":"Operator.Traits.html#module-implementing-the-behaviour"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Example: Combat vs Stealth Goals - Operator.Traits","doc":"Define goals with trait weights in metadata:\n\n    goal :frontal_assault do\n      decompose do\n        task :charge_enemy\n        task :melee_attack\n      end\n      metadata trait_weights: %{aggressive: 3, brave: 2}\n    end\n\n    goal :sneak_attack do\n      decompose do\n        task :find_shadows\n        task :backstab\n      end\n      metadata trait_weights: %{sneaky: 3, patient: 2}\n    end\n\nNow an agent with `traits: [:aggressive, :brave]` will score +5 for\n`:frontal_assault` but +0 for `:sneak_attack`, making them prefer\ndirect combat.","ref":"Operator.Traits.html#module-example-combat-vs-stealth-goals"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Archetype System - Operator.Traits","doc":"Archetypes are coarser categories than traits. A \"warrior\" archetype\nmight encompass both \"aggressive\" and \"brave\" traits:\n\n    goal :defend_ally do\n      metadata archetype_weights: %{warrior: 5, paladin: 7}\n    end","ref":"Operator.Traits.html#module-archetype-system"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"Default Implementation - Operator.Traits","doc":"If no traits module is configured, Operator uses sensible defaults:\n\n* `traits/1` - Returns `genome[:traits]` or empty list\n* `trait_affinity_score/2` - Uses `metadata[:trait_weights]`\n* `archetype_affinity_score/2` - Uses `metadata[:archetype_weights]`","ref":"Operator.Traits.html#module-default-implementation"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"See Also - Operator.Traits","doc":"* `Operator.HTN.GoalSelector` - Uses traits for goal scoring\n* `Operator.HTN.DSL` - Define trait weights in goal metadata","ref":"Operator.Traits.html#module-see-also"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.Traits.genome/0","doc":"","ref":"Operator.Traits.html#t:genome/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Operator.Traits.metadata/0","doc":"","ref":"Operator.Traits.html#t:metadata/0"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.Traits.archetype_affinity_score/2","doc":"Score archetype-specific affinity.\n\nArchetypes are higher-level categorizations (e.g., \"warrior\", \"thief\")\nthat can influence goal selection.","ref":"Operator.Traits.html#c:archetype_affinity_score/2"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.Traits.trait_affinity_score/2","doc":"Score how well an agent's traits match goal metadata.\n\nReturns a numeric bonus to add to goal priority scoring.","ref":"Operator.Traits.html#c:trait_affinity_score/2"},{"type":"callback","title":"Operator.Traits.traits/1","doc":"Return the list of trait atoms for a genome.\n\nTraits are used in goal selection to weight certain goals higher\nfor agents with matching traits.","ref":"Operator.Traits.html#c:traits/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Traits.archetype_affinity_score/2","doc":"Calculate archetype affinity score, using configured module or defaults.","ref":"Operator.Traits.html#archetype_affinity_score/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Traits.get_module/0","doc":"Get the configured traits module.","ref":"Operator.Traits.html#get_module/0"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Traits.trait_affinity_score/2","doc":"Calculate trait affinity score, using configured module or defaults.","ref":"Operator.Traits.html#trait_affinity_score/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Operator.Traits.traits/1","doc":"Get traits for a genome, using configured module or defaults.","ref":"Operator.Traits.html#traits/1"},{"type":"extras","title":"Operator","doc":"# Operator\n\nWelcome to Operator. We're done here.\n\nJust kidding. But seriously, if you've ever watched an NPC walk into a wall for six hours because someone forgot to tell it that doors exist, you know why this library exists. We built Operator because game AI deserves better than a pile of if-statements held together with prayers and energy drinks.\n\nOperator gives you two things:\n\n- **HTN Planning** - Your NPCs will actually *think*. Goals break down into tasks, tasks break down into actions, and suddenly your village blacksmith stops trying to forge swords in the middle of a lake.\n- **Director** - A narrative orchestration system that decides when interesting things should happen. Think Left 4 Dead's AI Director, but you're the one holding the reins.","ref":"readme.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Installation - Operator","doc":"```elixir\ndef deps do\n  [\n    {:operator, \"~> 0.1.0\"}\n  ]\nend\n```\n\nThat's it. No C dependencies. No NIFs that only compile on a full moon. Just pure Elixir.","ref":"readme.html#installation"},{"type":"extras","title":"Quick Start (5 Minutes) - Operator","doc":"This is the smallest end-to-end loop that proves the library works. You can copy it\ninto a scratch module and expand from there.\n\n1. Define a behavior module.\n1. Build facts.\n1. Plan.\n1. Execute one step.\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyGame.QuickstartBehavior do\n  use Operator.HTN.DSL\n\n  goal :patrol do\n    precond fn facts ->\n      Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:self, :energy}, 0) > 10\n    end\n\n    decompose do\n      task :move_to, :waypoint_1\n      task :look_around\n      task :move_to, :waypoint_2\n      task :look_around\n    end\n\n    metadata priority: 3, domain: :routine\n  end\n\n  primitive :move_to, waypoint do\n    run fn actor, _facts ->\n      {:ok, %{actor | position: waypoint}}\n    end\n  end\n\n  primitive :look_around do\n    run fn actor, _facts ->\n      {:ok, actor}\n    end\n  end\nend\n\nalias Operator.HTN.{Executor, Facts, Planner}\n\nfacts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{energy: 50}})\ntraits = %{archetype: :guard}\nactor = %{id: 1, position: :start}\n\n{:ok, plan} = Planner.run(:patrol, facts, traits)\n{:ok, :continue, actor, facts, remaining} = Executor.step(plan, actor, facts)\n```\n\nIf that runs, you are up and planning. Everything else is just richer behaviors.","ref":"readme.html#quick-start-5-minutes"},{"type":"extras","title":"Guides And References - Operator","doc":"For fast adoption, start here:\n\n- [Getting Started](guides/getting_started.md) for the full walkthrough.\n- [How-To](guides/howto.md) for practical recipes.\n- [Cheatsheet](guides/cheatsheet.md) for a quick API map.\n- [Testing](guides/testing.md) for safe Registry usage and isolation.\n- [Debugging](guides/debugging.md) for tracing and plan introspection.\n- [DSL Reference](guides/dsl_reference.md) for a full HTN DSL reference.\n- [Architecture](guides/architecture.md) for system-level flow and scaling.\n- [Director](guides/director.md) for narrative pacing and events.\n- [Best Practices](guides/best_practices.md) for pragmatic, production-oriented guidance.\n- [Anti-Patterns](guides/anti_patterns.md) for common failure modes and fixes.\n\nThe generated API docs live in `doc/` after `mix docs`.","ref":"readme.html#guides-and-references"},{"type":"extras","title":"Adoption Checklist - Operator","doc":"Treat this as a ruthless, practical path to production.\n\n1. Define one behavior module with one goal, one task, one primitive.\n1. Hook `Planner.run/3` into a single entity.\n1. Use `Executor.step/3` in your game loop.\n1. Add a facts builder and keep it deterministic.\n1. Add tests with `Operator.HTN.TestHelpers` and `async: false`.\n1. Add tracing while you tune behaviors, then disable it.\n1. Add storage only if your plans span multiple ticks.\n1. Add the Director only when you want global pacing.\n1. Use `GoalSelector.explain/3` and `Planner.explain/3` to debug decisions.\n1. Add planning budgets once you scale beyond a handful of agents.","ref":"readme.html#adoption-checklist"},{"type":"extras","title":"HTN Planning (or: Teaching Rocks to Think) - Operator","doc":"HTN stands for Hierarchical Task Network. The idea came from some very smart people who got tired of writing behavior trees that looked like spaghetti painted by Jackson Pollock.\n\nHere's the deal: you define **goals** (what the NPC wants), **tasks** (how to break that down), and **primitives** (the actual buttons to press). The planner figures out the rest.","ref":"readme.html#htn-planning-or-teaching-rocks-to-think"},{"type":"extras","title":"Defining Behavior - Operator","doc":"```elixir\ndefmodule MyGame.NPCBehavior do\n  use Operator.HTN.DSL\n\n  # \"I want data and I want it now\"\n  goal :acquire_data do\n    # IMPORTANT: Use full module paths in precond/decompose functions!\n    # Aliases from your module header don't work here - these functions\n    # are evaluated at runtime in a different scope.\n    precond fn facts ->\n      not Operator.HTN.Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :has_data})\n    end\n\n    decompose do\n      task :go_to_terminal\n      task :download_data, \"target_server\"\n    end\n\n    metadata priority: 5, domain: :infiltration\n  end\n\n  # \"Getting there is half the battle\"\n  task :go_to_terminal do\n    precond fn facts ->\n      Operator.HTN.Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :can_move})\n    end\n\n    decompose fn facts ->\n      terminal = Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:world, :nearest_terminal})\n      [{:move_to, [terminal]}]\n    end\n\n    cost 2.0\n  end\n\n  # \"The part where things actually happen\"\n  primitive :download_data, target do\n    run fn actor, _facts ->\n      # Your game logic here. We're not picky.\n      {:ok, actor}\n    end\n\n    metadata action_type: :interact\n  end\nend\n```\n\n> **Heads up:** Functions inside `precond` and `decompose` blocks are evaluated at runtime, which means your module's `alias` statements won't work inside them. Always use full module paths like `Operator.HTN.Facts.get(...)` instead of `Facts.get(...)`.","ref":"readme.html#defining-behavior"},{"type":"extras","title":"Making Plans Happen - Operator","doc":"```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.{Facts, Plan, Planner}\n\n# What does your NPC know about the world?\nfacts = Facts.from_perception(%{\n  self: %{can_move: true, has_data: false},\n  world: %{nearest_terminal: :server_room}\n})\n\n# Or start with empty facts\nfacts = Facts.new()\n\n# What kind of NPC is this?\ntraits = %{archetype: :infiltrator, traits: [:stealthy]}\n\n# Let's see what we've got\ncase Planner.run(:acquire_data, facts, traits) do\n  {:ok, plan} ->\n    IO.inspect(plan.tasks)\n    # => [{:move_to, [:server_room]}, {:download_data, [\"target_server\"]}]\n    # Look at that. A real plan. Made by a computer.\n\n  {:error, :preconditions_not_met} ->\n    # Can't get blood from a stone\n    :retry_later\n\n  {:error, :goal_not_found} ->\n    # You asked for a goal that doesn't exist. Classic.\n    :unknown_goal\nend\n```","ref":"readme.html#making-plans-happen"},{"type":"extras","title":"Loop Helper (Less Boilerplate) - Operator","doc":"If you want to wire planning into a tick loop quickly:\n\n```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Loop\n\nresult = Loop.tick(entity.plan, entity, facts, traits, goal: :patrol)\n```","ref":"readme.html#loop-helper-less-boilerplate"},{"type":"extras","title":"Executing Plans - Operator","doc":"Plans are just data - sequences of primitives to execute. The `Executor` module handles the messy business of actually running them:\n\n```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.{Executor, Planner}\n\n# Generate a plan\n{:ok, plan} = Planner.run(:patrol, facts, traits)\n\n# Execute step by step (recommended for game loops)\ncase Executor.step(plan, npc, facts) do\n  {:ok, :completed, npc, facts, _plan} ->\n    # All done!\n    {:idle, npc, facts}\n\n  {:ok, :continue, npc, facts, remaining_plan} ->\n    # More to do - store remaining plan for next tick\n    {:running, %{npc | plan: remaining_plan}, facts}\n\n  {:error, reason, npc, facts, _plan} ->\n    # Something went wrong - maybe replan\n    {:failed, %{npc | plan: nil}, facts}\nend\n\n# Or run the whole plan at once (useful for turn-based games)\ncase Executor.run_plan(plan, npc, facts) do\n  {:ok, npc, facts} ->\n    # Everything worked\n    :done\n\n  {:error, reason, npc, facts, remaining} ->\n    # Failed partway through\n    :partial_failure\nend\n```","ref":"readme.html#executing-plans"},{"type":"extras","title":"Effects: The Secret Sauce - Operator","doc":"Here's where it gets spicy. When the planner is figuring out what to do, it can *simulate* the effects of actions. Your NPC can reason about unlocking a door *before* it tries to walk through it.\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyGame.DoorBehavior do\n  use Operator.HTN.DSL\n\n  goal :enter_locked_room do\n    precond fn facts ->\n      not Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:world, :in_room}, false)\n    end\n\n    decompose do\n      task :unlock_door\n      task :enter_room\n    end\n  end\n\n  primitive :unlock_door do\n    run fn actor, _facts ->\n      # Unlock animation, key consumption, etc.\n      {:ok, actor}\n    end\n\n    # This effect is applied DURING PLANNING so :enter_room knows\n    # the door will be unlocked by the time it runs\n    effect Operator.HTN.Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:world, :door_unlocked}, true)\n  end\n\n  primitive :enter_room do\n    # This precondition passes during planning because :unlock_door's\n    # effect has already been applied to the planning state\n    precond fn facts ->\n      Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:world, :door_unlocked}, false)\n    end\n\n    run fn actor, _facts ->\n      {:ok, %{actor | location: :room}}\n    end\n\n    effect Operator.HTN.Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:world, :in_room}, true)\n  end\nend\n```\n\n**Effect flavors:**\n- `:plan_only` - \"Let's pretend this happened\" (planning only, ignored during execution)\n- `:plan_and_execute` - \"This will actually happen\" (applied during both planning and execution)\n- `:permanent` - \"This happened and nothing can undo it\" (persists even on task failure)","ref":"readme.html#effects-the-secret-sauce"},{"type":"extras","title":"Automatic Goal Selection - Operator","doc":"Don't want to micromanage which goal your NPC pursues? Let the `GoalSelector` handle it:\n\n```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.{GoalSelector, Planner}\n\ncase GoalSelector.pick_goal(facts, traits) do\n  {:ok, goal_name} ->\n    Planner.run(goal_name, facts, traits)\n\n  :none ->\n    # Nothing to do. Time to stand around looking mysterious.\n    :idle\nend\n```","ref":"readme.html#automatic-goal-selection"},{"type":"extras","title":"Common Gotchas (Read This) - Operator","doc":"- Use full module paths inside `precond` and `decompose` functions. Aliases do not work there.\n- The Registry is global state. Use `async: false` for tests that touch it.\n- Facts are immutable. Always use the returned facts after `Effect` or `Facts.put/3`.\n- Plans are data. If you mutate the actor, keep facts in sync.\n- Do not run `Planner.run/3` inside tight loops without caching if the world state is stable.\n- Use `Planner.needs_replan?/2` before throwing away a plan.","ref":"readme.html#common-gotchas-read-this"},{"type":"extras","title":"The Director (or: Playing God, Responsibly) - Operator","doc":"Ever play a game where nothing happens for twenty minutes and then everything happens at once? That's bad directing. The Director system lets you control the *pacing* of your simulation.\n\nYou write a **Storyteller** that decides when and what events should fire based on the current world state. Tension too low? Spawn a wandering merchant. Tension too high? Maybe hold off on that dragon attack.","ref":"readme.html#the-director-or-playing-god-responsibly"},{"type":"extras","title":"Writing a Storyteller - Operator","doc":"```elixir\ndefmodule MyGame.DramaticStoryteller do\n  @behaviour Operator.Storyteller\n\n  @impl true\n  def init(opts) do\n    %{\n      last_event_tick: 0,\n      tension_threshold: Map.get(opts, :tension_threshold, 0.7)\n    }\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def pick_event(tick, world_state, state) do\n    tension = Map.get(world_state, :tension, 0.0)\n\n    if tension > state.tension_threshold do\n      event = %{\n        type: :dramatic_confrontation,\n        location: pick_location(world_state),\n        severity: 4\n      }\n      {event, %{state | last_event_tick: tick}}\n    else\n      {nil, state}  # Sometimes the best event is no event\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp pick_location(world_state) do\n    %{district: \"downtown\"}  # Your logic here\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"readme.html#writing-a-storyteller"},{"type":"extras","title":"Running the Show - Operator","doc":"```elixir\n{:ok, _pid} = Operator.Director.start_link(\n  storyteller: MyGame.DramaticStoryteller,\n  on_event: fn event ->\n    MyGame.EventHandler.process(event)\n  end\n)\n\n# Every tick, feed it the world state\nOperator.Director.tick(%{\n  tick: current_tick,\n  tension: world_tension,\n  summary: %{total_entities: 150}\n})\n```","ref":"readme.html#running-the-show"},{"type":"extras","title":"Director + HTN Integration - Operator","doc":"The Director generates world events; HTN planning lets NPCs react to them:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyGame.AILoop do\n  alias Operator.HTN.{Executor, Facts, GoalSelector, Planner}\n\n  def tick(entity, world_state, director_events) do\n    # Build facts from perception + any director events\n    facts = build_facts(entity, world_state, director_events)\n    traits = entity.traits\n\n    case entity.current_plan do\n      nil ->\n        # No plan - pick a goal and make one\n        case GoalSelector.pick_goal(facts, traits) do\n          {:ok, goal} ->\n            case Planner.run(goal, facts, traits) do\n              {:ok, plan} -> %{entity | current_plan: plan}\n              {:error, _} -> entity\n            end\n\n          :none ->\n            entity  # Idle\n        end\n\n      plan ->\n        # Execute one step of current plan\n        case Executor.step(plan, entity, facts) do\n          {:ok, :completed, entity, _facts, _plan} ->\n            %{entity | current_plan: nil}\n\n          {:ok, :continue, entity, _facts, remaining} ->\n            %{entity | current_plan: remaining}\n\n          {:error, _reason, entity, _facts, _plan} ->\n            # Plan failed - will replan next tick\n            %{entity | current_plan: nil}\n        end\n    end\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"readme.html#director-htn-integration"},{"type":"extras","title":"Registry API - Operator","doc":"The registry stores all registered goals, tasks, primitives, and axioms:\n\n```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Registry\n\n# Get specific items by name\ngoal = Registry.get_goal(:patrol)\ntask = Registry.get_task(:move_to)\nprimitive = Registry.get_primitive(:attack)\naxiom = Registry.get_axiom(:enemy_nearby)\n\n# List all registered names\nRegistry.list_goal_names()      # => [:patrol, :attack, :flee]\nRegistry.list_primitive_names() # => [:move, :strike, :block]\n\n# Get the full registry map\nregistry = Registry.all()\n# => %{goals: %{...}, tasks: %{...}, primitives: %{...}, axioms: %{...}}\n\n# Stats\nRegistry.stats()\n# => %{goals: 5, tasks: 12, primitives: 8, axioms: 3}\n```","ref":"readme.html#registry-api"},{"type":"extras","title":"Testing - Operator","doc":"The Registry uses `persistent_term` for fast lookups, which means tests need some care:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyApp.BehaviorTest do\n  use ExUnit.Case, async: false  # Important!\n\n  import Operator.HTN.TestHelpers\n\n  alias Operator.HTN.{Facts, Plan, Planner}\n\n  # Reset registry before each test\n  setup :reset_registry\n\n  # Register your behavior module(s)\n  setup do\n    register_modules([MyApp.NPCBehavior])\n    :ok\n  end\n\n  test \"patrol goal generates valid plan\" do\n    facts = Facts.from_perception(%{\n      self: %{on_duty: true, can_move: true}\n    })\n\n    {:ok, plan} = Planner.run(:patrol, facts, %{})\n\n    assert Plan.has_tasks?(plan)\n    assert_has_task(plan, :walk_to_waypoint)\n  end\nend\n```\n\nKey points:\n- Use `async: false` - the Registry is global state\n- Call `reset_registry` in setup to ensure clean state\n- Use `register_modules/1` to register your behavior modules\n- See `Operator.HTN.TestHelpers` for more utilities\n\n```bash\nmix test\n```\n\nRun it. Keep it green.","ref":"readme.html#testing"},{"type":"extras","title":"Performance Notes - Operator","doc":"The planner is optimized for many reads and few writes. Registry reads are\n`persistent_term` lookups and are effectively free. Planning cost scales with\nthe breadth of your decomposition and the number of preconditions. Keep your\nfacts small, avoid heavy IO inside tasks, and use tracing only while debugging.","ref":"readme.html#performance-notes"},{"type":"extras","title":"Configuration - Operator","doc":"Operator is pluggable. Don't like how we do something? Swap it out.\n\n```elixir\nconfig :operator,\n  telemetry_module: MyApp.OperatorTelemetry,      # Your metrics, your way\n  traits_module: MyApp.OperatorTraits,            # Custom genome/personality system\n  storage_module: Operator.HTN.Storage,           # Where plans live (default: ETS)\n  rationalization_module: MyApp.OperatorRationalization,  # Plan annotation\n\n  # Weight certain trait+goal combinations\n  htn_trait_weights: %{\n    {:aggressive, :attack} => 5,\n    {:cautious, :scout} => 3\n  }\n```","ref":"readme.html#configuration"},{"type":"extras","title":"Behaviours - Operator","doc":"We expose several behaviours so you can integrate Operator with whatever bizarre architecture you've already committed to.","ref":"readme.html#behaviours"},{"type":"extras","title":"Telemetry - Operator","doc":"```elixir\ndefmodule MyApp.OperatorTelemetry do\n  @behaviour Operator.Telemetry\n\n  @impl true\n  def emit_goal_selected(goal_name, measurements, metadata) do\n    :telemetry.execute([:my_app, :htn, :goal_selected], measurements, metadata)\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def emit_htn_plan_generated(goal, task_count, duration_ms) do\n    :telemetry.execute([:my_app, :htn, :plan_generated],\n      %{task_count: task_count, duration: duration_ms},\n      %{goal: goal})\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def emit_director_event(event_type, tick) do\n    :telemetry.execute([:my_app, :director, :event],\n      %{count: 1},\n      %{type: event_type, tick: tick})\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"readme.html#telemetry"},{"type":"extras","title":"Traits - Operator","doc":"```elixir\ndefmodule MyApp.OperatorTraits do\n  @behaviour Operator.Traits\n\n  @impl true\n  def traits(genome), do: Map.get(genome, :traits, [])\n\n  @impl true\n  def trait_affinity_score(genome, metadata) do\n    # How much does this agent want to do this thing?\n    0\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def archetype_affinity_score(genome, metadata) do\n    # Warriors gonna war, healers gonna heal\n    0\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"readme.html#traits"},{"type":"extras","title":"Storage - Operator","doc":"```elixir\ndefmodule MyApp.PlanStorage do\n  @behaviour Operator.Storage\n\n  @impl true\n  def persist_plan(entity_id, plan) do\n    MyApp.Cache.put({:plan, entity_id}, plan)\n    :ok\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def fetch_plan(entity_id) do\n    MyApp.Cache.get({:plan, entity_id})\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def clear_plan(entity_id) do\n    MyApp.Cache.delete({:plan, entity_id})\n    :ok\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def list_plans do\n    MyApp.Cache.list_by_prefix(:plan)\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"readme.html#storage"},{"type":"extras","title":"Examples - Operator","doc":"Check out the `examples/` directory. We've got:\n\n- **game_npc** - Combat, patrol, survival behaviors\n- **web_scraper** - Yes, you can use HTN for web scraping. We won't judge.\n- **job_worker** - Background job orchestration\n- **chatbot** - Conversation flow management\n- **simulation** - Multi-agent chaos with the Director","ref":"readme.html#examples"},{"type":"extras","title":"Module Index - Operator","doc":"**Core HTN:**\n- `Operator.HTN.DSL` - Macro-based DSL for defining behaviors\n- `Operator.HTN.Facts` - World state representation\n- `Operator.HTN.Plan` - Generated plan structure\n- `Operator.HTN.Planner` - High-level planning API\n- `Operator.HTN.Executor` - Plan and task execution\n- `Operator.HTN.Engine` - Low-level plan expansion\n- `Operator.HTN.Loop` - Tick-based planning/execution helper\n- `Operator.HTN.Registry` - Goal/task/primitive storage\n- `Operator.HTN.Effect` - World state modifications\n- `Operator.HTN.Task` - Task definitions\n- `Operator.HTN.Axiom` - Reusable query patterns\n- `Operator.HTN.Precondition` - Logical operators\n- `Operator.HTN.GoalSelector` - Automatic goal selection\n- `Operator.HTN.TestHelpers` - Testing utilities\n\n**Director:**\n- `Operator.Director` - Event orchestration GenServer\n- `Operator.Storyteller` - Storyteller behaviour\n\n**Integration:**\n- `Operator.Telemetry` - Metrics callbacks\n- `Operator.Traits` - Personality/genome integration\n- `Operator.Storage` - Plan persistence\n- `Operator.Rationalization` - Plan annotation","ref":"readme.html#module-index"},{"type":"extras","title":"Why \"Operator\"? - Operator","doc":"Because your NPCs are finally going to operate like they have a brain cell or two. Also it sounds cool.","ref":"readme.html#why-operator"},{"type":"extras","title":"License - Operator","doc":"MIT. Do whatever you want. Make something great.","ref":"readme.html#license"},{"type":"extras","title":"Changelog","doc":"# Changelog\n\nAll notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\n\nThe format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),\nand this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).\n\n## [Unreleased]\n\n## [0.1.0] - 2025-02-01","ref":"changelog.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Added - Changelog","doc":"#### HTN Planning System\n- `Operator.HTN.DSL` - Declarative macro-based DSL for defining goals, tasks, and primitives\n- `Operator.HTN.Planner` - High-level planning API with `plan/3`, `plan_and_execute/3`, and `execute/2`\n- `Operator.HTN.Engine` - Core plan generation algorithm with backtracking support\n- `Operator.HTN.Facts` - World state representation with nested path access\n- `Operator.HTN.Plan` - Generated plan structure with step tracking and execution state\n- `Operator.HTN.Task` - Task definition struct with preconditions and effects\n- `Operator.HTN.Effect` - World state modifications (set, delete, increment, decrement, append, remove)\n- `Operator.HTN.Precondition` - Logical operators (AND, OR, NOT) for complex conditions\n- `Operator.HTN.Axiom` - Reusable query patterns for common precondition logic\n- `Operator.HTN.GoalSelector` - Automatic goal selection with trait-based weighting\n- `Operator.HTN.Registry` - ETS-based goal and task registration\n- `Operator.HTN.Storage` - Default ETS-based plan persistence\n- `Operator.HTN.Trace` - Debug tracing infrastructure with pluggable handlers\n\n#### Director System\n- `Operator.Director` - GenServer for tick-based event orchestration\n- `Operator.Director.Storyteller` - Behaviour for implementing narrative event generators\n- `Operator.Director.NullStoryteller` - Default no-op storyteller implementation\n\n#### Integration Behaviours\n- `Operator.Telemetry` - Callbacks for metrics and observability integration\n- `Operator.Traits` - Agent personality/genome integration for goal weighting\n- `Operator.Storage` - Pluggable plan persistence backend behaviour\n- `Operator.Rationalization` - Plan annotation and event rationalization callbacks\n\n#### Documentation & Examples\n- Comprehensive README with quick start guide\n- Detailed moduledocs for all public modules\n- Five complete example applications:\n  - `game_npc` - NPC AI with patrol, combat, and survival behaviors\n  - `web_scraper` - Intelligent web scraping with retry/fallback\n  - `job_worker` - Background job orchestration with dependencies\n  - `chatbot` - Conversation flow management\n  - `simulation` - Agent-based simulation with Director events\n\n[Unreleased]: https://github.com/gamedev-company/operator/compare/v0.1.0...HEAD\n[0.1.0]: https://github.com/gamedev-company/operator/releases/tag/v0.1.0","ref":"changelog.html#added"},{"type":"extras","title":"Architecture","doc":"# Architecture\n\nThis guide explains the data flow so you can reason about performance and\nintegration points.","ref":"architecture.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"High-Level Flow - Architecture","doc":"1. Behavior modules define goals, tasks, primitives, axioms.\n1. The Registry collects those definitions.\n1. Facts capture the world state for an agent.\n1. The Planner expands a goal into a plan.\n1. The Executor steps through the plan.\n1. Effects mutate facts during planning and execution.","ref":"architecture.html#high-level-flow"},{"type":"extras","title":"Data Model - Architecture","doc":"Facts are a plain struct with three maps:\n\n- `:self` for agent state.\n- `:world` for environment state.\n- `:social` for relationships and factions.\n\nPlans are immutable structs:\n\n- `:goal` the selected objective.\n- `:tasks` the remaining primitive tasks.\n- `:validity` active, invalid, completed.\n- `:metadata` for trace and instrumentation.","ref":"architecture.html#data-model"},{"type":"extras","title":"Registry Model - Architecture","doc":"The Registry stores definitions in `persistent_term` for fast reads.\n\n- Reads are O(1).\n- Writes are expensive and should be rare.","ref":"architecture.html#registry-model"},{"type":"extras","title":"Runtime vs Compile Time - Architecture","doc":"The DSL is compiled into structs, but `precond` and `decompose` run at runtime.\nPreconditions are stored as a list of conditions and evaluated through\n`Operator.HTN.Precondition`. This is why aliases do not work inside them.","ref":"architecture.html#runtime-vs-compile-time"},{"type":"extras","title":"Replanning Strategy - Architecture","doc":"Use this approach for predictable behavior:\n\n1. Keep the current plan if it still applies.\n1. Call `Planner.needs_replan?/2` before discarding it.\n1. Replan only when facts change materially.","ref":"architecture.html#replanning-strategy"},{"type":"extras","title":"Scaling Tips - Architecture","doc":"- Keep facts small and focused.\n- Avoid heavy work inside `precond` and `decompose`.\n- Use tracing only when needed.\n- Cache expensive facts outside the planner.","ref":"architecture.html#scaling-tips"},{"type":"extras","title":"Best Practices","doc":"# Best Practices\n\nThis is the aggressive, practical guidance for using Operator in real systems.","ref":"best_practices.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Core HTN Practices - Best Practices","doc":"- Keep goals small and specific. Large, vague goals lead to unstable plans.\n- Prefer shallow decompositions. Deep trees are harder to debug and tune.\n- Keep `precond` functions pure and fast. Do not hit IO or external state.\n  Preconditions are evaluated via `Operator.HTN.Precondition`.\n- Use `Facts` as a snapshot, not a database. Keep it compact.\n- Use `cost` to shape behavior. If two paths are valid, costs decide the plan.\n- Keep primitives deterministic. If you need randomness, isolate it upstream.","ref":"best_practices.html#core-htn-practices"},{"type":"extras","title":"Facts Discipline - Best Practices","doc":"- Build facts in one place. Do not scatter facts creation across codepaths.\n- Use consistent keys. Changing keys breaks preconditions silently.\n- Treat facts as immutable. Always use the returned struct after updates.\n- Declare required fact keys in goal metadata (`requires_facts`) for validation.","ref":"best_practices.html#facts-discipline"},{"type":"extras","title":"Planning Discipline - Best Practices","doc":"- Use `Planner.needs_replan?/2` before throwing away a plan.\n- Avoid planning every tick unless the world is highly volatile.\n- Cache plans for multi-tick actions; replan only when facts change.\n- Use budgets for large NPC counts to cap planning cost.","ref":"best_practices.html#planning-discipline"},{"type":"extras","title":"Task And Goal Design - Best Practices","doc":"- Put preconditions on the highest level that makes sense.\n- Keep goal preconditions strict enough to avoid garbage plans.\n- Prefer small primitives that do one thing well.\n- Use metadata for analytics and tuning (`priority`, `domain`, etc.).","ref":"best_practices.html#task-and-goal-design"},{"type":"extras","title":"Effects - Best Practices","doc":"- Use effects to allow multi-step reasoning.\n- Use `:plan_only` for optimistic assumptions you do not want executed.\n- Use `:permanent` only for irreversible world changes.","ref":"best_practices.html#effects"},{"type":"extras","title":"Director + Storyteller - Best Practices","doc":"- Keep storytellers deterministic. You want reproducible event streams in tests.\n- Use Director events as facts, not direct commands. Let HTN decide response.\n- Control global pacing in the Director; keep per-agent intent in HTN.","ref":"best_practices.html#director-storyteller"},{"type":"extras","title":"Debugging Strategy - Best Practices","doc":"- Turn on tracing early during behavior tuning.\n- Inspect plans directly. The plan is just data.\n- Add metadata to plans to track why they were selected.\n- Use `GoalSelector.explain/3` and `Planner.explain/3` for deterministic diagnostics.","ref":"best_practices.html#debugging-strategy"},{"type":"extras","title":"Testing Strategy - Best Practices","doc":"- Always `async: false` for tests that touch the Registry.\n- Reset the Registry per test.\n- Use `with_registry/2` for isolation.\n- Write at least one integration test that runs planning + execution end-to-end.","ref":"best_practices.html#testing-strategy"},{"type":"extras","title":"Scaling Strategy - Best Practices","doc":"- Precompute expensive facts outside the planner.\n- Keep planning on a budget (limit ticks/agents per frame).\n- Use per-entity plan storage to avoid recomputation.","ref":"best_practices.html#scaling-strategy"},{"type":"extras","title":"Common Failure Modes - Best Practices","doc":"- Preconditions referencing keys that never exist in facts.\n- Aliases inside `precond` or `decompose` (will fail at runtime).\n- Planning every tick with no caching.\n- Effects missing for prerequisites (planner cannot reason about state changes).","ref":"best_practices.html#common-failure-modes"},{"type":"extras","title":"Anti-Patterns Guide - Best Practices","doc":"See `guides/anti_patterns.md` for real examples and fixes.","ref":"best_practices.html#anti-patterns-guide"},{"type":"extras","title":"Anti-Patterns","doc":"# Anti-Patterns\n\nThis guide shows the most common ways HTN systems fail in practice, with fixes.","ref":"anti_patterns.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"1) Planning Every Tick With No Caching - Anti-Patterns","doc":"Bad:\n\n```elixir\n# Replans every tick regardless of change\n{:ok, plan} = Operator.HTN.Planner.run(:patrol, facts, traits)\n```\n\nBetter:\n\n```elixir\nif Operator.HTN.Planner.needs_replan?(plan, facts) do\n  {:ok, plan} = Operator.HTN.Planner.run(:patrol, facts, traits)\nend\n```","ref":"anti_patterns.html#1-planning-every-tick-with-no-caching"},{"type":"extras","title":"2) Facts As A Dumping Ground - Anti-Patterns","doc":"Bad:\n\n```elixir\nfacts = Operator.HTN.Facts.from_perception(%{\n  world: %{raw_game_state: huge_struct}\n})\n```\n\nBetter:\n\n```elixir\nfacts = Operator.HTN.Facts.from_perception(%{\n  world: %{threat_level: :high, target_visible: true}\n})\n```","ref":"anti_patterns.html#2-facts-as-a-dumping-ground"},{"type":"extras","title":"2a) No Facts Validation - Anti-Patterns","doc":"Bad:\n\n```elixir\nmetadata priority: 5\n```\n\nBetter:\n\n```elixir\nmetadata priority: 5, requires_facts: [{:self, :energy}, {:world, :threat_level}]\n```","ref":"anti_patterns.html#2a-no-facts-validation"},{"type":"extras","title":"3) Preconditions With Side Effects - Anti-Patterns","doc":"Bad:\n\n```elixir\nprecond fn facts ->\n  MyApp.SideEffectingCache.refresh()\n  Operator.HTN.Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :ready})\nend\n```\n\nBetter:\n\n```elixir\nprecond fn facts ->\n  Operator.HTN.Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :ready})\nend\n```","ref":"anti_patterns.html#3-preconditions-with-side-effects"},{"type":"extras","title":"4) Missing Effects For Multi-Step Plans - Anti-Patterns","doc":"Bad:\n\n```elixir\nprimitive :unlock do\n  run fn actor, _facts -> {:ok, actor} end\nend\n\nprimitive :open_door do\n  precond fn facts -> Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:world, :door_unlocked}, false) end\n  run fn actor, _facts -> {:ok, actor} end\nend\n```\n\nBetter:\n\n```elixir\nprimitive :unlock do\n  effects [Operator.HTN.Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:world, :door_unlocked}, true)]\n  run fn actor, _facts -> {:ok, actor} end\nend\n```","ref":"anti_patterns.html#4-missing-effects-for-multi-step-plans"},{"type":"extras","title":"5) Aliases Inside precond and decompose - Anti-Patterns","doc":"Bad:\n\n```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Facts\n\nprecond fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :ready}) end\n```\n\nBetter:\n\n```elixir\nprecond fn facts -> Operator.HTN.Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :ready}) end\n```","ref":"anti_patterns.html#5-aliases-inside-precond-and-decompose"},{"type":"extras","title":"6) Deep, Monolithic Goals - Anti-Patterns","doc":"Bad:\n\n```elixir\ngoal :do_everything do\n  # 20 tasks, 5 branches, 3 levels deep\nend\n```\n\nBetter:\n\n```elixir\ngoal :patrol do\n  # Small, clear, testable\nend\n```","ref":"anti_patterns.html#6-deep-monolithic-goals"},{"type":"extras","title":"7) Hidden Randomness In Primitives - Anti-Patterns","doc":"Bad:\n\n```elixir\nprimitive :shoot do\n  run fn actor, _facts ->\n    if :rand.uniform() < 0.1, do: {:error, :jammed}, else: {:ok, actor}\n  end\nend\n```\n\nBetter:\n\n```elixir\n# Roll randomness outside, pass into facts or actor\nprimitive :shoot do\n  run fn actor, _facts ->\n    if actor.weapon_jammed, do: {:error, :jammed}, else: {:ok, actor}\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"anti_patterns.html#7-hidden-randomness-in-primitives"},{"type":"extras","title":"Debugging","doc":"# Debugging\n\nThis guide focuses on getting signal when your plans fail or behave oddly.","ref":"debugging.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Enable Trace Output - Debugging","doc":"Tracing shows the planner's choices and is the fastest way to understand why\na goal was or was not selected.\n\n```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Trace\nalias Operator.HTN.Trace.ConsoleHandler\n\nTrace.set_handler(ConsoleHandler)\n{:ok, plan} = Operator.HTN.Planner.run(:patrol, facts, traits)\nTrace.reset()\n```","ref":"debugging.html#enable-trace-output"},{"type":"extras","title":"Read The Plan - Debugging","doc":"A plan is just data. Print it and inspect it.\n\n```elixir\nIO.inspect(plan.goal)\nIO.inspect(plan.tasks)\nIO.inspect(plan.validity)\n```","ref":"debugging.html#read-the-plan"},{"type":"extras","title":"Explain Goal Selection - Debugging","doc":"Use `GoalSelector.explain/3` to see why a goal was selected.\n\n```elixir\nresult = Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.explain(facts, traits)\nIO.inspect(result.selected)\nIO.inspect(result.eligible)\nIO.inspect(result.ineligible)\nIO.inspect(result.ineligible |> Enum.map(& &1.missing_facts))\n```","ref":"debugging.html#explain-goal-selection"},{"type":"extras","title":"Explain Plan Generation - Debugging","doc":"Use `Planner.explain/3` for a structured payload of the plan and checks.\n\n```elixir\nresult = Operator.HTN.Planner.explain(:patrol, facts, traits)\nIO.inspect(result.result)\nIO.inspect(result.reason)\nIO.inspect(result.plan)\nIO.inspect(result.missing_facts)\n```","ref":"debugging.html#explain-plan-generation"},{"type":"extras","title":"Check Preconditions Manually - Debugging","doc":"If a goal does not appear, the precondition is likely failing.\n\n```elixir\ngoal = Operator.HTN.Registry.get_goal(:patrol)\nOperator.HTN.Precondition.all_satisfied?(goal.precond, facts, traits)\n```","ref":"debugging.html#check-preconditions-manually"},{"type":"extras","title":"Validate Registry State - Debugging","doc":"The Registry must know about your behavior module.\n\n```elixir\nOperator.HTN.Registry.list_goal_names()\nOperator.HTN.Registry.list_task_names()\n```","ref":"debugging.html#validate-registry-state"},{"type":"extras","title":"Use Planner.needs_replan?/2 - Debugging","doc":"If an agent keeps repeating bad plans, check when you should replan.\n\n```elixir\nif Operator.HTN.Planner.needs_replan?(plan, facts) do\n  {:ok, new_plan} = Operator.HTN.Planner.run(plan.goal, facts, traits)\n  new_plan\nelse\n  plan\nend\n```","ref":"debugging.html#use-planner-needs_replan-2"},{"type":"extras","title":"Debug One Step At A Time - Debugging","doc":"`Executor.step/3` returns a full tuple with remaining plan state.\n\n```elixir\ncase Operator.HTN.Executor.step(plan, actor, facts) do\n  {:ok, :continue, actor, facts, remaining} -> remaining\n  {:ok, :completed, actor, facts, _plan} -> :done\n  {:error, reason, actor, facts, _plan} -> {:failed, reason}\nend\n```","ref":"debugging.html#debug-one-step-at-a-time"},{"type":"extras","title":"Custom Trace Handlers - Debugging","doc":"You can implement a structured logger to send traces to your telemetry stack.\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyGame.HTNLogger do\n  require Logger\n\n  def on_goal_start(goal, _facts, _opts), do: Logger.debug(\"[HTN] start #{goal}\")\n  def on_goal_end(goal, result, _opts), do: Logger.debug(\"[HTN] end #{goal}: #{result}\")\n  def on_task_expand(task, args, _facts, _opts), do: Logger.debug(\"[HTN] task #{task} #{inspect(args)}\")\nend\n\nOperator.HTN.Trace.set_handler(MyGame.HTNLogger)\n```","ref":"debugging.html#custom-trace-handlers"},{"type":"extras","title":"Checklist - Debugging","doc":"- Registry has the expected modules.\n- Facts contain the keys your preconditions read.\n- Preconditions return the values you expect.\n- Trace output shows the exact failure point.","ref":"debugging.html#checklist"},{"type":"extras","title":"HTN DSL Reference","doc":"# HTN DSL Reference\n\nThis is a full reference to the HTN DSL macros.\n\n## `use Operator.HTN.DSL`\n\nThe entry point for HTN definitions.\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyGame.Behavior do\n  use Operator.HTN.DSL\nend\n```\n\nUse `auto_register: false` if you want manual control of Registry registration.\n\n```elixir\nuse Operator.HTN.DSL, auto_register: false\n```\n\n## `goal`\n\nGoals are top-level objectives. They decompose into tasks.\n\n```elixir\ngoal :patrol do\n  precond fn facts ->\n    Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:self, :energy}, 0) > 10\n  end\n\n  decompose do\n    task :move_to, :waypoint_1\n    task :look_around\n  end\n\n  metadata priority: 3, domain: :routine\nend\n```\n\n## `task`\n\nTasks are abstract steps that can decompose into other tasks or primitives.\n\n```elixir\ntask :travel_to, destination do\n  precond fn facts ->\n    Operator.HTN.Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :can_move})\n  end\n\n  decompose fn facts ->\n    has_vehicle = Operator.HTN.Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :vehicle})\n    if has_vehicle, do: [{:drive_to, [destination]}], else: [{:walk_to, [destination]}]\n  end\n\n  cost 2.0\n  metadata kind: :movement\nend\n```\n\n## `primitive`\n\nPrimitives are executable actions. They must define `run`.\n\n```elixir\nprimitive :move_to, destination do\n  run fn actor, _facts ->\n    {:ok, %{actor | position: destination}}\n  end\n\n  effects [\n    Operator.HTN.Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:self, :position}, destination)\n  ]\n\n  metadata kind: :movement\nend\n```\n\n## `axiom`\n\nAxioms are reusable precondition helpers.\n\n```elixir\naxiom :enemy_in_range do\n  fn facts, args ->\n    max_range = Keyword.get(args, :range, 10)\n    dist = Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:world, :enemy_distance}, 999)\n    dist <= max_range\n  end\nend\n```\n\nUse them in preconditions.\n\n```elixir\ngoal :ranged_attack do\n  precond {:axiom, :enemy_in_range, range: 20}\n  decompose do\n    task :aim\n    task :fire\n  end\nend\n```\n\n## `precond`\n\nPreconditions control eligibility. You can use anonymous functions or logical\noperators. Preconditions are stored as a list of conditions and evaluated at\nruntime via `Operator.HTN.Precondition`.\n\n```elixir\nprecond fn facts ->\n  Operator.HTN.Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :weapon})\nend\n```\n\nLogical operators:\n\n```elixir\n{:all, [fn1, fn2]}\n{:any, [fn1, fn2]}\n{:not, fn1}\n{:none, [fn1, fn2]}\n{:first, [fn1, fn2]}\n{:axiom, :enemy_in_range, range: 10}\n\nTo evaluate goal preconditions manually:\n\n```elixir\ngoal = Operator.HTN.Registry.get_goal(:patrol)\nOperator.HTN.Precondition.all_satisfied?(goal.precond, facts, traits)\n```\n```\n\n## `decompose`\n\nDecomposition can be a static block or a function.\n\n```elixir\ndecompose do\n  task :move_to, :door\n  task :open_door\nend\n```\n\n```elixir\ndecompose fn facts ->\n  if Operator.HTN.Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :has_key}) do\n    [{:unlock, []}, {:enter, []}]\n  else\n    [{:find_key, []}]\n  end\nend\n```\n\n## `cost`\n\nCosts influence plan selection when multiple options are valid.\n\n```elixir\ncost 1.0\n```\n\n```elixir\ncost fn facts ->\n  danger = Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:world, :danger}, 1.0)\n  5.0 * danger\nend\n```\n\n## `effects`\n\nEffects describe how world state changes.\n\n```elixir\neffects [\n  Operator.HTN.Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:world, :door_unlocked}, true)\n]\n```\n\nEffect types:\n\n- `:plan_only`\n- `:plan_and_execute`\n- `:permanent`\n\n## `metadata`\n\nAttach arbitrary metadata for goal selection and analytics.\n\n```elixir\nmetadata priority: 5, domain: :combat, required_traits: [:aggressive]\n```\n\nYou can also declare required fact keys for validation and diagnostics:\n\n```elixir\nmetadata requires_facts: [{:self, :energy}, {:world, :threat_level}]\n```","ref":"dsl_reference.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"DSL Gotchas - HTN DSL Reference","doc":"- `precond` and `decompose` run at runtime, not compile time.\n- Use fully qualified module names in those functions.\n- Keep side effects out of preconditions.","ref":"dsl_reference.html#dsl-gotchas"},{"type":"extras","title":"Director","doc":"# Director\n\nThe Director is a global pacing system. It decides when world events should\nhappen based on evolving state. It is not tied to a single NPC.","ref":"director.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Core Idea - Director","doc":"- HTN handles per-agent intent.\n- The Director handles global narrative pressure.","ref":"director.html#core-idea"},{"type":"extras","title":"Minimal Storyteller - Director","doc":"```elixir\ndefmodule MyGame.SimpleStoryteller do\n  @behaviour Operator.Storyteller\n\n  @impl true\n  def init(_opts), do: %{last_event_tick: 0}\n\n  @impl true\n  def pick_event(tick, world_state, state) do\n    tension = Map.get(world_state, :tension, 0.0)\n\n    if tension > 0.7 do\n      event = %{type: :ambush, severity: round(tension * 5)}\n      {event, %{state | last_event_tick: tick}}\n    else\n      {nil, state}\n    end\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"director.html#minimal-storyteller"},{"type":"extras","title":"Start The Director - Director","doc":"```elixir\n{:ok, _pid} = Operator.Director.start_link(\n  storyteller: MyGame.SimpleStoryteller,\n  on_event: &MyGame.EventHandler.process/1\n)\n```","ref":"director.html#start-the-director"},{"type":"extras","title":"Drive It Every Tick - Director","doc":"```elixir\nOperator.Director.tick(%{tick: current_tick, tension: world_tension})\n```\n\nUse `tick_sync/1` if you want the event returned immediately.\n\n```elixir\nevent = Operator.Director.tick_sync(%{tick: current_tick, tension: world_tension})\n```","ref":"director.html#drive-it-every-tick"},{"type":"extras","title":"Integrate With HTN - Director","doc":"Treat Director events as facts in your agents.\n\n```elixir\nfacts = Operator.HTN.Facts.from_perception(%{\n  self: %{energy: 40},\n  world: %{director_event: event}\n})\n```","ref":"director.html#integrate-with-htn"},{"type":"extras","title":"Testing Storytellers - Director","doc":"```elixir\nstate = MyGame.SimpleStoryteller.init([])\n{event, _state} = MyGame.SimpleStoryteller.pick_event(10, %{tension: 0.8}, state)\nassert event.type == :ambush\n```","ref":"director.html#testing-storytellers"},{"type":"extras","title":"Checklist - Director","doc":"- Storyteller is pure and deterministic.\n- Events are small maps with a clear `:type`.\n- Director ticks are called exactly once per frame or simulation step.","ref":"director.html#checklist"},{"type":"extras","title":"Getting Started","doc":"# Getting Started\n\nThis guide walks you through building your first HTN (Hierarchical Task Network)\nplanning system with Operator. By the end, you'll have an NPC that can plan and\nexecute behaviors based on world state.","ref":"getting_started.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"What You'll Build - Getting Started","doc":"You will build a single NPC behavior module, generate a plan, and execute it\nstep-by-step. The focus is clarity, not scale.","ref":"getting_started.html#what-you-ll-build"},{"type":"extras","title":"Prerequisites - Getting Started","doc":"- Elixir 1.15 or later.\n- A Mix project where you can add a dependency.\n- A willingness to keep facts deterministic.","ref":"getting_started.html#prerequisites"},{"type":"extras","title":"Installation - Getting Started","doc":"Add Operator to your `mix.exs` dependencies:\n\n```elixir\ndef deps do\n  [\n    {:operator, \"~> 0.1.0\"}\n  ]\nend\n```\n\nThen fetch dependencies:\n\n```bash\nmix deps.get\n```","ref":"getting_started.html#installation"},{"type":"extras","title":"A Minimal Mental Model - Getting Started","doc":"HTN is a hierarchy:\n\n- Goals define intent.\n- Tasks define how to achieve goals.\n- Primitives define real actions.\n\nFacts are the world snapshot. Plans are sequences of primitives.","ref":"getting_started.html#a-minimal-mental-model"},{"type":"extras","title":"Core Concepts - Getting Started","doc":"Before writing code, understand the HTN hierarchy:\n\n```\nGoals (high-level objectives)\n  └── Tasks (abstract steps)\n       └── Primitives (executable actions)\n```\n\n- **Goals** - What the agent wants to achieve (\"patrol area\", \"attack enemy\")\n- **Tasks** - How to achieve it, decomposed into subtasks\n- **Primitives** - Actual actions your game executes (\"move\", \"fire\", \"wait\")","ref":"getting_started.html#core-concepts"},{"type":"extras","title":"Your First Behavior Module - Getting Started","doc":"Create a behavior module that defines what your NPC can do:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyGame.GuardBehavior do\n  use Operator.HTN.DSL\n\n  # A goal that decomposes into tasks\n  goal :patrol do\n    precond fn facts ->\n      Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:self, :energy}, 0) > 20\n    end\n\n    decompose do\n      task :move_to, :waypoint_1\n      task :look_around\n      task :move_to, :waypoint_2\n      task :look_around\n    end\n\n    metadata priority: 3, domain: :routine\n  end\n\n  # Primitives are the leaf actions\n  primitive :move_to, destination do\n    run fn actor, _facts ->\n      # Your game's movement logic here\n      IO.puts(\"#{actor.name} moving to #{destination}\")\n      {:ok, actor}\n    end\n  end\n\n  primitive :look_around do\n    run fn actor, _facts ->\n      IO.puts(\"#{actor.name} scanning area...\")\n      {:ok, actor}\n    end\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"getting_started.html#your-first-behavior-module"},{"type":"extras","title":"Why Full Module Names Matter - Getting Started","doc":"Functions inside `precond` and `decompose` run at runtime in a different scope.\nPreconditions are stored as a list of conditions and evaluated through\n`Operator.HTN.Precondition`.\nThat means module aliases do not work. Always use fully qualified names inside\nthose functions.","ref":"getting_started.html#why-full-module-names-matter"},{"type":"extras","title":"Understanding Facts - Getting Started","doc":"Facts represent the agent's knowledge about the world:\n\n```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Facts\n\n# Create facts from perception data\nfacts = Facts.from_perception(%{\n  self: %{\n    health: 100,\n    energy: 80,\n    position: {10, 20}\n  },\n  world: %{\n    threat_level: :low,\n    time_of_day: :day\n  },\n  social: %{\n    faction: :guards\n  }\n})\n\n# Query facts in preconditions\nFacts.has?(facts, {:self, :health})      # => true\nFacts.get(facts, {:self, :health})       # => 100\nFacts.get(facts, {:self, :ammo}, 0)      # => 0 (default)\n```","ref":"getting_started.html#understanding-facts"},{"type":"extras","title":"Keep Facts Small - Getting Started","doc":"Facts are meant to be lightweight snapshots. If you have very large data, keep a\ncompact summary in facts and leave the heavy data elsewhere.","ref":"getting_started.html#keep-facts-small"},{"type":"extras","title":"Generating Plans - Getting Started","doc":"Use the Planner to create a plan for a goal:\n\n```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Planner\n\n# Build facts from your game state\nfacts = Facts.from_perception(%{\n  self: %{energy: 80}\n})\n\n# Traits influence goal selection and costs\ntraits = %{archetype: :guard}\n\n# Generate a plan\ncase Planner.run(:patrol, facts, traits) do\n  {:ok, plan} ->\n    IO.inspect(plan.tasks)\n    # => [{:move_to, [:waypoint_1]}, {:look_around, []}, ...]\n\n  {:error, :preconditions_not_met} ->\n    IO.puts(\"Guard doesn't have enough energy to patrol\")\n\n  {:error, :goal_not_found} ->\n    IO.puts(\"Unknown goal\")\nend\n```","ref":"getting_started.html#generating-plans"},{"type":"extras","title":"Handling Errors Cleanly - Getting Started","doc":"Always handle the planner's error tuples. They are your signal that either the\ngoal does not exist or the world state does not qualify.","ref":"getting_started.html#handling-errors-cleanly"},{"type":"extras","title":"Executing Plans - Getting Started","doc":"Execute plans step-by-step or all at once:\n\n```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Executor\n\nactor = %{name: \"Guard #1\", id: 1}\n\n# Execute one step at a time (good for game loops)\ncase Executor.step(plan, actor, facts) do\n  {:ok, :continue, updated_actor, updated_facts, remaining_plan} ->\n    # Store remaining_plan for next tick\n    {:continue, updated_actor, remaining_plan}\n\n  {:ok, :completed, final_actor, final_facts, _plan} ->\n    # Plan finished!\n    {:done, final_actor}\n\n  {:error, reason, actor, facts, plan} ->\n    # Task failed, might need to replan\n    {:failed, reason}\nend\n\n# Or execute entire plan at once\n{:ok, final_actor, final_facts} = Executor.run_plan(plan, actor, facts)\n```","ref":"getting_started.html#executing-plans"},{"type":"extras","title":"Loop Helper (Optional) - Getting Started","doc":"For quick integration, the `Loop` helper handles plan creation and one-step execution:\n\n```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Loop\n\nresult = Loop.tick(actor.plan, actor, facts, traits, goal: :patrol)\n```","ref":"getting_started.html#loop-helper-optional"},{"type":"extras","title":"Plan Lifecycles - Getting Started","doc":"- `:active` means it can run.\n- `:invalid` means the world changed.\n- `:completed` means it finished.","ref":"getting_started.html#plan-lifecycles"},{"type":"extras","title":"Game Loop Integration - Getting Started","doc":"Here's a typical integration pattern:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyGame.AISystem do\n  alias Operator.HTN.{Executor, Facts, GoalSelector, Planner}\n\n  def tick(entity, world_state) do\n    facts = build_facts(entity, world_state)\n    traits = entity.genome\n\n    case entity.current_plan do\n      nil ->\n        # No plan - pick a goal and plan\n        case GoalSelector.pick_goal(facts, traits) do\n          {:ok, goal} ->\n            case Planner.run(goal, facts, traits) do\n              {:ok, plan} -> %{entity | current_plan: plan}\n              {:error, _} -> entity\n            end\n          :none ->\n            entity  # No valid goals\n        end\n\n      plan ->\n        # Have a plan - execute next step\n        case Executor.step(plan, entity, facts) do\n          {:ok, :completed, updated, _facts, _plan} ->\n            %{updated | current_plan: nil}\n\n          {:ok, :continue, updated, _facts, remaining} ->\n            %{updated | current_plan: remaining}\n\n          {:error, _reason, entity, _facts, _plan} ->\n            # Invalidate plan, will replan next tick\n            %{entity | current_plan: nil}\n        end\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp build_facts(entity, world_state) do\n    Facts.from_perception(%{\n      self: %{\n        health: entity.health,\n        energy: entity.energy,\n        position: entity.position\n      },\n      world: Map.take(world_state, [:threat_level, :time_of_day])\n    })\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"getting_started.html#game-loop-integration"},{"type":"extras","title":"Replanning Strategy - Getting Started","doc":"If your world changes often, do not discard plans too aggressively. Use\n`Planner.needs_replan?/2` to decide when to regenerate.","ref":"getting_started.html#replanning-strategy"},{"type":"extras","title":"Adding Preconditions - Getting Started","doc":"Preconditions control when goals and tasks are available:\n\n```elixir\ngoal :attack do\n  # Simple precondition\n  precond fn facts ->\n    Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :weapon}) and\n    Facts.get(facts, {:self, :ammo}, 0) > 0\n  end\n\n  decompose do\n    task :aim_at_target\n    task :fire_weapon\n  end\nend\n```\n\nUse logical operators for complex conditions:\n\n```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Precondition\n\n# OR: has weapon OR near weapon pickup\n{:any, [\n  fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :weapon}) end,\n  fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:world, :weapon_nearby}) end\n]}\n\n# Negation\n{:not, fn facts -> Facts.get(facts, {:self, :stunned}, false) end}\n```","ref":"getting_started.html#adding-preconditions"},{"type":"extras","title":"Using Effects - Getting Started","doc":"Effects update world state during planning:\n\n```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Effect\n\nprimitive :unlock_door do\n  effects [\n    Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:world, :door_locked}, false)\n  ]\n\n  run fn actor, _facts ->\n    {:ok, actor}\n  end\nend\n```\n\nEffect types:\n- `:plan_only` - Only applied during planning (hypothetical)\n- `:plan_and_execute` - Applied during planning AND execution\n- `:permanent` - Applied at execution, persists beyond plan","ref":"getting_started.html#using-effects"},{"type":"extras","title":"Next Steps - Getting Started","doc":"- Read the [How-To Guides](howto.html) for specific recipes\n- Check the [Cheatsheet](cheatsheet.html) for quick reference\n- Explore the [API Reference](api-reference.html) for details\n- See the `examples/` directory for complete implementations\n- Read `guides/testing.md` for Registry-safe testing\n- Read `guides/debugging.md` for tracing and diagnostics","ref":"getting_started.html#next-steps"},{"type":"extras","title":"How-To Guides","doc":"# How-To Guides\n\nPractical recipes for common HTN planning scenarios.","ref":"howto.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Define Dynamic Decomposition - How-To Guides","doc":"When task subtasks depend on world state:\n\n```elixir\ntask :travel_to, destination do\n  decompose fn facts ->\n    current = Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:self, :position})\n    has_vehicle = Operator.HTN.Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :vehicle})\n\n    if has_vehicle do\n      [{:enter_vehicle, []}, {:drive_to, [destination]}, {:exit_vehicle, []}]\n    else\n      [{:walk_to, [destination]}]\n    end\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"howto.html#define-dynamic-decomposition"},{"type":"extras","title":"Create Branching Behaviors - How-To Guides","doc":"Use preconditions to select between approaches. Preconditions are stored as a\nlist of conditions and evaluated via `Operator.HTN.Precondition`.\n\n```elixir\ngoal :engage_enemy do\n  precond fn facts ->\n    Operator.HTN.Facts.has?(facts, {:world, :enemy_visible})\n  end\n\n  decompose fn facts ->\n    distance = Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:world, :enemy_distance}, 100)\n    has_ammo = Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:self, :ammo}, 0) > 0\n\n    cond do\n      distance < 5 ->\n        [{:melee_attack, []}]\n      has_ammo ->\n        [{:aim, []}, {:fire, []}]\n      true ->\n        [{:retreat, []}, {:find_ammo, []}]\n    end\n  end\n\n  metadata priority: 8, domain: :combat\nend\n```","ref":"howto.html#create-branching-behaviors"},{"type":"extras","title":"Implement Cost-Based Planning - How-To Guides","doc":"Make certain behaviors more or less \"expensive\":\n\n```elixir\n# Static cost\nprimitive :sprint do\n  cost 3.0  # Higher cost = less preferred\n\n  run fn actor, _facts ->\n    {:ok, %{actor | stamina: actor.stamina - 20}}\n  end\nend\n\n# Dynamic cost based on world state\ntask :attack do\n  cost fn facts ->\n    threat = Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:world, :threat_level}, 1.0)\n    5.0 * threat  # More expensive when dangerous\n  end\nend\n\n# Trait-influenced cost\ntask :negotiate do\n  cost fn _facts, traits ->\n    charisma = Map.get(traits, :charisma, 1.0)\n    10.0 / charisma  # Cheaper for charismatic agents\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"howto.html#implement-cost-based-planning"},{"type":"extras","title":"Add Trait-Based Goal Selection - How-To Guides","doc":"Use traits to influence which goals are selected:\n\n```elixir\n# In your behavior module\ngoal :aggressive_attack do\n  metadata priority: 5, required_traits: [:aggressive]\n  # ...\nend\n\ngoal :cautious_approach do\n  metadata priority: 5, required_traits: [:cautious]\n  # ...\nend\n\n# When selecting goals\nfacts = build_facts(entity)\ntraits = %{traits: [:aggressive, :brave]}\n\n{:ok, goal} = Operator.HTN.GoalSelector.pick_goal(facts, traits)\n# Will prefer goals matching the entity's traits\n```","ref":"howto.html#add-trait-based-goal-selection"},{"type":"extras","title":"Force Goal Ordering - How-To Guides","doc":"Sometimes you want deterministic ordering instead of scoring.\n\n```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.GoalSelector\n\n{:ok, goal} = GoalSelector.pick_goal(facts, traits,\n  goal_order: [:emergency_flee, :heal, :attack, :idle]\n)\n```","ref":"howto.html#force-goal-ordering"},{"type":"extras","title":"Add Plan Metadata For Diagnostics - How-To Guides","doc":"Metadata is useful for debugging and analytics.\n\n```elixir\nplan = Operator.HTN.Plan.add_metadata(plan, :source, \\\"goal_selector\\\")\nplan = Operator.HTN.Plan.add_metadata(plan, :tick, current_tick)\n```","ref":"howto.html#add-plan-metadata-for-diagnostics"},{"type":"extras","title":"Set Up Test Isolation - How-To Guides","doc":"HTN Registry uses global state. Isolate tests properly:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyBehaviorTest do\n  use ExUnit.Case, async: false  # Important!\n\n  alias Operator.HTN.TestHelpers\n\n  # Option 1: Reset registry in setup\n  setup do\n    TestHelpers.reset_registry()\n    :ok\n  end\n\n  # Option 2: Use isolated registry for specific tests\n  test \"my behavior works\" do\n    TestHelpers.with_registry([MyBehavior], fn ->\n      # Only MyBehavior is registered here\n      assert :my_goal in Operator.HTN.Registry.list_goal_names()\n    end)\n  end\n\n  # Option 3: Setup with specific modules\n  setup do\n    TestHelpers.setup_htn([MyBehavior, AnotherBehavior])\n    :ok\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"howto.html#set-up-test-isolation"},{"type":"extras","title":"Build Facts In One Place - How-To Guides","doc":"Keep your facts builder deterministic and side-effect free.\n\n```elixir\ndef build_facts(entity, world_state) do\n  Operator.HTN.Facts.from_perception(%{\n    self: %{energy: entity.energy, position: entity.position},\n    world: %{time: world_state.time, threat: world_state.threat}\n  })\nend\n```","ref":"howto.html#build-facts-in-one-place"},{"type":"extras","title":"Debug Plan Generation - How-To Guides","doc":"Use tracing to see what the planner is doing:\n\n```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Trace\nalias Operator.HTN.Trace.ConsoleHandler\n\n# Enable console tracing\nTrace.set_handler(ConsoleHandler)\n\n# Now plan - you'll see output like:\n# [HTN] ▶ GOAL patrol\n# [HTN]   ✓ Precondition passed (goal: patrol)\n# [HTN]   → TASK move_to [:waypoint_1]\n# [HTN]   ◀ GOAL patrol SUCCESS\n\n{:ok, plan} = Planner.run(:patrol, facts, traits)\n\n# Disable when done\nTrace.reset()\n```\n\nCreate a custom handler for structured logging:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyGame.HTNLogger do\n  require Logger\n\n  def on_goal_start(goal, _facts, _opts) do\n    Logger.debug(\"[HTN] Starting goal: #{goal}\")\n  end\n\n  def on_goal_end(goal, result, _opts) do\n    Logger.debug(\"[HTN] Goal #{goal} finished: #{result}\")\n  end\n\n  def on_task_expand(task, args, _facts, _opts) do\n    Logger.debug(\"[HTN] Expanding: #{task} #{inspect(args)}\")\n  end\n\n  # Implement other callbacks as needed...\nend\n\nTrace.set_handler(MyGame.HTNLogger)\n```","ref":"howto.html#debug-plan-generation"},{"type":"extras","title":"Implement Plan Persistence - How-To Guides","doc":"Store plans across game saves:\n\n```elixir\n# Default storage uses ETS (in-memory)\nalias Operator.HTN.Storage\n\n# Store a plan\nStorage.persist_plan(entity_id, plan)\n\n# Retrieve later\nplan = Storage.fetch_plan(entity_id)\n\n# Clear when entity dies/despawns\nStorage.clear_plan(entity_id)\n```\n\nFor disk persistence, implement the Storage behaviour:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyGame.PersistentStorage do\n  @behaviour Operator.Storage\n\n  @impl true\n  def persist_plan(entity_id, plan) do\n    # Save to database/file\n    MyGame.Repo.insert_or_update(%PlanRecord{\n      entity_id: entity_id,\n      plan_data: :erlang.term_to_binary(plan)\n    })\n    :ok\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def fetch_plan(entity_id) do\n    case MyGame.Repo.get(PlanRecord, entity_id) do\n      nil -> nil\n      record -> :erlang.binary_to_term(record.plan_data)\n    end\n  end\n\n  # Implement clear_plan/1 and list_plans/0...\nend\n\n# Configure in config.exs\nconfig :operator, storage_module: MyGame.PersistentStorage\n```","ref":"howto.html#implement-plan-persistence"},{"type":"extras","title":"Integrate the Director for Events - How-To Guides","doc":"Use the Director to generate narrative events:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyGame.TensionStoryteller do\n  @behaviour Operator.Storyteller\n\n  @impl true\n  def init(_opts), do: %{last_event_tick: 0}\n\n  @impl true\n  def pick_event(tick, world_state, state) do\n    tension = Map.get(world_state, :tension, 0.0)\n    cooldown = tick - state.last_event_tick\n\n    if tension > 0.7 and cooldown > 100 do\n      event = %{\n        type: :ambush,\n        severity: round(tension * 5),\n        location: pick_ambush_location(world_state)\n      }\n      {event, %{state | last_event_tick: tick}}\n    else\n      {nil, state}\n    end\n  end\n\n  defp pick_ambush_location(world_state) do\n    # Your location selection logic\n    :random_location\n  end\nend\n\n# Start the Director\n{:ok, _pid} = Operator.Director.start_link(\n  storyteller: MyGame.TensionStoryteller,\n  on_event: &MyGame.EventHandler.process/1\n)\n\n# In your game loop\ndef tick(world_state) do\n  Operator.Director.tick(world_state)\n  # ...\nend\n```","ref":"howto.html#integrate-the-director-for-events"},{"type":"extras","title":"Create Reusable Axioms - How-To Guides","doc":"Define query patterns once, use in many preconditions:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyGame.CommonAxioms do\n  use Operator.HTN.DSL\n\n  axiom :enemy_in_range do\n    fn facts, args ->\n      max_range = Keyword.get(args, :range, 10)\n      enemy_dist = Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:world, :enemy_distance}, 999)\n      enemy_dist <= max_range\n    end\n  end\n\n  axiom :has_resource do\n    fn facts, args ->\n      resource = Keyword.get(args, :resource)\n      min_amount = Keyword.get(args, :min, 1)\n      amount = Operator.HTN.Facts.get(facts, {:self, resource}, 0)\n      amount >= min_amount\n    end\n  end\nend\n\n# Use in preconditions\ngoal :ranged_attack do\n  precond {:axiom, :enemy_in_range, range: 20}\n  precond {:axiom, :has_resource, resource: :ammo, min: 1}\n  # ...\nend\n```","ref":"howto.html#create-reusable-axioms"},{"type":"extras","title":"Handle Plan Invalidation - How-To Guides","doc":"Detect when plans become invalid and replan:\n\n```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Planner\n\ndef tick(entity, world_state) do\n  facts = build_facts(entity, world_state)\n\n  case entity.current_plan do\n    nil ->\n      create_new_plan(entity, facts)\n\n    plan ->\n      # Check if world changed significantly\n      if Planner.needs_replan?(plan, facts) do\n        # Plan is stale, create new one\n        create_new_plan(entity, facts)\n      else\n        execute_plan(entity, plan, facts)\n      end\n  end\nend\n\ndefp create_new_plan(entity, facts) do\n  case Planner.run(:default_goal, facts, entity.traits) do\n    {:ok, plan} -> %{entity | current_plan: plan}\n    {:error, _} -> entity\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"howto.html#handle-plan-invalidation"},{"type":"extras","title":"Use The Loop Helper - How-To Guides","doc":"For game loops, the `Loop` helper reduces boilerplate:\n\n```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Loop\n\nresult = Loop.tick(entity.plan, entity, facts, entity.traits, goal: :patrol)\n\ncase result.status do\n  :idle -> %{entity | plan: nil}\n  :continue -> %{entity | plan: result.plan, current: result.actor}\n  :completed -> %{entity | plan: nil, current: result.actor}\n  :failed -> %{entity | plan: nil}\nend\n```","ref":"howto.html#use-the-loop-helper"},{"type":"extras","title":"Add Telemetry for Monitoring - How-To Guides","doc":"Track HTN performance in production:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyGame.HTNTelemetry do\n  @behaviour Operator.Telemetry\n\n  @impl true\n  def emit_goal_selected(goal, measurements, metadata) do\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:my_game, :htn, :goal_selected],\n      measurements,\n      Map.put(metadata, :goal, goal)\n    )\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def emit_htn_plan_generated(goal, task_count, duration_ms) do\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:my_game, :htn, :plan_generated],\n      %{task_count: task_count, duration_ms: duration_ms},\n      %{goal: goal}\n    )\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def emit_director_event(event_type, tick) do\n    :telemetry.execute(\n      [:my_game, :director, :event],\n      %{count: 1},\n      %{type: event_type, tick: tick}\n    )\n  end\nend\n\n# Configure\nconfig :operator, telemetry_module: MyGame.HTNTelemetry\n\n# Attach handlers in application start\n:telemetry.attach_many(\"htn-metrics\", [\n  [:my_game, :htn, :goal_selected],\n  [:my_game, :htn, :plan_generated]\n], &MyGame.MetricsHandler.handle/4, nil)\n```","ref":"howto.html#add-telemetry-for-monitoring"},{"type":"extras","title":"Testing","doc":"# Testing\n\nThis guide is ruthless about keeping tests deterministic when using HTN planning.","ref":"testing.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"The Core Rule - Testing","doc":"The HTN Registry is global state. Treat it like a singleton cache that must be\nreset or isolated for every test that touches it.","ref":"testing.html#the-core-rule"},{"type":"extras","title":"Safe Defaults - Testing","doc":"Use these defaults unless you have a strong reason not to.\n\n- `async: false` for any test that touches the Registry or plans.\n- `Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.reset_registry/0` in setup.\n- `Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.register_modules/1` for the behaviors under test.\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyGame.BehaviorTest do\n  use ExUnit.Case, async: false\n\n  import Operator.HTN.TestHelpers\n  alias Operator.HTN.{Facts, Planner}\n\n  setup :reset_registry\n\n  setup do\n    register_modules([MyGame.GuardBehavior])\n    :ok\n  end\n\n  test \"patrol goal produces tasks\" do\n    facts = Facts.from_perception(%{self: %{energy: 50}})\n    {:ok, plan} = Planner.run(:patrol, facts, %{})\n    assert length(plan.tasks) > 0\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"testing.html#safe-defaults"},{"type":"extras","title":"Isolating One Test - Testing","doc":"Use `with_registry/2` to scope the Registry to only the modules you need.\n\n```elixir\ntest \"single behavior isolated\" do\n  Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.with_registry([MyGame.GuardBehavior], fn ->\n    assert :patrol in Operator.HTN.Registry.list_goal_names()\n  end)\nend\n```","ref":"testing.html#isolating-one-test"},{"type":"extras","title":"Common Test Patterns - Testing","doc":"Plan generation pattern:\n\n```elixir\nfacts = Operator.HTN.TestHelpers.test_facts(%{self: %{can_move: true}})\n{:ok, plan} = Operator.HTN.Planner.run(:patrol, facts, %{})\nOperator.HTN.TestHelpers.assert_has_task(plan, :move_to)\n```\n\nExecutor step pattern:\n\n```elixir\nactor = %{id: 1, position: :start}\n{:ok, plan} = Operator.HTN.Planner.run(:patrol, facts, %{})\n{:ok, :continue, actor, _facts, remaining} = Operator.HTN.Executor.step(plan, actor, facts)\nassert length(remaining.tasks) >= 0\n```","ref":"testing.html#common-test-patterns"},{"type":"extras","title":"Doctests - Testing","doc":"Doctests are great for verifying examples. Keep them deterministic and minimal.\n\n- Do not rely on random data in doctests.\n- Do not rely on global Registry state without explicit setup.\n- Keep outputs simple and stable.","ref":"testing.html#doctests"},{"type":"extras","title":"Checklist - Testing","doc":"- Registry is reset.\n- Behaviors are registered.\n- Facts are deterministic.\n- Tests are `async: false` when needed.\n- Trace is disabled by default.","ref":"testing.html#checklist"},{"type":"extras","title":"Operator Cheatsheet","doc":"# Operator Cheatsheet\n\nQuick reference for HTN planning with Operator.","ref":"cheatsheet.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"DSL Basics - Operator Cheatsheet","doc":"```elixir\ndefmodule MyBehavior do\n  use Operator.HTN.DSL\n\n  # Goal: high-level objective\n  goal :name do\n    precond fn facts -> ... end\n    decompose do\n      task :task_name, arg1, arg2\n    end\n    metadata key: value\n  end\n\n  # Task: abstract, decomposes further\n  task :name, arg1 do\n    precond fn facts -> ... end\n    decompose fn facts -> [{:subtask, []}] end\n    cost 2.0\n    metadata key: value\n  end\n\n  # Primitive: executable action\n  primitive :name, arg1 do\n    run fn actor, facts -> {:ok, actor} end\n    effects [Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:key}, value)]\n    metadata key: value\n  end\n\n  # Axiom: reusable query\n  axiom :name do\n    fn facts, args -> boolean end\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"cheatsheet.html#dsl-basics"},{"type":"extras","title":"Facts - Operator Cheatsheet","doc":"```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Facts\n\n# Create\nfacts = Facts.from_perception(%{\n  self: %{health: 100},\n  world: %{time: :day},\n  social: %{faction: :guards}\n})\nfacts = Facts.new()  # Empty\n\n# Query\nFacts.has?(facts, {:self, :health})       # => true\nFacts.get(facts, {:self, :health})        # => 100\nFacts.get(facts, {:self, :mana}, 0)       # => 0 (default)\n\n# Modify (returns new struct)\nfacts = Facts.put(facts, {:self, :health}, 80)\nfacts = Facts.delete(facts, {:self, :temp})\nfacts = Facts.merge(facts, %{self: %{mana: 50}})\n```","ref":"cheatsheet.html#facts"},{"type":"extras","title":"Preconditions - Operator Cheatsheet","doc":"```elixir\n# Simple function\nprecond fn facts -> Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :ready}) end\n\n# With traits (arity-2)\nprecond fn facts, traits -> :brave in traits.traits end\n\n# Logical operators\n{:all, [fn1, fn2]}           # AND (all must pass)\n{:any, [fn1, fn2]}           # OR (one must pass)\n{:not, fn}                   # Negate\n{:none, [fn1, fn2]}          # None pass\n{:first, [fn1, fn2]}         # First match (ordered OR)\n\n# Axiom reference\n{:axiom, :name}\n{:axiom, :name, arg: value}\n\n# Nested\n{:all, [fn1, {:any, [fn2, fn3]}]}\n\n# Evaluate goal preconditions\nOperator.HTN.Precondition.all_satisfied?(goal.precond, facts, traits)\n```","ref":"cheatsheet.html#preconditions"},{"type":"extras","title":"Effects - Operator Cheatsheet","doc":"```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Effect\n\n# Types\nEffect.new(:plan_only, key, value)        # Planning only\nEffect.new(:plan_and_execute, key, value) # Planning + execution\nEffect.new(:permanent, key, value)        # Execution, persists\n\n# In primitives\nprimitive :unlock do\n  effects [\n    Effect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:world, :door_locked}, false)\n  ]\nend\n\n# Special values\nEffect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:self, :ammo}, :decrement)\nEffect.new(:plan_and_execute, {:self, :ammo}, :increment)\n```","ref":"cheatsheet.html#effects"},{"type":"extras","title":"Planning - Operator Cheatsheet","doc":"```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.{Planner, GoalSelector}\n\n# Generate plan for specific goal\n{:ok, plan} = Planner.run(:goal_name, facts, traits)\n{:error, :preconditions_not_met}\n{:error, :goal_not_found}\n\n# Replan decision\nPlanner.needs_replan?(plan, facts)\n\n# Auto-select best goal\n{:ok, goal} = GoalSelector.pick_goal(facts, traits)\n:none  # No valid goals\n\n# Explain selection\nGoalSelector.explain(facts, traits)\n\n# Explain plan generation\nPlanner.explain(:goal_name, facts, traits)\n\n# Budgeted planning\nPlanner.run(:goal_name, facts, traits, budget: [max_tasks: 50, timeout_ms: 5])\n\n# Options\nGoalSelector.pick_goal(facts, traits,\n  trait_weights: %{{:aggressive, :attack} => 10},\n  goal_order: [:preferred, :fallback],\n  priority_bonus: 5\n)\n\n# Score a goal without selecting it\nGoalSelector.score_goal(:goal_name, facts, traits)\n```","ref":"cheatsheet.html#planning"},{"type":"extras","title":"Execution - Operator Cheatsheet","doc":"```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Executor\n\n# Step-by-step (for game loops)\ncase Executor.step(plan, actor, facts) do\n  {:ok, :continue, actor, facts, remaining_plan} -> ...\n  {:ok, :completed, actor, facts, plan} -> ...\n  {:error, reason, actor, facts, plan} -> ...\nend\n\n# Run entire plan\n{:ok, actor, facts} = Executor.run_plan(plan, actor, facts)\n{:error, reason, actor, facts, remaining_plan}\n\n# Options\nExecutor.run_plan(plan, actor, facts,\n  max_steps: 100,\n  on_task_complete: fn task, actor, facts -> :ok end\n)\n```\n\n# Loop Helper\n\n```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Loop\n\nresult = Loop.tick(plan, actor, facts, traits, goal: :patrol)\nresult.status  # :idle | :continue | :completed | :failed\nresult.plan    # remaining plan or nil\n```","ref":"cheatsheet.html#execution"},{"type":"extras","title":"Plans - Operator Cheatsheet","doc":"```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Plan\n\nplan.goal        # Goal name atom\nplan.tasks       # [{:task, [args]}, ...]\nplan.validity    # :active | :invalid | :completed\n\nPlan.task_count(plan)\nPlan.has_tasks?(plan)\nPlan.valid?(plan)\nPlan.next_task(plan)  # {task_tuple, remaining_plan}\nPlan.add_metadata(plan, :source, \"manual\")\nPlan.get_metadata(plan, :source)\n```","ref":"cheatsheet.html#plans"},{"type":"extras","title":"Registry - Operator Cheatsheet","doc":"```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Registry\n\nRegistry.all()                    # Full registry map\nRegistry.get_goal(:name)          # Goal definition\nRegistry.get_task(:name)          # Task struct\nRegistry.get_primitive(:name)     # Primitive struct\nRegistry.get_axiom(:name)         # Axiom struct\n\nRegistry.list_goal_names()\nRegistry.list_task_names()\nRegistry.list_primitive_names()\nRegistry.list_axiom_names()\n\nRegistry.stats()    # %{goals: n, tasks: n, ...}\nRegistry.reset()    # Clear all (for tests)\n```","ref":"cheatsheet.html#registry"},{"type":"extras","title":"Tracing - Operator Cheatsheet","doc":"```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Trace\nalias Operator.HTN.Trace.ConsoleHandler\n\nTrace.set_handler(ConsoleHandler)  # Enable console output\nTrace.enabled?()                   # Check if active\nTrace.get_handler()                # Current handler\nTrace.reset()                      # Disable tracing\n```","ref":"cheatsheet.html#tracing"},{"type":"extras","title":"Director - Operator Cheatsheet","doc":"```elixir\nalias Operator.Director\n\n# Start\n{:ok, pid} = Director.start_link(\n  storyteller: MyStoryteller,\n  on_event: fn event -> ... end,\n  name: :my_director\n)\n\n# Tick\nDirector.tick(world_state)              # Async\nevent = Director.tick_sync(world_state) # Sync (returns event)\n\n# Control\nDirector.current_tick()\nDirector.change_storyteller(NewModule)\nDirector.get_state()\n```","ref":"cheatsheet.html#director"},{"type":"extras","title":"Storyteller Behaviour - Operator Cheatsheet","doc":"```elixir\ndefmodule MyStoryteller do\n  @behaviour Operator.Storyteller\n\n  @impl true\n  def init(_opts), do: %{state: :initial}\n\n  @impl true\n  def pick_event(tick, world_state, state) do\n    # Return {event_map, new_state} or {nil, state}\n    {%{type: :event}, state}\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"cheatsheet.html#storyteller-behaviour"},{"type":"extras","title":"Storage - Operator Cheatsheet","doc":"```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.Storage\n\nStorage.persist_plan(entity_id, plan)\nStorage.fetch_plan(entity_id)\nStorage.clear_plan(entity_id)\nStorage.list_plans()\nStorage.clear_all()\nStorage.stats()\n```","ref":"cheatsheet.html#storage"},{"type":"extras","title":"Testing - Operator Cheatsheet","doc":"```elixir\nalias Operator.HTN.TestHelpers\n\n# In test setup\nsetup do\n  TestHelpers.reset_registry()\n  :ok\nend\n\n# Register specific modules\nTestHelpers.register_modules([MyBehavior])\nTestHelpers.setup_htn([Mod1, Mod2])  # Reset + register\n\n# Isolated registry scope\nTestHelpers.with_registry([MyBehavior], fn ->\n  # Only MyBehavior registered here\nend)\n\n# Create test facts\nfacts = TestHelpers.test_facts(%{self: %{hp: 100}})\n\n# Assertions\nTestHelpers.assert_has_task(plan, :task_name)\nTestHelpers.assert_has_task(plan, :task_name, [:expected_arg])\n```","ref":"cheatsheet.html#testing"},{"type":"extras","title":"Configuration - Operator Cheatsheet","doc":"```elixir\n# config/config.exs\nconfig :operator,\n  storage_module: MyApp.Storage,\n  telemetry_module: MyApp.Telemetry,\n  rationalization_module: MyApp.Rationalization,\n  traits_module: MyApp.Traits\n```","ref":"cheatsheet.html#configuration"},{"type":"extras","title":"Common Patterns - Operator Cheatsheet","doc":"```elixir\n# Game loop integration\ndef tick(entity, world) do\n  facts = build_facts(entity, world)\n\n  case entity.plan do\n    nil -> maybe_create_plan(entity, facts)\n    plan -> execute_or_replan(entity, plan, facts)\n  end\nend\n\n# Conditional decomposition\ntask :approach do\n  decompose fn facts ->\n    if Facts.has?(facts, {:self, :vehicle}) do\n      [{:drive_to, [target]}]\n    else\n      [{:walk_to, [target]}]\n    end\n  end\nend\n\n# Priority-based goal selection\ngoal :critical do\n  metadata priority: 10  # Higher = more important\nend\n\ngoal :idle do\n  metadata priority: 1\nend\n```","ref":"cheatsheet.html#common-patterns"}],"proglang":"elixir","content_type":"text/markdown","producer":{"name":"ex_doc","version":"0.40.1"}}